window.TECHNIQUE_FEATS = {"e001": [{"name": "Double Up", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Kaichi", "text": "The horn, doubled — two manifestations, two prices. Ambition, posted twice. One Kaichi activation may create two drill-horn manifestations; pay and track each horn separately. Both persist under the normal Kaichi duration. Horns are not summoned creatures, do not require a summon command, and do not consume creature or manifestation capacity. When you take the Attack action, resolve each available horn attack as part of that action; this never grants a second action."}, {"name": "Zero Friction", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Reiki", "text": "Reiki’s speed and Kaichi’s reach were always one answer divided in two. This feat reunites them: strike mid-sprint, and carry the momentum through the horn. While Reiki's movement increase is active, you can resolve your Kaichi horn attack at any point during your movement instead of only as part of the Attack action. If you move at least 20 feet in a straight line immediately before the attack, a hit also shoves the target 10 feet away from you, carrying your momentum through the horn."}, {"name": "Maximum: Kirin’s Flames", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Kirin and CE score 20", "text": "Kirin’s endurance, inverted: every melee hit taken returns fire threefold. The trade no longer asks the sorcerer to stand still — it dares the enemy to strike. While Kirin is active, each melee hit against you deals fire damage to its attacker equal to three times the HP you actually lost after reductions and temporary HP. This requires no reaction, cannot trigger from reflected damage, and cannot recursively trigger itself."}], "e002": [{"name": "Deathwatch", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Cursed Crow", "text": "To mark a creature through a crow’s eyes is to borrow the flock’s patience: direction and distance for an hour, through invisibility, darkness, cover. Death, watched in advance. While seeing through a crow, you can use a bonus action to mark one creature the crow can see. For 1 hour you sense the marked creature's direction and distance through the bond, even through invisibility, darkness, or cover, while both of you remain on the same plane. Only one creature can be marked this way at a time."}, {"name": "Murder's Due", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Omen of Death", "text": "The frightened one is released — and the flock collects the debt, every nearby crow spending its reaction to close in. Mercy, weaponized. As a bonus action, end Omen of Death's frightened condition on one creature within 60 feet of you. Each of your active crows within 30 feet of it can use its reaction to fly up to its speed toward that creature without provoking opportunity attacks, converging on the scent of its fear."}, {"name": "Maximum: Kamikaze", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Bird Strike and CE score 20", "text": "When the crow dies in its strike, the death-cry becomes an Omen. The flock’s terror outlives the flock — fear, funded by a corpse. When your Bird Strike destroys its crow, the death-cry becomes an Omen of Death. Each creature within 15 feet of the target must make your Omen Wisdom save or become frightened of you until the end of your next turn. A creature that succeeds is immune to this effect until the next dawn."}, {"name": "All Seeing", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Cursed Crow", "text": "The bond deepens until the sorcerer is no longer blinded while seeing through his crows, and every nearby crow lends him ten feet of blindsight. The network stops borrowing his eyes and gives him theirs. You have improved your ability to manage information. While you see through the crows you don’t gain the blinded condition. You gain 10 ft of blindsight for every cursed crow within 60 ft of you that is not incapacitated."}, {"name": "Scavenger", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Omen of Death", "text": "The crows taught him their opportunism: strike what is already frightened, and the fear feeds him — temporary HP equal to his level, once per turn. You have learned from the opportunistic way of the crows. Once per turn when you hit a frightened creature with an attack, you gain temporary hit points equal to your level."}], "e003": [{"name": "Blood Transfusion", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Blood Manipulation", "text": "The engineer learns to irrigate others: 1 CE and 5 HP become 2d6 + CE modifier of healing in a willing creature. His own river, lent out — never to himself. As an action, spend 1 CE and 5 HP to transfuse freshly produced blood into a willing creature within 5 feet. It regains 2d6 + your CE modifier hit points. You cannot target yourself with this transfusion."}, {"name": "Crimson Clot", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Blood Manipulation", "text": "A reaction to clot the blood in a wound he has dealt — the victim’s speed halved as the blood hardens. The river leaves dams behind it. Once per turn, when you damage a creature with a blood attack, you can use your reaction to clot the blood in the wound. The creature's speed is halved until the end of its next turn as the blood hardens around the injury. A creature with no blood is immune."}, {"name": "Blood Crystallization", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Blood Construction", "text": "Blood, frozen into armor: resistance to the three physical damage types, a larger unarmed die, +5 AC as a reaction — at the price of a d20 rolled each turn, exhaustion waiting on 1–3. The crystal is strong because the flesh beneath it is brittle. Bonus action, 3 CE, Technique Focus for 1 minute: resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing; unarmed die increases one size; reaction adds +5 AC against one attack. At each turn’s start roll d20; on 1–3 gain one exhaustion level. Ending the form requires no action."}, {"name": "Red Current", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Flowing Red Scale", "text": "While the Red Scale floods him, he may run on liquid and up walls — the slipstream carrying him past guards who expected gravity to do their work. While Flowing Red Scale is active, you can move across the surface of liquids and up vertical surfaces without falling; if you end your turn on neither solid ground nor a surface, you fall. Your rushing slipstream carries you past guards: your movement does not provoke opportunity attacks while Flowing Red Scale is active."}, {"name": "Blood Edge", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Convergence and CE score 20", "text": "A blade bled into being: 1 to CE-modifier CE, matching HP, for a cursed weapon rising from d10 to 2d8. The sword that costs its smith — and cannot be sundered without sundering him. Once on your turn with no action, spend 1–CE modifier CE and matching HP to form one proficient melee weapon for 1 minute. It is cursed; base damage is d10, rising one step per 2 CE to d12 then 2d8. A suitable outside blood source waives only the HP cost."}, {"name": "Maximum: Supernova", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Piercing Blood and CE score 20", "text": "Up to PB orbs, each a Piercing Blood waiting to happen, detonated on his reaction. The general’s calculus: one man’s blood, spent to wound many. Action: create up to PB orbs in open spaces within 30 feet. Each costs 10 CE and 10 HP as Piercing Blood. An orb lasts 1 minute and detonates immediately or by your reaction: creatures within 10 feet make Dexterity saves, taking 10d8 piercing and prone on failure, half and no prone on success. Resolve overlapping orbs separately."}, {"name": "Maximum: Wing King", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Piercing Blood and CE score 20", "text": "The river takes flight: quadrupled speed, a flying speed, an extra action for three ranged strikes. Blood was never meant to fly; that is exactly why it terrifies. Bonus action, 10 CE, once per long rest: for 1 minute with Technique Focus, quadruple walking speed and gain flying speed equal to half that walking speed. Gain one restricted extra action that can make three ranged CE attacks, each dealing 3d10 + CE modifier necrotic on hit."}, {"name": "Flowing Red Scale: Stack", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Flowing Red Scale", "text": "The flood, deepened: 6 CE for a greater Red Scale. The sluices were never the limit — only the engineer’s caution was. The power of the Flowing Red Scale has reached new heights. As a bonus action for 6 CE or while Flowing Red Scale is active for 3 CE, you instead gain the following benefits for 1 minute: ●​ Your movement speed is tripled ●​ You gain a +4 bonus to AC ●​ You have advantage on Dexterity and Strength saving throws and Strength checks and once per round you can reroll a check or save ●​ You gain one extra action and reaction."}], "e004": [{"name": "Flawless Acting", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Graverobber", "text": "Seven days and $2,500 buy a false identity — clothing, records, profession, affiliations. The tenant furnishes the house. After seven days and $2,500 of expenses, establish one false identity with clothing, records, profession, and affiliations. It cannot duplicate a real person. Investigation contests your Deception to expose inconsistencies; the identity grants no legal authority the fiction cannot support."}, {"name": "Memory Bank", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Skill Theft", "text": "He remembers everything, and can store a remembered experience in a touched object. A tenant who has lived a hundred lives needs an archive. You perfectly remember everything you experience. As an action, touch an object and store any continuous portion of one remembered experience in it; there is no added object or duration cap. A creature touching it may use an action to begin experiencing the memory from your point of view at normal speed and may stop at will. A memory grants information, not proficiency, statistics, or technique access."}, {"name": "Maximum: Backup", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Immortality and CE score 20", "text": "Eight hours of preparation, 10 CE, and one designated corpse: on death, the lease transfers. The tenant keeps a spare house. Prepare an eligible humanoid corpse over 8 hours, then use an action and 10 CE to designate it as your only backup. On death, resolve the Clone spell’s soul-transfer procedure using that body, without its gold or maturation time. Preparing a new backup destroys the old link; a trapped or unwilling soul cannot transfer."}], "e005": [{"name": "Boogie Down", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Boogie", "text": "Struck by an attack, he answers with a reaction clap — swapping himself out and letting the blow meet whoever arrives. The best defense is to not be where the blade lands. When you are hit by an attack, you can use your reaction to swap yourself with a willing creature or eligible object within range, following all normal Boogie Woogie rules and paying its normal CE cost. The attack instead targets whoever arrives in your space; compare the original attack roll against its AC and resolve damage normally."}, {"name": "Beguiling Tactics", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Woogie", "text": "The swapped are not merely moved but stunned — an Intelligence save, and the first success teaches them advantage thereafter. The fake-clap, Performance or Deception, keeps the audience guessing which beat is real. An unwilling creature swapped by Woogie makes an Intelligence save; failure stuns it until the start of its next turn. After its first success it has advantage on later saves that encounter. As an action, fake-clap with Performance or Deception contested by Insight; on a win it has disadvantage on its next Beguiling save before end of your next turn."}, {"name": "Maximum: Best Friend", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Round of Applause and CE score 20", "text": "The duet: one chosen ally, and once per round when either is targeted, a reaction swaps the two for no CE. Two dancers, one tempo, no missteps. At the start of combat, choose one willing ally you can perceive. You fight as a duet: once per round, when either of you is targeted by an attack, you can use your reaction to swap the two of you with no CE cost, following all normal Boogie Woogie range and legality rules. The attack targets whoever arrives in the targeted space; compare the original attack roll against their AC and resolve damage normally."}], "e006": [{"name": "Subtle Constructs", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Construct", "text": "She may build unseen — the dagger that was not there a breath ago, the tool no eye marked in the making. Against the fooled, the first use strikes with advantage. The quietest blade is the one that was never drawn, only remembered into being. After creating an item, make Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) against each observer’s passive Perception. Against a creature you fool, your first attack or check using that item before end of next turn has advantage. The creation itself remains subject to line of sight and obvious physical evidence."}, {"name": "Imbue", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Cursed Creation", "text": "At double the price, she may lend a created tool a Technique for seven days — a borrowed soul, housed in borrowed steel. No further limit; the only laws are attunement and her own strength. But the oldest price stands: a Special Grade soul still kills its maker. Some guests cannot be hosted. When using Cursed Creation to construct a cursed tool, pay twice that tool’s normal CE cost to imbue the creation with the tool’s Technique for 7 days. There is no added one-item cap. The created tool uses the normal attunement rules and your CE attack/DC when its technique needs them; Creating a Special Grade tool still kills the creator afterward and cannot be reversed or revived."}, {"name": "Maximum: Perfect Sphere", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Insectoid Armor and CE score 20", "text": "The Maximum: a five-foot sphere, perfect, indestructible, moved by a thought — thirty feet at a gesture, shattering walls and the unready alike, dealing ruin to all it touches or nears. The simplest shape, perfected. There is a lesson the masters carve above their doors: when you can build anything, build the thing nothing can break. Action, 10 CE: create one 5-foot-radius sphere within 10 feet for 1 minute with Technique Focus. It is indestructible while maintained. Ending a turn adjacent or being rammed forces one Dexterity save per turn for 5d12 force, half on success. Bonus action moves it 30 feet; it destroys barriers and unattended nonmagical structures in its path."}], "e007": [{"name": "Detonate", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Granite Blast", "text": "The beam, shortened to a blade: Granite Blast as a melee CE attack with 5-foot reach. The cannon learns the knife’s range. When activating Granite Blast, you may make it a melee CE attack with 5-foot reach instead of a ranged attack. All cost, damage, and other modifiers remain unchanged."}, {"name": "Canshot", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Grape Shot", "text": "After one blast hits, 3 CE shrapnels the impact — every other creature within 5 feet takes half the damage dealt, no roll, no save. The shell keeps giving. Corrected prerequisite: Grape Shot. Once per Granite Blast activation after one blast hits, spend 3 CE; every other creature within 5 feet of that target takes half the damage actually dealt, with no additional attack or save. The original target is not hit twice."}, {"name": "Maximum: Antimatter Bomb", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Nuclear Shell", "text": "The cone becomes a 100-foot-radius sphere centered on the sorcerer — himself excluded, everything else saving normally. The battery fires in all directions at once. When you activate Nuclear Shell, its cone may become a 100-foot-radius sphere centered on you. You are excluded; all other creatures save normally. Unattended nonmagical objects and structures in the sphere are reduced to dust. Pay Nuclear Shell’s normal cost and charge time."}, {"name": "Croquembouche", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Granite Blast", "text": "The master gunner’s trick: once per turn, replace one Attack-action attack with a melee Granite Blast for 1 CE. The cannon joins the volley. You have realized a new way to utilize your massive output. Once per turn when you take the Attack action on your turn, you can spend 1 CE to replace an attack with a use of your Granite Blast as a melee cursed energy attack. This cannot be used with Grape Shot."}], "e008": [{"name": "Fighting Words", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Power of Words", "text": "Those who fail a word’s save make a second Wisdom save — failure leaves them disadvantaged on attacks that spare the speaker. The words teach their victims manners. When a creature fails a save against your cursed word, it makes a second Wisdom save. On failure, for 1 minute it has disadvantage on attacks that do not include you as a target; it repeats the save at the end of each turn. A creature can be affected by only one Fighting Words at a time."}, {"name": "Hushed Word", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Interjection", "text": "The Interjection word, pitched as a whisper to one creature within 30 feet — only it hears, only it suffers. Command, narrowed to a single ear. When you use a word with Interjection, you can pitch it as a whisper aimed at one creature within 30 feet that can hear you. Only that creature hears and is affected by the word, even if it would normally reach further; you still pay its full CE and vocal strain."}, {"name": "Megaphone", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Resounding Voice", "text": "Resounding Voice, focused into a 5-foot-wide, 70-foot line. The broadcast becomes a lance. When you use Resounding Voice, you can focus the broadcast into a 5-foot-wide, 70-foot line originating from you instead of a cone. Only creatures in the line that can hear you are affected; all vocal-cord, target, and save rules remain."}, {"name": "Quick Tongue", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Interjection", "text": "One more word falls under Interjection’s speed. The vocabulary of the instant grows. Your versatility and training have increased the amount of words you have and your speed. You can choose one more word to be under the effect of Interjection."}], "e009": [{"name": "Cursed Spirit Embodiment", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Cursed Spirit Absorption and CE score 16+", "text": "The eater becomes the eaten: spend CE equal to a stored spirit’s CR and wear its body for hours. Digestion, run in reverse. Action; spend CE equal to the absorbed spirit’s CR, rounded up (minimum 1), and transform for up to half your character level in hours. Replace your Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, AC, current HP, movement, senses, and creature actions with the spirit’s profile; retain your Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma, personality, alignment, and any proficiency bonus that is higher. You cannot use Cursed Spirit Manipulation features or legendary, lair, or mythic actions while transformed. At 0 spirit HP you revert, and excess damage carries over to your original HP."}, {"name": "Defensive Summoning", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Perfect Control", "text": "Struck and not yet damaged, he spends 5 CE plus a spirit’s cost to manifest it adjacent — and the spirit takes the blow. The collection serves as a wall. Reaction when hit, before damage: spend 5 CE plus the chosen stored spirit’s summon cost and manifest it in an adjacent legal space. It becomes the attack’s target; compare the original attack roll with its AC and apply damage to it. Area effects still affect every creature normally."}, {"name": "Uzumaki Versatility", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Maximum: Uzumaki and CE score 20", "text": "Two stored spirits, permanently consumed, become a miniature Uzumaki for one minute — fired by action or reaction when a target comes within 60 feet. The stomach, kept honest in small change. Bonus action: permanently consume exactly two stored spirits to form a miniature Uzumaki for 1 minute. Action or reaction when a target comes within 60 feet, 5 CE: ranged CE attack; hit deals Xd12 necrotic, X = combined CR rounded up. Ignore resistance, treat immunity as resistance. Undetected target grants advantage. Extract one action using the revised Uzumaki rules."}, {"name": "Minimum: Uzumaki", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Maximum: Uzumaki", "text": "The smaller, deadlier Uzumaki: a bonus action, two spirits, harder to dodge. The blast, refined by hunger. Due to your extended studies, you have made a smaller version of Uzumaki that's more deadly and much harder to dodge. As a bonus action, you can spend two cursed spirits to create a miniature Uzumaki that fits in your hand. It can't be seen by the creature unless its passive Perception is 25 or higher, or the creature succeeds a Perception check. As an action or reaction for 5 Cursed Energy, you can release all the condensed energy from this Uzumaki at a target within 30 feet. Make a ranged cursed energy attack roll, on a hit the target takes Xd12 of necrotic damage(X being the combined CR of the 2 curses). Like Maximum Uzumaki, this ignores resistance and treats immunity like resistance. You have advantage on your attack roll if the target has not detected your Minimum Uzumaki. Similar to Maximum Uzumaki, you can obtain actions, reactions, bonus actions, and legendary actions of the creature's technique."}], "e010": [{"name": "Tool Versatility", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Judge’s Gavel", "text": "As a bonus action, reshape the gavel into any melee weapon. You are proficient with it and it uses that weapon’s damage and properties; no ammunition, consumable, or attached special-grade property is created. It returns to gavel form when released."}, {"name": "Weight of Judgment", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Judge’s Gavel", "text": "As an action, spend 2 CE to slam your gavel into the ground. Each creature within 15 feet that can hear the slam must make a Wisdom save against your CE DC. On a failure, it cannot take reactions until the start of your next turn: order in the court."}, {"name": "Judgeman Release", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Deadly Sentencing", "text": "Bonus action, 5 CE, Technique Focus for 1 minute: summon intangible Judgeman and designate one perceived opponent within 60 feet. Every time that opponent attacks, its cumulative assault penalty increases by 1. Subtract the full penalty from its attack rolls and saving throws until Judgeman leaves; there is no added charge cap."}], "e011": [{"name": "Ashfall", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Flames of Disaster", "text": "The cone’s damage, snuffed and traded for a minute of choking ash — the area heavily obscured. Fire, spent as shadow. When you activate Flames of Disaster, you can snuff its damage to fill the cone's area with choking ash for 1 minute. The area is heavily obscured."}, {"name": "Volcanic Launch", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Erupting Volcanoes", "text": "A volcano erupts beneath the sorcerer himself — 2 CE, a bonus action, and he is launched up to 60 feet to safety. The disaster, ridden. As a bonus action, spend 2 CE to have one of your volcanoes within 30 feet erupt directly beneath you instead of along its line. You are launched up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see and land safely without taking falling damage; the eruption still deals its normal damage along one 30-by-10-foot line of your choice originating from the volcano."}, {"name": "Hellscape", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Maximum: Meteor", "text": "15 CE and a minute of Focus: the ground in a 100-foot radius melts into lava — difficult terrain, 4d6 fire for entering or lingering. The battlefield, rezoned as a furnace. Action, 15 CE, Technique Focus for 1 minute: unattended nonmagical objects and ground in a 100-foot radius melt into lava. It is difficult terrain; entering or ending a turn there causes a Constitution save, 4d6 fire on failure, half on success, once per turn. Bonus action moves one 10-foot lava square up to 20 feet along a surface."}, {"name": "Pyrokinesis", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Flames of Disaster", "text": "Training finds new applications for the old flame — resistance, reach, or refinement, taken more than once. The catastrophe, studied. Through training and understanding, you have found new applications to your flames. You gain the one of the following (This feat can be taken more than once): ●​ Resistance to Fire Damage and when you roll damage for a technique that deals fire damage, you can reroll any 1s, but must take the new result, even if the new roll is a 1. ●​ Two spells below 5th level dealing fire damage. The ce cost equals the spell’s level."}], "e012": [{"name": "Hydrokinesis", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Tides of Disaster", "text": "A high-pressure lance: 2 CE, a ranged CE attack within 30 feet — 2d10 cold plus 2d6 piercing, and a Constitution save. The tide, sharpened. Action, 2 CE: make a ranged CE attack against a creature within 30 feet, firing a high-pressure lance of water. On a hit, it takes 2d10 cold + 2d6 piercing damage and must make a Constitution save against your CE DC. On a failure, it is knocked prone and takes the rolled damage again as the jet bores through."}, {"name": "Shoal", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Horizon of Captivating Skandha", "text": "Death Swarm, outside the Domain — same action, same costs, but no sure-hit. The school hunts in open water now. You may activate Death Swarm outside the Domain with its normal action, target, summon capacity, and any listed CE cost. It has no sure-hit; attacks and saves resolve normally."}, {"name": "Typhoon", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Water Defensive Ring", "text": "For 4 more CE, the Defensive Ring becomes a 20-foot-radius sphere storm for its duration. The wall learns weather. For 4 additional CE, the Ring creates a 20-foot-radius sphere storm for the Ring's duration (1 minute with Technique Focus; the storm is stationary unless moved by a stated effect). A creature makes a Strength save once when the storm appears and whenever it ends a turn there, taking 2d6 bludgeoning on failure. As a bonus action each turn, make a 60-foot 4d6 lightning strike: each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save, taking the damage on failure, or half on success. The area moves with you and is difficult terrain."}], "e013": [{"name": "Chlorokinesis", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Forests of Disaster", "text": "A bonus action reshapes an active root wall into another wall option — HP and duration unchanged. The garden, re-landscaped mid-battle. As a bonus action, transform one active root wall into a different wall option without refreshing its HP or duration."}, {"name": "Bouquet", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Flower Field", "text": "One creature, 60 feet, the full Flower Field save and duration — no area, no bystanders. A single bloom, hand-delivered. Action, 3 CE: one creature within 60 feet makes the normal Flower Field save and suffers its effects for the normal duration. It does not create an area and cannot affect additional creatures through movement."}, {"name": "Stranglehold", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Cursed Bud", "text": "A bonus action constricts the buds on a chosen host: a failed Strength save restrains it. The garden tightens its embrace. As a bonus action, choose one creature hosting at least one of your buds. The buds constrict: it must make a Strength save against your CE DC. On a failure, it is restrained until the end of its next turn. On a success, it tears one bud off, destroying it."}, {"name": "Sapping Roots", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Cursed Bud", "text": "For 5 CE, a minute of draining: melee hits and technique damage siphon the victim’s cursed energy. The roots drink deeper than blood. Your power has increased and been honed. As an action, for 5 Cursed Energy you give yourself the ability to drain Cursed Energy for 1 minute. On a hit with a melee attack or if you damage a creature with your Innate Technique, they lose 1 cursed energy which you gain."}], "e014": [{"name": "Black Belt", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Martial Prowess", "text": "Repeatable; choose each maneuver once. Takedown uses a bonus-action grapple after a melee hit. Judo Throw triggers on a hit against your grappled Huge-or-smaller target: Strength save, prone on failure and stunned to end of next turn if failed by 5+. Flying Drop Kick uses an action and your jump movement for one unarmed attack, pushing 30 feet on hit."}, {"name": "Opportunistic Blow", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Controlled Divergent Flow", "text": "Once per turn after the delayed Divergent Fist damage lands, the target makes an Intelligence save. On failure, attacks against it have advantage until the start of your next turn."}, {"name": "Maximum: Soul Punch", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Chosen by the Sparks and CE score 20", "text": "He strikes past flesh into the soul — a wound no reversal can knit, that tangles the victim's energy tighter with every hit. Mark where he aims: not the soldier, but the road his supplies travel. Before an unarmed attack, spend 5 CE; all your unarmed hits this turn deal soul damage that ordinary RCT cannot heal. Each hit gives one Output Suppression, maximum CE modifier: reduce optional CE spending ceiling by 1 per stack and disable Maximum Output while any stack remains. All stacks end after a short or long rest."}], "e015": [{"name": "Thunderous Applause", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Hands of Love", "text": "The two hands clap around a creature within 5 feet of both — 2 CE, a Constitution save, deafness on failure. Applause, weaponized. As an action, spend 2 CE to clap your two active hands together around a creature within 5 feet of both. It must make a Constitution save against your CE DC. On a failure, it is deafened until the end of its next turn and pushed 10 feet directly away from the midpoint between the hands. On a success, it is not deafened and is pushed 5 feet."}, {"name": "Handy Dandy", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Hand Shield", "text": "One hand locks into a 10-by-10-foot platform — 2,000 pounds supported, ten minutes — and can no longer attack, grapple, or shield. The guardian becomes architecture. Action, 2 CE: lock one active Hand into a solid 10-by-10-foot platform for up to 10 minutes. It supports up to 2,000 pounds and uses the Hand’s AC/HP. The locked Hand cannot attack, grapple, shove, or shield; bonus action releases it."}, {"name": "Maximum: Love at First Sight", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Cutie Honey and CE score 20", "text": "10 CE: one creature in a hand’s reach makes the Cutie Honey save at full strength, no prior hit required. Devotion, declared at first sight. Action, 10 CE: one creature within an active Hand’s reach makes the Cutie Honey Wisdom save. On failure it suffers that feature’s full 1-minute effect and repeating save without requiring a hit or restraint first."}, {"name": "Lover's Embrace", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Hands of Love", "text": "Shoves push 10 feet; the grappled and restrained take a d6 at the start of their turns. The embrace leaves marks. You have mastered the basic use of your love hands. Whenever you Shove a creature, they are instead pushed 10 feet. When creatures are grappled or restrained, they take a d6 bludgeoning damage at the start of their turn. Structures also take maximum damage from your Love Hands."}], "e016": [{"name": "Iceshape", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ice Creation", "text": "An action and 1 CE shape a melee weapon from ice — proficient, cursed, an hour’s life, melting harmlessly when destroyed. Winter, armed. Action, 1 CE: form one simple or martial melee weapon from ice in your reach. You are proficient with it, it counts as cursed, and it lasts 1 hour. It has AC 13 and HP equal to 5 + level, melts harmlessly when destroyed, and grants no copied item property."}, {"name": "Permafrost", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Frost Calm", "text": "When the restrained break free on their Strength save, a reaction keeps their feet in clinging ice — speed halved until the end of their next turn. The refusal lingers. When a creature restrained by your ice succeeds on the Strength save to end the restraint, you can use your reaction to keep its feet frozen in clinging ice. Its speed is halved until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Maximum: Shatter", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ice Fall", "text": "Choose a creature restrained by the ice: a failed Constitution save breaks a limb and ends the restraint. What the ice kept, the shatter collects. Action: choose a creature restrained by your ice; it makes a Constitution save. Failure breaks one chosen limb and ends the restraint. It severs instead only if the restraint or same activation meets the revised Sever threshold, or the target is at or below 25% maximum HP. Success ends the restraint without injury."}, {"name": "Frostbite", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Frost Calm", "text": "The cold deepens: the restrained gain another temporary exhaustion level and −2 to attacks and ability checks. Winter, sharpened. The cold of your ice has increased exponentially. While restrained by your ice, your opponent gains an additional temporary level of exhaustion and a -2 to attack rolls and ability checks."}], "e017": [{"name": "Remote Transfiguration", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Transfiguration", "text": "A bare-hand touch plants a detectable soul mark on a humanoid — indefinitely. Later, from the same plane, the sorcerer pays the normal cost and reshapes from afar. The clay remembers the hand. A deliberate bare-hand touch may place one detectable soul mark on a Humanoid indefinitely. While on the same plane and knowing its identity, use an action and pay the normal Transfiguration cost to affect it at any distance; it saves normally. The mark is consumed after the attempt and can be removed by Technique Extermination or explicit soul repair."}, {"name": "Awakening", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ally Alteration", "text": "Altering a willing non-sorcerer may — DC 15, 10 CE, 1d4+1 days — wake a latent innate technique. The workshop does not only reshape. It opens. When altering a willing Non-Sorcerer, make one DC 15 CE ability check per creature. Success and 10 CE awaken a latent, lore-consistent innate technique after 1d4+1 days. The GM records the technique; it uses the target’s character level and does not grant class features or a second technique. The permanent change can reshape a campaign."}, {"name": "Maximum: Spirit Body of Distorted Killing", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Self-Embodiment of Perfection and CE score 20", "text": "10 CE for ten minutes: AC never below 25, elbow blades at 1d12 + CE modifier. The sculptor, become his own final work. Action, 10 CE: for 10 minutes your AC cannot be below 25 and you gain proficient elbow blades (1d12 + CE modifier piercing). On each blade attack, spend 1 CE for advantage and 15-foot reach. The form ends if incapacitated; AC bonuses do not raise the 25-floor unless they normally stack."}, {"name": "Transfiguration Adept", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Transfiguration", "text": "Mastery of grotesque molds: two new ways to spend transfigured humans, repeatable. The idle hands find new idleness. You have mastered your observation of the soul and learned grotesque molds to shape them into. You gain the two of the following ways to use transfigured humans (this feat can be repeated): ●​ Remote Transfiguration. When using Transfiguration, you can instead imprint a small, latent amount of cursed energy upon their souls, allowing you to transfigure them from large distances (only one touch per creature). ●​ Wall of Flesh. As an action, you spend humans up to your proficiency bonus to form a flat panel of human flesh up to 5 ft long and wide per human used in an unoccupied space within 5 ft. The wall’s AC equals your CE save DC and has hit points equal to 5 x the combined CR of the creatures used. You can move it 5 ft as a bonus action and can have only one wall at a time. ●​ Human Weapon. As a bonus action, you form a creature into a simple or martial weapon or ammunition. The weapon gains a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls if the creature’s CR is 5 or higher and increases by +1 per 5 CR to a maximum of +4. ●​ People Spikes. As an action, you spend humans up to your proficiency bonus, covering a 5 ft area per human on the ground within 30 ft of you with human spikes for 1 minute with Technique Focus. A creature that walks through this area takes 2d8 piercing damage, once per turn when it first enters or starts its turn in the area."}], "e018": [{"name": "Offensive Infinity", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Infinity", "text": "Infinity, weaponized: 1–PB CE pins a creature within 15 feet against a solid surface — Xd6 force and restraint on a failed Constitution save. The wall that refuses becomes the wall that crushes. Action, spend 1–PB CE: choose a creature within 15 feet and within 10 feet of a solid surface. Constitution save; failure takes Xd6 force and is restrained against that surface until start of your next turn, success takes half and is not restrained. X equals CE spent."}, {"name": "Spatial Skirmishing", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Blue", "text": "Blue rides an unarmed strike — CE ability for the attack, advantage on the hit; once Red is learned, the strike may carry Red instead. The moods, delivered by fist. Once per turn when making an unarmed strike, pay Blue’s normal cost and use CE ability for the attack; on hit apply Blue and gain advantage on that attack. After learning Red, choose Red instead: on hit the target makes the normal Strength save and is launched as Red states. One strike cannot carry both."}, {"name": "Teleportation", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Blue and CE score 20", "text": "Blue’s logic, applied to the self: 1–PB CE carries the sorcerer 10 feet per CE to a seen space — plus one willing passenger for 1 more. The impossible center, relocated at will. Action, spend 1–PB CE: teleport yourself to an open space you can see, 10 feet per CE. You may carry worn/held equipment and one willing creature no larger than you if you spend 1 additional CE within the same PB cap."}, {"name": "Delayed Purple", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Hollow Purple", "text": "Red, fired into a persisting Blue — as an action, or as a reaction when a creature enters or lingers in it. Both costs paid; everything inside suffers. The two truths, annihilated on schedule. While one of your Blues persists within 120 feet, activate Red into it as an action, or as a reaction when a creature enters or ends a turn in the Blue. Pay both Red and Hollow Purple costs. Every creature—including you—in a 100-foot radius centered on the Blue makes a Dexterity save; failure takes the maximum value of Hollow Purple’s 20d12 base dice (240 force damage), success half. Riders and amplifier dice are rolled normally."}], "e019": [{"name": "Lodestar", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Effective Marking", "text": "Turn the chart inward: mark herself, and become the brightest star. While she bears the mark and holds the greatest cursed energy among its bearers, every violation drags the fleet toward her. The navigator becomes the reef. When you use Effective Marking's additional reaction, you can mark yourself instead of the triggering creature. You bear that star normally, counting toward your per-star limit. While you bear it, Gravity's violation pull can draw pulled creatures toward you whenever you hold the greatest current CE among that star's bearers."}, {"name": "Repelling Forces", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Gravity", "text": "The tide reverses. For three to PB cursed energy, every marked body is hurled away from the brightest — ten feet per coin spent, simultaneous, taking no opportunity. The sea exhales. Bonus action, spend 3–PB CE: every marked creature is forced directly away from the marked body with the greatest current CE, 10 feet per CE spent. This is simultaneous forced movement, causes no opportunity attacks, and stops at solid obstacles."}, {"name": "Collapsing Stars", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Shining Star and CE score 20", "text": "The rarest maneuver: a vessel bearing all five stars, and the chart collapses inward — a Constitution save against 25d4 force, the marks consumed, the constellation spent in one detonation. No critical can multiply it; the sea does not double-count its wrecks. Action, 10 CE: choose a creature within 120 feet carrying all five marks. The marks collapse into it; Constitution save, taking 25d4 force on failure or half on success. All five marks are consumed. This damage cannot be multiplied by critical hits or other effects."}, {"name": "Comet Reactions", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Effective Marking", "text": "Her quickened hand learns new trades. The marking reaction may now be spent on defense — the Dodge's disadvantage, the Disengage's clean water — for a single coin of energy. A chart-drawer who can also vanish is doubly hard to corner. Your reaction speed has further increased. At the cost of one CE, you gain the ability to use the additional marking reaction from Effective Marking for other purposes: the Dodge benefit (attacks against you have disadvantage until the start of your next turn) or the Disengage benefit (your movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks until the end of your turn)."}], "e020": [{"name": "Defensive Surge", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Electric Energy", "text": "The storm bites back uninvited. When a melee strike lands, his reaction forces the attacker to save or seize up — paralyzed, though the blow itself still lands. Lightning does not forgive a hand laid on it. Reaction when a melee attack hits you: the attacker makes a Constitution save. On failure it is paralyzed until the start of its next turn. This does not cancel the triggering hit and can affect a creature only once per turn."}, {"name": "Imbued Weapon", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Lightning Discharge", "text": "The weapon becomes a battery. Charge it with stored strikes, and a bonus action within sixty feet draws a five-foot line of lightning between him and it — every creature along the wire pays by the charge. Each melee weapon hit may place one positive charge in that weapon, maximum twice CE modifier for one weapon. Bonus action while it is within 60 feet: consume all charges to create a 5-foot-wide line between you and it. Creatures in the line make Dexterity saves, taking 1d12 lightning per charge, half on success."}, {"name": "Final Discharge", "prereq": "Prerequisite: CE score 20 and Mythical Beast Amber Release", "text": "If he deactivates before the fifth minute, he may vent the account's remainder: two d12 of lightning per full minute endured, thirty feet, Dexterity halves it — and the deactivation saves are still owed. Even the exit is a detonation. When you deactivate your Mythical Beast Amber Release with a bonus action before the minute-5 collapse, you can vent its remaining charge as a final blast. Each creature within 30 feet of you must make a Dexterity save against your CE DC, taking 2d12 lightning damage per full minute endured (maximum 8d12), or half on a success. You still resolve the Release's deactivation Constitution saves normally."}], "e021": [{"name": "Augmented Vow", "prereq": "Prerequisite: True New Shadow Style: Simple Domain", "text": "When opening Simple Domain, state one symmetrical conduct rule and one consequence no harsher than 5d10 damage or one condition until end of the breaker’s next turn. Every creature inside, including you, knows it and is bound for CE modifier rounds or until leaving. It cannot compel impossible actions, surrender, self-harm, or permanent loss."}, {"name": "Instantaneous Attack", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Batto Sword Draw", "text": "While your Simple Domain is active, use an action to prepare. The next time a hostile creature enters your weapon reach before the Domain ends, use your reaction to make one weapon attack. The preparation is then consumed."}, {"name": "First Strike", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Evening Moon Sword Drawing", "text": "Once per combat, before your first turn begins, you may use your reaction to assume the Evening Moon stance without an active Simple Domain. Until the end of your first turn, hostile creatures entering your weapon reach provoke your Evening Moon reaction attack as normal. The stance ends early if you activate your Simple Domain."}], "e022": [{"name": "Contagious Luck", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Great Luck", "text": "Luck, it turns out, is transferable: his forced twenty may be dealt to a willing creature within thirty feet. The cost and the recharge are his; the benefit is theirs. The house honors proxies. When using Great Luck, you may choose one willing creature within 30 feet instead of yourself. The use, duration, die, and any cost are unchanged; you do not also gain the benefit."}, {"name": "Pachinko Manifest", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Idle Death Gamble", "text": "He carries the parlor's tools outside its doors: the three attacks at thirty feet, normal actions and costs — but no sure-hit, no expectation, no jackpot. The machines are unplugged on the street. You may use the technique’s Pachinko Attacks outside the Domain at a 30-foot range. Use their normal actions, attack/DC, and CE costs; they gain no sure-hit, expectation modifier, jackpot roll, or Domain-only event unless an entry expressly grants it."}, {"name": "Maximum: Love Train", "prereq": "Prerequisite: The Fever and Pachinko Manifest", "text": "The Maximum plugs the machines back in. Ten coins, one action: all three attacks as a single pull at thirty feet, hits adding expectation even outside the Domain — and if all three strike the same creature, the bet is placed on the spot. The floor comes to him. Action, 10 CE: unleash your Green, Red, and Gold Pachinko attacks as a single activation at 30-foot range, resolving each with its normal attack roll and no sure-hit. Hits add expectation even outside the Domain. If all three strike the same creature, you may immediately place a bet as part of this action."}], "e023": [{"name": "Fortissimo", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Marcado", "text": "The soloist. Her cumulative personal benefits may be dealt to one willing creature within sixty feet instead of herself; the target's penalties stay where they were. If the soloist leaves range or sight, the melody returns to her. When you begin Prayer, choose one willing creature you can perceive within 60 feet as your soloist. Your cumulative personal benefits from the Prayer track - bonuses to AC, saves, damage, attacks, and critical range - apply to the soloist instead of you; penalties to the target are unchanged. If the soloist leaves 60 feet or becomes imperceptible, the benefits return to you."}, {"name": "Cadence", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Caesura", "text": "The conductor's veto: after a Prayer-afflicted creature rolls but before the outcome, four coins and a reaction turn a hit into a miss or a successful save into a failure. Legendary Resistance, immunity, and natural twenties do not take direction. Reaction, 4 CE, after a creature affected by your Prayer rolls but before outcome: make its attack miss or turn its successful save into a failure. This cannot override Legendary Resistance, immunity, or a natural 20 attack."}, {"name": "Maximum: Grand Chorus", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Crescendo and CE score 20", "text": "The Maximum needs no single partner. For a minute, every hostile creature she can perceive within sixty feet suffers the penalties of her current beat, and she gains the benefits once. The duet becomes a chorus; the whole room falls out of step. Action, 10 CE: for 1 minute using Technique Focus, your Prayer needs no single target - at the start of each of your turns, every hostile creature you can perceive within 60 feet suffers the Prayer penalties for your current beat count, and you gain the personal benefits once. Starting Prayer anew resets the count as normal."}], "e024": [{"name": "White Space", "prereq": "Prerequisite: 24 Frame Rule", "text": "The frame between frames. When targeted, two coins and a reaction step him up to fifteen feet to a seen, unoccupied space — the attack resolves against the new position and misses outright if he left its range. Only while Projection runs; the trick needs the reel turning. Reaction when targeted by an attack, 2 CE: step between frames. Move up to 15 feet to an unoccupied space you can see without provoking opportunity attacks; the triggering attack resolves against your new position and misses automatically if you left its range or reach. You may use this only while Projection is active."}, {"name": "Air Shatter", "prereq": "Prerequisite: 24 Frame Rule", "text": "The wake of the run: after a straight twenty-foot segment on the declared route, a bonus action and three coins shatter the displaced air — a thirty-foot line, Dexterity save, his modifier in d10s of force. The film leaves debris. When you complete a straight, uninterrupted segment of at least 20 feet on your declared route, use a bonus action and 3 CE to shatter the displaced air. Creatures in a 30-foot line along the segment you just traveled make a Dexterity save, taking CE modifier d10 force on failure or half on success. Roll damage once."}, {"name": "Maximum: Sakuga", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Fastest Sorcerer Alive and CE score 20", "text": "The Maximum is the showpiece sequence: twelve five-foot frames declared at once, ten coins, and until the end of his next turn he executes at blinding speed — attacking at any point along the route, splitting movement, opportunity attacks at disadvantage, passage through hostile spaces. Deviate, and the sequence is cut. Action, 10 CE: declare a complete route of up to twelve 5-foot frames. Until the end of your next turn you execute it at blinding speed - you may take the Attack action at any point along the route, splitting movement before and after, opportunity attacks against you have disadvantage, and you may pass through hostile spaces. Deviating from the declared route ends the effect."}], "e025": [{"name": "Puppet Armor", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ultimate Puppet", "text": "Wear the work: adjacent to an active puppet, an action dons it — off the roster, onto the body. Temporary hit points equal to its current health, plus two armor, its physical scores, movement, senses, and passive traits. When the borrowed health ends, the armor is destroyed. Action while adjacent to an active puppet: wear it and remove it from the active roster. Gain temporary HP equal to its current HP, +2 AC, its physical scores, movement, senses, and non-action traits. When temporary HP ends the armor is destroyed; action exits early with remaining puppet HP. It cannot act separately while worn."}, {"name": "Communication Puppets", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Lesser Puppet", "text": "The workshop's quietest product: up to proficiency-bonus Tiny messengers, each a snapshot of his consciousness with five minutes of activity. They cannot fight; they can only remember — and when the activity ends, every memory synchronizes across the plane. After each long rest, with 10 minutes of light activity during or after the rest, create up to PB Tiny messengers, each holding a snapshot of your consciousness and 5 minutes of activity. AC 15, 1 HP, speed 20; no attacks or technique. Set a perceivable trigger. While any are active on the same plane, memories they acquire synchronize with you and each other when the activity ends."}, {"name": "Maximum: Ultimate Puppet", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Absolute Puppet", "text": "The Maximum is a wedding: two prepared puppets fused over a long rest into one Ultimate chassis — the higher statistics, both full trait sets, both hit points combined, fielded as one for the higher summoning cost. At zero hit points the fusion breaks and both are destroyed. The masterpiece does not survive its own ending. During a long rest, fuse two of your prepared puppets into one Ultimate chassis: it uses the higher of their statistics, keeps both puppets' full trait sets, has hit points equal to both combined, and counts as one active puppet. It is summoned for the higher of the two CE costs. If it is reduced to 0 HP, the fusion breaks and both puppets are destroyed."}], "e026": [{"name": "Measured Guard", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Critical Focus", "text": "The auditor reads incoming blows too: when hit by a weapon attack, a coin and a reaction roll the Ratio die — three or seven, declared before damage, and the blow's damage is halved. He found its weak ratio. Reaction when you are hit by a weapon attack, 1 CE: roll your Ratio d10 (two dice from level 11, as the feature). On a 3 or 7 you found the blow's weak ratio and the damage is halved. Declare before damage is rolled."}, {"name": "Weapon Breaker", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Collapse", "text": "Three coins and a reaction when targeted by a weapon attack: the wielder saves Dexterity, and on failure a mundane weapon breaks before damage is dealt. Cursed tools break only against an equal or higher grade; artifacts break only when their story permits. Reaction when targeted by a weapon attack, 3 CE: wielder makes Dexterity save. On failure a mundane weapon breaks before damage; a cursed tool breaks only if your striking tool is equal or higher grade, otherwise the attack is deflected and misses. Artifacts and unique Special Grades break only when their own story permits."}, {"name": "Fatal Ratio", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Improved Ratio", "text": "After a Ratio critical, two coins tag the hit as a limb strike without targeted-strike disadvantage. Damage and the revised injury threshold resolve normally — the feat aims the verdict; it does not guarantee the severing. Corrected prerequisite: Improved Ratio. After a Ratio critical, spend 2 CE to make it a limb-tagged hit without targeted-strike disadvantage. Resolve damage and the revised injury threshold/save normally; the feat does not automatically sever a limb."}], "e027": [{"name": "Spiderweb", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Dismantle", "text": "The cut widens: for one more coin, Dismantle's attack becomes a thirty-foot cone — Dexterity saves, normal damage on failure, half on success, rolled once. The altar accepts groups. For 1 additional CE, replace Dismantle’s attack with a 30-foot cone. Creatures make Dexterity saves, taking the normal Dismantle damage on failure or half on success. Roll once for the area."}, {"name": "Form of Battle", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Perfect Form", "text": "The grapple becomes the altar: while he holds a creature, Dismantle and Cleave need no ranged attack roll against it — the cuts ride the grip as melee attacks, mark and penetration intact. While the grapple holds, no other creature may be targeted. While you grapple a creature, your Dismantle and Cleave need no ranged attack roll against it - the cuts ride your grip. Resolve them as melee CE attacks instead, with Cleave's mark and penetration applying normally. You cannot target any other creature with those slashes while the grapple holds."}, {"name": "Maximum: World Cutter", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Malevolent Shrine and CE score 20", "text": "The Maximum: an audible chant, a free hand, five coins over the technique's cost — and the cut goes through occupied space, ignoring cover, barriers, technique-made armor, resistance, and immunity, resolving against base armor alone. A miss still spends the coins; it will not combine with Chanting or Maximum Output. Action with an audible chant and free hand: pay Cleave/Dismantle’s cost +5 CE and make its attack. It cuts occupied space, ignores cover, barriers, technique-created AC, resistance, and immunity. Resolve against base armor/natural/unarmored AC. A miss still expends CE; it cannot combine with Chanting or Maximum Output."}], "e028": [{"name": "Cloak of Invisibility", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Sky Shape", "text": "The still water, unseen: an action and three coins cast Invisibility through Technique Focus, no spellcasting required. Sky Armor's protection and flight persist beneath it; attacking or raising a hostile technique breaks the surface as the spell states. Action, 3 CE: cast Invisibility on yourself using Technique Focus, without needing spellcasting. If you have Sky Armor, its AC and flight remain active while invisible. Attacking or activating a hostile technique ends invisibility as the spell states."}, {"name": "Spatial Tear", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Thin Ice Breaker", "text": "The ice, torn rather than broken: for two more coins, Thin Ice Breaker's line becomes a single melee attack — her modifier in d10s of force and prone on a hit, nothing on a miss. Still one activation. Corrected feature name: Thin Ice Breaker. When activating it, spend 2 additional CE to replace the line and save with one melee CE attack. On hit, deal force damage equal to a number of d10s equal to your CE modifier and knock the target prone; on miss, no damage. It remains one activation."}, {"name": "Maximum: Hurricane", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Thin Ice Breaker and CE score 20", "text": "The Maximum is the sky exhaling: an action and ten coins, and chosen creatures within thirty feet save Strength or are launched a thousand feet upward. Flight, reactions, ceilings, and ordinary falling damage all apply — a ceiling simply stops the ascent early. Action, 10 CE: creatures of your choice within 30 feet make Strength saves. Failure launches a creature 1,000 feet upward; success leaves it in place. Flying, reactions, ceilings, and normal falling damage apply; a ceiling stops ascent at the available distance."}], "e029": [{"name": "Blessing Relay", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Bless", "text": "The sanctuary, extended: while the Zone stands, an action and three coins name a willing creature inside as a relay — allies within thirty feet of the relay gain the Zone's advantage as if standing inside it. The relay itself, carrying the blessing, receives none of it. Action, 3 CE while your Zone is active: designate one willing creature inside it as a relay for up to 1 minute, using your Technique Focus alongside the Zone. Allies you regard as such within 30 feet of the relay gain the Zone's advantage as if standing inside it. The relay itself gains no benefit while relaying."}, {"name": "Blessing of Combat", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Arena", "text": "The threshold, weaponized: once per turn, when an ally inside the Zone lands an attack on a hostile, the hit may push the target up to ten feet — and a push across the boundary triggers the Arena's Charisma save. The sanctuary evicts. Once per turn when an ally inside your Zone hits a hostile creature with an attack, they may push that hostile up to 10 feet as part of the hit. If the push carries it across the Zone boundary, it makes the Arena crossing Charisma save as normal."}, {"name": "Maximum: Shrine of the Gods", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Arena, Bless, and CE score 20", "text": "The Maximum walks: an action and ten coins raise the Zone centered on himself for a minute, and this time it moves with him — boundary and blessings traveling from its current position. Bless cannot be sustained separately while the shrine is walking. Action, 10 CE: establish your Zone centered on yourself for 1 minute using Technique Focus. It moves with you, applying the Arena boundary and ally benefits from its current position. You cannot sustain Bless separately while it moves."}], "e030": [{"name": "Massive Push", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Virtual Mass Increase", "text": "The shove of the collapse: once per turn, a critical while mass is active pushes the target fifteen feet directly away — forced movement, no opportunity taken. Once per turn when you score a critical hit while virtual mass is active, push the target 15 feet directly away. This is forced movement and causes no opportunity attack."}, {"name": "Shooting Star", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Virtual Mass Improvement", "text": "The kicked star: an action and five coins, while mass is active, to boot one unsecured object within reach down a fifty-by-five line — twice her base unarmed dice plus ability modifier on a failed Dexterity save, half on success. The injury check follows only if the single damage meets the revised threshold. Action, 5 CE while mass is active: kick one unsecured object within reach through a 50-by-5-foot line. Creatures make Dexterity saves, taking twice your base unarmed dice plus attack ability modifier bludgeoning on failure, half on success. A failed save also allows an injury check only if that single damage meets the revised threshold."}, {"name": "Maximum: Black Hole", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Virtual Mass Mastery", "text": "The Maximum is the star's death, priced accordingly: twenty coins, a radius to a hundred feet, and she is irrevocably sacrificed — her body the singularity. Strength saves: failure is death, success is survival pulled thirty feet toward the center; the death-immune take 20d10 force instead. No ordinary revival answers. Action, 20 CE: choose a radius up to 100 feet and irrevocably sacrifice yourself; your body becomes the singularity. Other creatures make Strength saves. Failure dies; success survives and is pulled 30 feet toward center. A creature immune to instant death instead takes 20d10 force on failure, half on success. Ordinary RCT or revival cannot restore you."}], "e031": [{"name": "Nail Volley", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Nail Projectile", "text": "The scattered punctuation: an action spends up to her modifier in coins and nails for a cone ten feet long per nail — Dexterity saves, a d4 per nail piercing, half on success. The nails land in the area and may be recovered. Action: spend X CE and consume X nails, X from 1 to CE modifier. Create a cone 10 × X feet long. Creatures make Dexterity saves, taking Xd4 piercing on failure or half on success. All nails land in the area and may be recovered normally."}, {"name": "1000 Needles", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Hairpin", "text": "The barbed planting: one extra coin per nail when the Hairpin is set, and any creature failing a detonation save is restrained for a minute — Athletics or Acrobatics against her DC at each turn's end to escape, a d8 of piercing for each failed attempt. The nails do not stack their cruelty. When planting Hairpin nails, pay 1 extra CE per nail. A creature failing any detonation save is restrained for 1 minute. At each turn’s end it chooses Athletics or Acrobatics against CE DC; success ends it, failure deals 1d8 piercing. Multiple nails do not stack the condition or damage."}, {"name": "Maximum: Last Nail in the Coffin", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Improved Resonance", "text": "The Maximum: while a Resonance link persists, an action and ten coins uproot every planted Hairpin nail — wherever they were set — and drive them unerringly into the linked target, detonating on arrival as one Hairpin. All nails consumed, the link ended. The coffin gets its last nail. Action, 10 CE while a Resonance link persists: every nail you planted with Hairpin uproots and streaks unerringly to the linked target, detonating on arrival as Hairpin - one Dexterity save, 6d8 + (X - 1)d8 force for X nails, half on success - regardless of where they were planted. All nails are consumed and the link ends."}], "e032": [{"name": "Blessed Blow", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Extinguishment", "text": "The refusal, delivered by hand: on a weapon hit, a coin and the forfeited damage force the Charisma save against Extinguishment's suppression — no radiant damage. Failure suppresses until the end of her next turn. When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you may spend 1 CE and forgo the attack's damage to force it to make the Charisma save against your Extinguishment's suppression, dealing no radiant damage. On a failure it is suppressed until the end of your next turn; on a success nothing happens."}, {"name": "Archangel’s Present", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Angel’s Blessing and Breakthrough", "text": "The open gift: when the breakthrough occurs, choose a Blessing suited to it and record its complete rules. A custom Blessing of comparable scope is valid with the GM's approval — the choir improvises within its key. Choose a Blessing suited to the breakthrough when it occurs and record its complete rules. A custom Blessing of comparable scope is also valid with your GM’s approval."}, {"name": "Sword of Michael", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Maximum: Jacob’s Ladder and CE score 20", "text": "The trumpet, narrowed to a blade: an action, the Ladder's cost plus five coins, one melee attack — on a hit, that creature alone suffers 10d12 radiant and the revised Ladder nullification. On a miss, every coin is spent. No area, only the one judgment. Action: pay Jacob’s Ladder’s normal cost +5 CE and make one melee CE attack. On hit the creature alone suffers 10d12 radiant damage and the revised Jacob’s Ladder technique-nullification effect; on miss all CE is spent. It does not create the original area."}], "e033": [{"name": "Maximum: Crippling Strikes", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Unblockable Blows and CE score 20", "text": "The unblockable, extended to the inanimate: his attacks ignore damage thresholds, and a structure's, barrier's, or ward's immunity softens to resistance. Shatter a barrier or object, and the remaining damage carries through to one creature directly behind it. Your Unblockable Blows extends to the inanimate: your attacks ignore damage thresholds, and a structure's, barrier's, or ward's immunity to your damage becomes resistance. When such an attack destroys a barrier or object, remaining damage carries to one creature directly behind it."}, {"name": "Maximum: Blast Away", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Energy Blast and CE score 20", "text": "The blast, ridden: aim Energy Blast at empty space within five feet, and the recoil launches him twenty feet in his chosen direction — no opportunity taken, no damage suffered. Spend five or more coins, and a fifteen-foot cone behind his path saves Strength or is pushed ten feet and knocked prone. When you use Energy Blast, you may target a point in free space within 5 feet of yourself instead of a creature. You are launched 20 feet in a direction of your choice without provoking opportunity attacks and take no damage from the blast. If you spent at least 5 CE, each creature in a 15-foot cone behind your path makes a Strength save or is pushed 10 feet and knocked prone."}, {"name": "Maximum: Fortress", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Defensive Form and CE score 20", "text": "The ward, detonated: an action, while holding Defensive Form's temporary hit points, ends the form and turns the ward outward — creatures within ten feet save Constitution against force equal to the remaining temporary hit points, half on success, pushed ten feet on failure. He is unaffected; the fortress was always his. Action while you hold Defensive Form temporary HP: end the form to detonate the ward. Each creature within 10 feet makes a Constitution save, taking force damage equal to the remaining temporary HP on failure (half on success) and being pushed 10 feet on a failed save. You are unaffected."}], "e034": [{"name": "Partial Manifestation Versatility", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Partial Manifestation", "text": "Her partial hand need not only wound — it can seize, shove, unbalance. The commander who uses his detachment only for killing wastes half its worth. A hand that can grip is worth a hand that can cut. Once per turn when Partial Manifestation would add damage, forgo all of that added damage to attempt one grapple or shove against the hit target as part of the attack, using your CE ability in place of Strength if desired."}, {"name": "Technique Storage", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Mimicry", "text": "What she has learned, he may wield through his own hands — her library opened to him while she stands near, the techniques flowing through his action instead of hers. Two warriors, one arsenal. The deepest trust in war: to let another's learning become your own muscle. A technique your spirit has mimicked can be wielded through you: while the spirit is manifested, partially or fully, you may use your action to activate one stored mimicry as if you knew it, paying its CE cost and using your attack bonus and save DC. The spirit cannot activate that same mimicry on the same turn."}, {"name": "Directed Frenzy", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Stronger Bond", "text": "Even in berserk grief, she can be pointed. Name the enemy, and the flood aims itself — her fury given a single direction, her blows falling with advantage on the named. The storm does not calm. It is merely told where to rain. There is no taming love like this; there is only aiming it. While the appendix spirit is berserk, use a bonus action to name one creature you can see. Until the start of your next turn the spirit treats that creature as the last creature to damage you when choosing targets, and its attacks against the named creature have advantage. This does not end the berserk state."}], "e035": [{"name": "Divine Dog Totality", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Divine Dogs tamed, and one Divine Dog has died (reduced to 0 HP).", "text": "When one Dog has fallen, the survivor may inherit — the Totality hound, carrying its packmate's strength in its own frame. Grief, forged into muscle. The lone hound that remains is no longer half a pair; it is the pair, remembered in one body. Inheritance. Manifest the surviving Dog as Divine Dog Totality. Totality is mutually exclusive with both original Dogs and uses the revised Totality stat block."}, {"name": "Shadow Skulker", "prereq": "", "text": "He may sink into his own shadow and travel within it — unseen, untouchable, perceiving the world from darkness, commanding his officers while submerged. The general become a rumor: present everywhere through his shadows, personally nowhere. Emerge where the shadow falls. An army whose commander cannot be found cannot be beheaded. Shadow movement. As an action for 2 CE, submerge into your shadow for consecutive turns equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum one). While submerged, you have total cover and perceive the space around your shadow; your shadow moves across connected surfaces at half your speed; you may summon, dismiss, and command Ten Shadows shikigami; you cannot personally attack, use RCT, expand a Domain, or activate other cursed techniques. Emerge within 5 feet as a bonus action. You are forcibly ejected when the duration ends — or at the end of your next turn if no manifested shikigami remain."}, {"name": "Chimerafication", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Wells Unknown Abyss and a 20 CE ability score.", "text": "Beyond the fifteen stable marriages lies the freeform art: one base, up to three donors, no shadow sacrificed, none required dead — living fusion, built to order. Zagroth, Hageshi, Agito: the named precedents. The commander's late mastery: to compose his forces the way a poet composes verse, to the occasion. Freeform fusion. Build one base plus as many as three donor additions under the Chimerafication rules: living shikigami combine — no shadow is sacrificed and none need be dead. Three ready-to-play presets — Zagroth, Hageshi, and Agito — appear in the Fusion Catalog."}, {"name": "Maximum: Embodiment", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Chimera Shadow Garden (Domain Expansion).", "text": "The Maximum: rather than summoning the shadow, he becomes it — its movement, its actions, its nature, worn for an hour. To borrow Mahoraga's Wheel is to borrow adaptation itself: exposure, resistance, immunity, turning above his own head. The final lesson of command: the general who has mastered his officers may, for a little while, become each of them. Maximum Technique. As an action, spend half the manifestation cost (minimum 1 CE) of one of your tamed shikigami (no Totality or Chimera). Rather than summoning it, you instead gain that shikigami's movement, actions, legendary actions, features, and one ability score of your choice for 1 hour. You can embody one shikigami at a time. Mahoraga: borrowing Mahoraga's Adaptation grants its Eight-Handled Wheel three-stage adaptation as described in this dossier's Mahoraga stat block (damage types, conditions, and obstacles each adapt through exposure → resistance → immunity or functional counter)."}], "e036": [{"name": "Early Trigger", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Siphon", "text": "Bonus action: reset your Siphon Counter to 0. If it was at least 2 - or at least 1 from level 6 - Siphon triggers immediately against the last creature you hit since your last turn, draining as normal. If the counter was lower, nothing happens."}, {"name": "Redistributed Drain", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Siphon, level 4", "text": "Bonus action: transfer any amount of your Temporary CE to a willing creature within 30 feet. It gains that Temporary CE, up to its own cap, and you lose it; transferred CE expires on its normal schedule."}, {"name": "Blood-Price Champion", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Amphitheater of the Living Dead", "text": "Once per round when one of your qualifying attacks removes Gladiator HP from a hostile competitor, add 1 CE to the Colosseum Pool after the damage resolves. If that attack was a critical hit, add your PB instead. This contribution does not drain either combatant and cannot itself change Favor until the Pool is recalculated."}, {"name": "Curator of Spoils", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Colosseum Spoils", "text": "You may lend a Spoil you hold to a willing creature: it gains the Spoil's benefit until your next long rest, and you cannot benefit from it meanwhile. Reclaim it as a bonus action while within 60 feet."}], "e037": [{"name": "Flywheel Counter", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Kinetic Transmission", "text": "When you take bludgeoning, piercing, slashing, force, or thunder damage, use your reaction and spend 2 CE. Roll PB Drive Dice and add CE modifier once, reducing the damage by the total. Gain 1 Gear per Drive Die, maximum Gear 10. If inactive, Kinetic Transmission activates at Gear 0 before these Gears are gained."}, {"name": "Suspended Interval", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Velocity Override, level 6", "text": "Projectile: reaction and 3 CE; stop one moving physical projectile within 60 feet for up to 1 minute. Maintain up to PB and release any number as a bonus action, making ranged CE attacks."}, {"name": "Vector Skip", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Clutch Control, CE 18+", "text": "When using Acceleration Shift, pay 1 additional CE. For every Gear lowered, teleport 20 feet instead of gaining 15 feet of speed. Bring one willing adjacent creature by lowering one additional Gear. Your first Impact Shift that turn adds one Drive Die."}, {"name": "Relativistic Break", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Redline, CE 20+, breakthrough", "text": "While at Gear 10 during Redline, as a full-turn action spend 10 CE and lower all 10 Gears. Travel instantly through a 300-foot, 15-foot-wide line. Creatures make Dexterity saves: failure takes 20d12 force, moves to the end, falls prone, and cannot react; success takes half only. Damage ignores resistance; immunity becomes resistance. Structures automatically fail and take maximum damage. Redline ends; take 4 Drive Dice unavoidable recoil and suffer Technique Burnout."}], "e038": [{"name": "Snare Glyph", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Directive Inscription", "text": "When you inscribe arrows, you may designate up to PB of them as snares. When a hostile creature enters a snare's space, use your reaction to expend it: the creature makes a Strength save or is moved the full Arrow Distance in the arrow's direction without provoking opportunity attacks. You decide which arrows are snares when placing them."}, {"name": "Rescue Vector", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Shared Route", "text": "When a willing creature is targeted by an attack while within 10 feet of one of your arrows, use your reaction, spend 2 CE, and expend that arrow to move the creature its full Arrow Distance in the displayed direction without provoking. Recalculate the attack’s reach, range, line, and cover from the new space; it misses only if the target is no longer legal."}, {"name": "Double Bank", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Projectile Redirection", "text": "When you use Projectile Redirection, you may spend 1 additional CE and expend a second active arrow whose space lies in the redirected line. The same attack changes direction again from that arrow before finding its final target. This is one reaction, uses the original attack roll and source, and is an explicit exception to the ordinary one-redirection limit; it cannot be redirected a third time."}, {"name": "Shared Vector Edge", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Acceleraise Boost", "text": "Once per round after a willing creature activates one or more of your arrows and hits with a weapon attack, use your reaction and spend 1 CE. Add one current Arrow Die per arrow it activated that turn, maximum PB dice, to that hit as force damage. This cannot combine with Acceleraise Boost on the same hit, but it can support a different ally or a later turn."}], "e039": [{"name": "Bestowed Memory", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Solar Memory", "text": "When you complete the Solar Memory rite, you may store the rank in a willing creature's held weapon or worn object instead of yourself. That creature may release it once as a bonus action for 2 CE, gaining its effects for 1 minute; the memory is then expended. You cannot release a bestowed memory."}, {"name": "Corona of Command", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Sunshine", "text": "While your effective rank is at least 2, use an action and 3 CE to release a corona pulse: each hostile within 15 feet makes a Constitution save or is blinded until the end of your next turn, and each ally in the pulse has advantage on saves against being frightened or charmed until the end of your next turn. You cannot pulse again until 1 minute passes."}, {"name": "Night-Prowling Lion", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Pride Incarnate", "text": "At effective rank 0, use a bonus action and 1 CE to begin the prowl for 1 minute: you leave no tracks, have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks, and your first weapon or unarmed hit each turn against a creature that cannot see you deals an extra Solar Die of damage. This grants no rank, sunlight, or daylight features."}, {"name": "Grace Bestowed", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Solar Infusion, level 6", "text": "When a willing creature within 120 feet hits with a weapon, unarmed, natural, or CE attack carrying its own CE, use your reaction and pay Solar Infusion’s normal 1 CE to add your current Solar Infusion damage to that hit. This use counts against every per-turn Solar Infusion limit and receives the same station and Perfect Grace multipliers."}], "e040": [{"name": "Armed Ally", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Charge Object", "text": "During a short or long rest, you may charge one object and gift it to a willing creature: its Charge lasts 24 hours in their hands, and they may release it as you could, using your Kinetic Die. You may maintain up to PB such gifted charges; gifting beyond the limit ends one of your choice."}, {"name": "Twin Conduits", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Bound Conduit", "text": "While touching two charged objects, you may link them as a circuit without an action (once per turn). When one releases its Charge, the other immediately releases half its Charge, rounded down, as part of the same detonation, sharing the first object's radius and save. Either object detonating normally breaks the circuit."}, {"name": "Kinetic Catch", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Loaded Toss, level 6", "text": "When you see a physical ranged attack made against a creature within 30 feet, after seeing its roll but before resolution, use your reaction and spend 2 CE. Make a CE attack roll. If your total equals or exceeds the triggering attack roll, that attack misses and its projectile lands in an empty hand or at your feet with 1 Charge. This cannot catch an area, energy beam, siege projectile larger than you, artifact, or attack without a physical projectile."}, {"name": "Royal Flush", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Cardsharp Barrage, level 9", "text": "After one Cardsharp Barrage resolves, if at least four of its separate attacks hit the same creature, that creature makes a Constitution save. On failure it is stunned until the start of your next turn as overlapping kinetic vectors arrest its body. On success it cannot take reactions until the start of your next turn. The condition is one result of the barrage, not an additional hit or detonation."}], "e041": [{"name": "Tripwire", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Bungee Gum", "text": "Stretch a strand across a doorway, corridor, or trail and leave it: the instant anything crosses it you know its size and number, and it can't surprise you. The strand holds until detached, no concentration required."}, {"name": "Gum Gag", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Bungee Gum", "text": "Contract a strand across a stuck creature's mouth as part of the same bonus action you use to pull it: it can't speak or supply verbal components until it breaks free (an action, Strength check vs. your CE save DC). Quiet is a kind of winning."}, {"name": "False Floor", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Texture Surprise", "text": "Texture Surprise can disguise a pit, snare, or doorway as solid ground or blank wall. The first creature to cross it must succeed on an Investigation check against your CE save DC or fall in — or walk straight through a door it never saw."}, {"name": "Card Return", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Bungee Gum", "text": "A strand left on a thrown weapon or object lets you recall it to your hand as a bonus action from up to 120 feet away, arcing back along the strand. Hisoka's cards always come back."}, {"name": "Bungee Parachute", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Slingshot", "text": "Anchor a strand to anything above you — a ceiling, a branch, the shimmer in the air is enough — and descend any distance safely. As a reaction, you can arrest another falling creature within 60 feet the same way."}], "e042": [{"name": "Unbroken Mudra", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Prayer Palm", "text": "Your interrupted gestures still complete themselves. When a Palm attack misses, the mudra flows through unbroken: make a second Palm attack against a different creature within 15 feet of the original target as part of the same Palm, paying 1 CE for the echo. If the echo misses, the gesture ends."}, {"name": "Great Compassion", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Prayer Palm", "text": "Your mercy widens to cover two. When Merciful Palm moves a willing creature, you may spend 1 CE to move a second willing creature within 15 feet of the first the same distance along the same vector, resolved with the same roll. When Guarding Palm shields a willing creature, you may spend 1 CE to extend its damage reduction to a second willing creature adjacent to the first."}, {"name": "Opening Salutation", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Prayer Before Violence", "text": "Immediately after initiative is rolled, once per combat, you may perform one Merciful Palm on yourself or a willing creature within Palm Reach without spending an action, reaction, or CE. Resolve this movement before the first turn is taken; it cannot target an unwilling creature."}, {"name": "Hundred-and-First Hand: Lotus Prison", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Third Hand: Converging Mercy", "text": "As an action for 4 CE, choose one creature within Palm Reach and make three ranged CE attacks against it. Each hit deals 2 Prayer Dice of force or radiant damage; add your CE modifier to one hit only. If at least two attacks hit, spectral petals restrain the target until the end of your next turn. The prison has AC equal to your CE save DC and HP equal to 10 × PB; destroying it ends the restraint."}, {"name": "The Hundredth Name", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ninety-Ninth Hand: Endless Litany", "text": "Invent your own hand: combine two intentions into a single Palm, paying 1 CE per intention and resolving both effects — a Grasping-Merciful hand that restrains a willing ally to drag them from danger without harming them, a Guarding-Driving hand that shoves an ally clear while shielding them. Once named, the hand is yours permanently; describe its prayer."}], "e044": [{"name": "Many Names, One Banner", "prereq": "Prerequisite: War God's Household", "text": "Your names answer from afar. When you use Battle Muster, you may call one Regalia into vessel form at a point you can see within 60 feet instead of beside you — a Sky Lion where your allies need it, a shield already in a friend's hands. It still counts against your Active Limit."}, {"name": "Line That Casts Out Evil", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Borderline", "text": "Your Borderline may be up to 120 feet long, may bend once at a point you can see, and ignores chosen nonhostile creatures. A hostile creature that fails its save is also Restrained until the end of its turn. If it succeeds, it crosses and cannot be affected by that Borderline again that turn."}, {"name": "Blessed Beyond Death", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Blessed Vessel, level 12", "text": "A blessed vessel's devotion extends to its kin. When a non-Blessed Regalia would become Broken, your Blessed Vessel may use its reaction to suffer the breaking in its place: the Blessed Vessel becomes Broken instead, and the other Regalia remains at 1 Integrity."}, {"name": "Cavalry of Heaven", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Sky Lion vessel, level 6", "text": "Every Sky Lion can carry you plus PB willing Medium or smaller creatures. Once on each of your turns after the Lion moves at least 30 feet, one rider may use its reaction to make one weapon attack or take the Disengage action. A creature can benefit from Cavalry of Heaven only once per round."}], "e045": [{"name": "Postage Due", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Dimensional Authorship", "text": "A folded victim makes an excellent parcel. When you successfully Fold the Panel on a creature, you may immediately use Panel Step — paying its normal cost plus 1 CE — and carry the folded target with you to your destination. It remains folded until the fold’s normal duration ends."}, {"name": "Smash Cut", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Panel Step, level 6", "text": "Once per turn after Panel Step, spend 2 CE to make one weapon attack or Panel Strike without an action. On a hit add one RD and move yourself and the target up to 15 feet in the same direction."}, {"name": "Living Illustration", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Prop Extraction, level 8", "text": "As an action, spend 5 CE and choose a creature depicted in an image within Snap Range. You manifest it in an unoccupied space beside that image for 1 hour; it counts as one Active Edit. It has AC 15 + half PB, HP equal to 10 × PB, speed 40 feet, and one attack using your CE attack bonus that deals 2 RD + your CE modifier in an appropriate damage type. It acts immediately after you and Dodges unless you command it with a bonus action. If reduced to 0 HP, dismissed without an action, or no longer within Snap Range at the end of your turn, it folds back into its source image."}, {"name": "Unreliable Narrator", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Dimensional Authorship, level 4", "text": "As an action, spend 3 CE to place a false caption, sound, image, creature, object, or apparent terrain change inside a 30-foot cube within Snap Range for 10 minutes. The scene counts as one Active Edit and can include touch, temperature, scent, and convincing CE texture. A creature that uses an action to investigate makes an Intelligence save against your Technique DC, recognizing the false scene on a success. Physical interaction does not automatically reveal it; the fiction supplies expected resistance but cannot deal damage, restrain a creature, or bear real weight."}, {"name": "Continuity Error", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Dimensional Authorship, level 14", "text": "When you are reduced to 0 HP, killed by damage, or subjected to an incapacitating condition, use your reaction and spend 8 CE to restore your HP, CE, position, dimensions, and conditions to their state at the start of your previous turn. Other creatures, spent items, and scene changes are not reversed. The first use per long rest is safe; each later use before that rest inflicts 2 levels of exhaustion that cannot be prevented or removed until the scene ends."}, {"name": "Executive Editor", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Authorial Privilege, level 18", "text": "You make two cuts in a single motion. When you apply Cut Turn to a hostile creature, you may spend 2 additional CE to also apply Reblock Scene to that creature alone, teleporting it to a legal space within Snap Range as its turn is removed. This combination costs no additional Authorial Privilege use."}], "e046": [{"name": "Redmane Greatbow", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Gravity Sovereignty", "text": "You can mark ammunition as part of firing it. Long-range weapon attacks against a marked creature ignore disadvantage from long range, and once per turn a hit may Pull the target 10 feet."}, {"name": "Lion’s Gravity", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 6", "text": "When you succeed on a save against forced movement or prone, use your reaction to place an Anchor mark on yourself and Pull the source 15 feet toward you if it is within Gravity Range."}, {"name": "Starcaller’s Mark", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Starcaller Cry", "text": "What the cry cannot crush, it claims. Each creature that succeeds on its save against Starcaller Cry gains a Gravity Mark with the Anchor vector for 1 minute, with no additional save; a creature can carry only one such mark at a time."}, {"name": "Grand Conjunction", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Maximum: Festival of Falling Stars", "text": "You merge held meteors into a greater one. When you launch meteors as a bonus action, you may merge two or more into a single burst: it creates a 15-foot-radius burst dealing 4d8 per merged meteor, with a Dexterity save for half. Declare the merger before launching."}], "e047": [{"name": "Beast’s Agility", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Destined Death", "text": "After using Beast Step, you may move along walls or ceilings for that movement without falling until it ends, the beast’s stride ignoring the floor’s claim on it."}, {"name": "Rune-Eater", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Deathbrand", "text": "When a creature with Fate Scars spends 3+ CE on one activation, once per round you may use your reaction to extend all its Fate Scars by 1 round."}, {"name": "Black Knife Geometry", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Black Blade Wave", "text": "Black Blade Wave ignores half and three-quarters cover and can originate from the edge of your manifested blade even while you are airborne."}, {"name": "The Beast Collects", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 11", "text": "You harvest the dooms you have marked. When you would drop to 0 HP, use your reaction and spend 3 CE to consume all Fate Scars on one creature you can see within 60 feet, regaining 10 HP per scar consumed. If this healing leaves you above 0 HP, you do not fall unconscious."}], "e048": [{"name": "Sigil Shatter", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Dark Moon Covenant", "text": "As a bonus action, consume all Lunar Sigils on one creature you can perceive within Lunar Range. It takes 5 cold damage per sigil consumed, and its speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of your next turn as the shattered cold sinks into its limbs."}, {"name": "Bell of Many Ashes", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ashen Familiar", "text": "When your Ashen Familiar is destroyed, its ashes remember the cold. It bursts into freezing mist: creatures within 10 feet of it make a Constitution save against your Technique DC, taking 5 cold damage and suffering −10 speed until the end of your next turn on a failure, or half damage on a success."}, {"name": "Occult Moon", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Cold Moon Guard", "text": "The dark moon returns what it swallows. When Cold Moon Guard fully negates a ranged technique attack, you may immediately make one Lunar Bolt attack against the attacker as part of the same reaction, spending 1 CE or 1 Moon Shard."}, {"name": "Fingerslayer Principle", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 11", "text": "Your Dark Moon learns new prey. It may target control effects, barriers, and technique-created constructs in addition to technique manifestations, using the normal suppression check. Domains remain beyond it."}], "e049": [{"name": "Feed the Flame", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Flame of Frenzy", "text": "As a bonus action, voluntarily gain 1 Madness, feeding the fire on purpose. The next Frenzy feature you use before the end of your turn deals +1 Frenzy Die."}, {"name": "Shabriri’s Cry", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Howl of Frenzy", "text": "You learn to aim the howl. While Howl of Frenzy is active, you may use your bonus action to loose a focused cry at one creature within 30 feet that can hear you; it makes a Wisdom save against your Technique DC, becoming frightened of you until the end of its next turn on a failure. The cry adds no Madness."}, {"name": "Yellow-Eyed Prophet", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 6", "text": "You can sense frightened, charmed, or Madness-affected creatures within 120 feet even without line of sight."}, {"name": "Lord Candidate", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 11", "text": "The first time each long rest you would gain Madness above 10, instead gain PB temporary HP per excess point and remain at 10."}], "e050": [{"name": "Apostle’s Reach", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Black Flame Apostasy", "text": "In Apostle stance, your opportunity attacks may apply Kindling, paying its normal CE cost — the long limb punishes retreat with godfire."}, {"name": "Shared Vestments", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Black Flame Apostasy", "text": "As a bonus action for 1 CE, extend your Godskin Stance to one willing creature within 15 feet until the start of your next turn. It gains the stance’s passive benefits — Apostle’s speed and reach, or Noble’s armor and stability — but not your armament, Black Flame, or stance actions."}, {"name": "Swaddling Cloth", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Swaddling Recovery", "text": "When you would gain temporary HP from Swaddling Recovery, you may instead grant those temporary HP to one willing creature within 15 feet, wrapping it in spectral swaddling cloth."}, {"name": "Choir of Two", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Skinbound Partner", "text": "Partner gains proficiency in one skill you have; while within 30 feet, you may perceive through its senses without an action."}], "e051": [{"name": "Static Sense", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Godspeed: Whirlwind", "text": "While Godspeed is active, you read the room by its charge: you can sense living creatures within 30 feet of you, even through darkness, invisibility, or thin cover — the storm feels every heartbeat's electricity. This reveals presence and direction only, not identity."}, {"name": "Programmed Fall", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Godspeed: Whirlwind", "text": "Set Whirlwind's standing orders to include the ground: while Godspeed is active, you cannot be knocked prone by falling, you always land on your feet, and you take no falling damage — the program catches you before the floor does."}, {"name": "Ground Wire", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Speed of Lightning", "text": "As a reaction when you or an ally within 15 feet would take lightning damage, you may absorb it: the target takes none, and you learn the direction and distance of the damage's source — the current tells you where it was born. You may do this even while Godspeed is inactive."}, {"name": "Thunderclap", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Thunderbolt", "text": "You may call Thunderbolt as a flash instead of a strike: no damage, but each creature within 30 feet of the point that can see must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your CE save DC or be blinded until the end of your next turn. The storm announces itself."}, {"name": "Dead-Man's Program", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Counter-Program", "text": "While Godspeed (Whirlwind) is active, you may set one contingency order (\"if I fall unconscious, move 30 feet toward the door\"). If the trigger occurs — even if you are incapacitated or unconscious — Whirlwind executes it immediately, no action required. The program outlives the programmer's awareness."}], "e052": [{"name": "Flowing Blade Disciple", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Scarlet Bloom", "text": "When you move through a hostile creature’s threatened space using Flowing Sword, you may leave an afterimage behind. The next attack that creature makes against you before the start of your next turn has disadvantage, striking the image instead. Once per round."}, {"name": "Cleanrot Resolve", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Rot Marks", "text": "The hand that sows the rot can reap it. As an action for 2 CE, touch a creature bearing your Rot Marks or suffering your Scarlet Rot and end the condition, removing all marks. Mercy, interrogation, or cleaning up after your own Aeonia — the rot obeys its gardener."}, {"name": "Waterfowl Savant", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Waterfowl Dance", "text": "You may perform Waterfowl Dance as a defensive spiral, forgoing all of its attacks. Until the start of your next turn, melee attacks against you have disadvantage and your movement does not provoke opportunity attacks."}, {"name": "Rot-Petal Squall", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Scarlet Wings", "text": "While Scarlet Wings is active, as a bonus action for 1 CE, beat your wings in a rot-laden gust. Each hostile creature within 15 feet makes a Constitution save against your Technique DC; on a failure it gains one Rot Mark. A creature can gain only one mark this way per round."}], "e053": [{"name": "Carian Dueling Form", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Twin Moon Armament", "text": "The duelist’s art: mark one creature, strike it with both Moon and Flame while the mark lasts, and it becomes Eclipsed — disadvantage on attacks against anyone but you. Two blades, one opponent; no distractions permitted. As a bonus action for 1 CE, mark one creature within 30 feet as your duelist until the end of your next turn. If you hit it with both a Moon-imbued and a Flame-imbued attack while it is marked, it becomes Eclipsed until the end of its next turn: it has disadvantage on attack rolls against creatures other than you."}, {"name": "Phalanx Reserve", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Carian Phalanx", "text": "The retinue can shield as well as strike: order the glintblades into a screening orbit, and ranged attacks against you miss more often — each miss shattering one blade in interception. A shield that spends itself is still a shield; count the cost. As a bonus action, order your active glintblades into a screening orbit until the start of your next turn. Ranged attacks against you have disadvantage; each time a ranged attack misses you, one glintblade of your choice shatters intercepting it."}, {"name": "Messmer Ember", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Flame Spiral", "text": "The Spiral leaves a wake of embers, and the knight’s post-resolution movement becomes a second attack — each hostile whose space she enters takes fire. Flame, once worn, keeps burning where she has been. Your spiral leaves an ember wake. Each hostile creature whose space you enter during Flame Spiral’s post-resolution movement takes 1 Twin Die of fire damage; a creature takes this damage only once per Spiral."}, {"name": "Moon Princess’s Guard", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Twin Aspect Guard", "text": "The ward extends beyond the self: Twin Aspect Guard can now shelter a willing creature within ten feet against the next matching instance. A knight’s guard was always meant to stand before another. Your ward extends to another. When you use Twin Aspect Guard, you may also shield one willing creature within 10 feet: it gains the same reduction against the next instance of the matching damage type before the start of your next turn."}], "e054": [{"name": "Dragon Communion Savant", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Dragonheart Incarnation", "text": "Learn another lineage’s breath rider and apply it to your primary Breath for +1 CE, without its resistance. The heart’s memories, cross-bred. Learn one additional lineage’s breath rider; you may apply it to your primary Breath by paying +1 CE, without gaining its resistance."}, {"name": "Scale Shelter", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Gravel Scales", "text": "While Gravel Scales is active, bonus action: extend plates over a willing creature within 5 ft for +1 AC till your next turn — your own scales undiminished. The debtor shares the armor. While Gravel Scales is active, as a bonus action you may extend stony plates over one willing creature within 5 feet; it gains +1 AC until the start of your next turn. Your own scales are not diminished by the sharing."}, {"name": "Winged Predator", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Wings", "text": "Descend 20+ ft before a melee attack: target Strength save or prone; you land safely. The sky, converted into leverage. After descending at least 20 feet before a melee attack, the target makes a Strength save or falls prone; you land without falling damage."}, {"name": "Dragonlord’s Echo", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 11", "text": "Originate Dragonstorm at a visible point within 90 ft instead of centered on yourself. The storm answers at a distance. The storm answers at a distance. You may originate Dragonstorm at a point you can see within 90 feet instead of centered on yourself, shaping the same 30-foot-radius storm around that point."}], "e055": [{"name": "Ground Slam", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Rock, Charging Fist", "text": "Release the charge downward instead of at a creature: all within fifteen feet save or take the Rock’s damage and fall prone. Sometimes the honest target is the floor. You may release a Rock charge downward instead of at a creature: each creature within 15 feet of you must succeed on a Strength saving throw against your CE save DC or take the Rock's damage and be knocked prone (half damage on a success, no prone). The charge is spent. Sometimes the honest target is the floor."}, {"name": "Signal Paper", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Paper", "text": "Fire Paper into the sky as a signal — a palm of aura visible for miles, shaping one short word, dealing no damage. Subtlety was never part of the game. You may fire Paper straight into the sky as a signal instead of an attack: a palm of aura visible for miles in daylight, farther at night, shaping one short word if you form it. It deals no damage. Gon never needed subtlety."}, {"name": "Sunder", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Scissors", "text": "Forgo Scissors’ damage to cut instead: destroy one nonmagical object held or worn — rope, weapon, strap, mask. The edge that scores can also sever. When you strike with Scissors, you may forgo damage to cut instead: destroy one nonmagical object the target holds or wears — a rope, a weapon, a strap, a mask. Against bindings or restraints worn by someone else, this works provided you can reach them."}, {"name": "Aftershock", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Rock, Charging Fist", "text": "When the released Rock hits, 1 CE drives the shockwave through: one creature directly behind the target within fifteen feet saves or takes half the Rock’s damage. The punch doesn’t stop at the first body. When your released Rock hits, you may spend 1 CE to drive the shockwave through: choose one creature directly behind the target within 15 feet — it must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw against your CE save DC or take half the Rock's damage. The punch doesn't stop at the first body."}, {"name": "Paper Mine", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Paper", "text": "Press a Paper charge into a touched object: the next creature to handle it triggers the blast — 3d8 on a failed Dexterity save, half on a success, lasting an hour. Even an honest game has traps. As an action, spend 1 CE to press a Paper charge into an object you touch: the next creature to pick up or handle the object triggers the blast (Dexterity saving throw against your CE save DC; 3d8 bludgeoning on a failure, half on a success). The mine lasts 1 hour or until triggered. Even an honest game has traps."}], "e056": [{"name": "Pre-Wound", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ripper Cyclotron", "text": "Winds banked outside combat last ten minutes instead of one. Walk into the fight already spinning — the first punch of the day is the one you started before the door opened. Preparation is a weapon; this feat makes it a doctrine. Winds gained outside of combat last 10 minutes instead of 1 minute. Walk into the fight already spinning — the first punch of the day is the one you started before the door opened."}, {"name": "Bank Shot", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Shockwave Release", "text": "The shockwave line may reflect off one solid surface — around a corner, off the ceiling, off a wall. The rotation doesn’t care about straight lines, and now neither does the geometry of the fight. Your shockwave line may reflect off one solid surface, changing direction once — around a corner, off the ceiling, off a wall. Declare the bounce when you release. The rotation doesn't care about straight lines."}, {"name": "Backblast", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Bleed-Off", "text": "When Bleed-Off vents winds into survival, the spin erupts outward: creatures within ten feet save or are pushed ten feet away. Survival, with a shockwave — the vented spring kicks on its way out. When you Bleed-Off winds to reduce damage, the vented spin erupts outward: each creature within 10 feet of you must succeed on a Strength saving throw against your CE save DC or be pushed 10 feet away from you. Survival, with a shockwave."}, {"name": "Gyroscope", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ripper Cyclotron", "text": "The spinning arm steadies the body around it: while holding any winds, advantage on saves and checks against being knocked prone or moved. The rotation holds you upright — momentum as ballast. The spinning arm steadies the body around it: while you hold any winds, you have advantage on saving throws and ability checks against being knocked prone or moved against your will. The rotation holds you upright."}, {"name": "Wind Reading", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ripper Cyclotron", "text": "The spinning arm reads the air it displaces: while holding any winds, sense invisible or hidden creatures within fifteen feet — total cover excepted. The wind finds what eyes can’t; the arm is an instrument as well as a weapon. The spinning arm reads the air it displaces: while you hold any winds, you can sense the location of invisible or hidden creatures within 15 feet of you — the wind finds what eyes can't. This doesn't defeat total cover."}], "e057": [{"name": "Field Surgeon", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Doctor Blythe", "text": "Blythe stabilizes a dying creature within tether range as a reaction, no CE, once per round. The needle reaches the dying before the paperwork does. Blythe can stabilize a dying creature within tether range as a reaction without CE once per round."}, {"name": "Invisible Strings", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Puppeteer", "text": "Puppeteer attachments hide from passive CE perception; only an active check against your DC reveals them. The theater’s cast can wait in the wings, unseen. Your Puppeteer attachments are hidden from passive CE perception; active Perception/CE check vs your DC reveals them."}, {"name": "Feral En", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Predatory En", "text": "Shape the En as a narrow tendril at twice the range, or a broad sphere at a quarter. The stage can be a corridor or a room, at the puppeteer’s discretion. You can shape En as a narrow tendril at twice normal range or a broad sphere at one-quarter range."}, {"name": "Dance Beyond Death", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Terpsichora", "text": "When Terpsichora would end because you are incapacitated, spend 3 CE before you lose agency: she persists and moves you defensively on a preset command. The strings hold even when the dancer cannot. When Terpsichora would end because you are incapacitated, spend 3 CE before becoming unable to act; it persists until end of your next turn and moves you defensively according to a preset command."}], "e058": [{"name": "Payment Plan", "prereq": "Prerequisite: A.P.R. (Potclean)", "text": "The debtor may use its action to pay down the debt 1-for-1 with its own CE. Owing becomes a negotiation — and every payment is a turn not spent fighting you. The lender profits from the installments and the distraction alike. The debtor may use its action to pay down the debt: spend any amount of its own CE to reduce the debt 1-for-1. Owing becomes a negotiation — and every payment is a turn not spent fighting you."}, {"name": "Credit Check", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Audit", "text": "Spend 1 CE and glance at any creature within sixty feet: read its books — current and maximum CE — with no loan required. You’d be amazed what people leave lying around. Foreknowledge is the cheapest instrument in the firm. Spend 1 CE and glance at any creature within 60 feet: read its books — current CE and maximum CE — with no loan required. You'd be amazed what people leave lying around."}, {"name": "Predatory Lending", "prereq": "Prerequisite: A.P.R. (Potclean)", "text": "Seal a Binding Vow: once Potclean latches, you can’t dismiss it for a minute — and in exchange, interest rises to fifteen percent per round, compounding on old debt plus fresh damage. The vow is the rate hike; the restriction is the price of the arithmetic. Seal a Binding Vow: once Potclean latches, you can't dismiss it for 1 minute. In exchange, interest rises to 15% per round — new debt = (old debt + damage dealt since last tick) × 1.15, rounded down. The vow is the rate hike."}, {"name": "Debt Transfer", "prereq": "Prerequisite: A.P.R. (Potclean)", "text": "Move an active loan to a different creature within sixty feet of the debtor — attack roll vs. AC — and the full outstanding debt follows. Someone else’s problem now. The ledger doesn’t care whose name is on it, only that the numbers keep compounding. As an action, spend 1 CE: move an active loan to a different creature within 60 feet of the debtor (CE-ability attack vs. AC). The full outstanding debt follows. Someone else's problem now."}, {"name": "Collateral", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Chapter 7", "text": "When a debtor goes bankrupt, seize collateral: one nonmagical object they’re holding or wearing comes to your hand. The debt’s paid. The watch is yours. Liquidation leaves nothing on the table — not even the table. When a debtor goes bankrupt, seize collateral: one nonmagical object they're holding or wearing comes to your hand. The debt's paid. The watch is yours."}], "e059": [{"name": "False General", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Smoke, Obey", "text": "Shape one soldier into your exact likeness — face, voice, mannerisms — indistinguishable without close inspection against your CE save DC. It still dissipates when struck. The decoy’s only armor is being believed. Shape one soldier into your exact likeness — face, voice, mannerisms. It mimics you well enough that no one can distinguish it from you without close inspection (an Investigation check against your CE save DC). It still dissipates when struck."}, {"name": "Dead Drop", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Eyes in the Fog", "text": "Detail one soldier as a courier: it carries a message or small object up to ten miles over twenty-four hours, traveling as drifting smoke, interceptable only by effects that target smoke, fog, or aura. The army’s postal service runs on weather. Detail one soldier as a courier: it can carry a written message or a small object up to 10 miles over 24 hours, traveling as drifting smoke. It cannot be intercepted except by effects that specifically target smoke, fog, or aura."}, {"name": "Secondhand Lungs", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Smoke, Obey", "text": "Shape a soldier into a breathing mask over a willing creature’s face: for one hour, immunity to inhaled poisons and gases, and underwater breathing — the soldier filters everything. The fog that chokes armies can also keep one man alive. Shape a soldier into a breathing mask fitted over a willing creature's face. For 1 hour, that creature is immune to inhaled poisons and gases and can breathe underwater — the soldier filters everything. The mask dissipates if struck."}, {"name": "Fog of War", "prereq": "Prerequisite: The Ranks Swell", "text": "As an action, 2 CE: the soldiers exhale a sixty-foot cube of heavy smoke, lasting a minute — heavily obscured, proof even against magical sight, dispersed only by strong wind. The fog of war, issued on demand. As an action, spend 2 CE: your soldiers exhale a 60-foot cube of heavy smoke that lasts 1 minute. The area is heavily obscured, and not even magical sight can pierce it. A strong wind disperses it early."}, {"name": "The Last Soldier", "prereq": "Prerequisite: The General Vanishes", "text": "Once per long rest: at 0 hit points, dissolve instead of falling — re-form adjacent to your most distant soldier within three hundred feet at 1 hit point. The fog always keeps one private in reserve. The general’s last order is to himself: survive. Once per long rest, when you drop to 0 hit points, you may dissolve instead of falling: you re-form adjacent to your most distant soldier within 300 feet at 1 hit point. The fog always keeps one private in reserve."}], "e060": [{"name": "Low Waltz", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Battle Waltz", "text": "Bonus action: send one active top into a hostile’s space within thirty feet — Dexterity save or fall prone, tripped by the waltzing top, which then returns. The low step in the choreography. As a bonus action, send one active top spinning into a hostile creature’s space within 30 feet of the top. The creature makes a Dexterity save against your Technique DC or falls prone, tripped by the waltzing top; the top then returns to its previous position."}, {"name": "Gyro Balance", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Dancing Top", "text": "Attune one willing creature within thirty feet to the tops’ gyroscopic rhythm: advantage on checks and saves against being knocked prone, steadied by the hum. The waltz steadies its friends. As a bonus action, attune one willing creature within 30 feet to your tops’ gyroscopic rhythm until the start of your next turn. It has advantage on ability checks and saving throws against being knocked prone, steadied by the hum."}, {"name": "Blue Shot", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Shotgun Blues", "text": "In single-target Shotgun Blues, sacrifice one selected top to add 2 Top Dice — the top shatters after damage. One dancer spent for a louder note. When using single-target Shotgun Blues, sacrifice one selected top to add 2 Top Dice; the sacrificed top shatters after damage."}, {"name": "Ringmaster", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 11", "text": "Designate PB willing creatures that your simple “attack nearby” orders treat as friendly. The ringmaster decides who the tops do not bite. You may designate PB willing creatures that your simple “attack nearby” orders automatically treat as friendly."}], "e061": [{"name": "Armored Vessel", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Anime & Manga, level 4+", "text": "While Full Cowl is active the whole body is one braced vessel: use your reaction to reduce falling or collision damage by one Stockpile Die + PB. Distributed output, absorbing distributed impact. While Full Cowl is active, your whole body is one braced vessel. When you take falling damage or damage from a collision, you may use your reaction to reduce it by one Stockpile Die + PB, the distributed output absorbing the impact."}, {"name": "Tendril Snare", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Blackwhip", "text": "As an action for 2 CE, weave Blackwhip into a lattice across a fifteen-foot cube: difficult terrain for hostiles until your next turn, the first hostile entering saves or is restrained. The rescue tool, re-tasked as a trap. As an action for 2 CE, weave Blackwhip tendrils into a lattice across a 15-foot cube within reach. Until the start of your next turn the cube is difficult terrain for hostiles, and the first hostile to enter it must succeed on a Strength save against your Technique DC or be restrained until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Council of Embers", "prereq": "Prerequisite: at least two awakened Vestiges", "text": "Ten minutes in meditation convenes the past bearers: advantage on one Intelligence or Wisdom check within the next hour. Lifetimes of experience, consulted like a library. The past bearers hold counsel. Spend 10 minutes in meditation to convene them; you gain advantage on one Intelligence or Wisdom check made within the next hour, as the vestiges weigh in with lifetimes of experience."}, {"name": "Smash Artisan", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Air Force or Kinetic Surge", "text": "Fuse your signature forms: on a Smash hit, spend 2 CE to add one rider from another known Smash form — Groundbreak’s prone, St. Louis’s push, Whip-Sling’s continued movement. The stockpile’s forms, crossbred. You fuse your signature forms. When you hit with a Smash, you may spend 2 CE to add one rider from another Smash form you know: Groundbreak's prone (Dexterity save negates), St. Louis's push (5 feet × Output Band; Strength save halves), or Whip-Sling's continued movement (up to half your remaining speed). Only one added rider per Smash."}], "e099": [{"name": "Passive Filter", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 3", "text": "He extends his customs house over his allies: once per round, a known physical vector aimed at an ally within 15 ft is reflected as though it targeted him. Command extends its protection outward. You have learned to share your calculations: once per round, when an ally within 15 ft would be hit by a known physical vector, you may spend your reaction and 1 CE to extend your Filter over them, reflecting the attack as if it targeted you."}, {"name": "Kihara Counterstudy", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 6", "text": "He learns from the one who got through: once per long rest, a creature that bypassed his Filter finds the same bypass path turned against it — the reflection travels the attacker’s own road home, and cannot be dodged the second time. Once you have witnessed a creature bypass your Filter, you learn the path it took: once per long rest, when that creature attacks you with the same bypass method, you may spend a reaction and 2 CE to reflect the attack back along its own bypass path — it cannot use that method to avoid the reflection."}, {"name": "Borrowed Vector", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 9", "text": "An ally’s willing movement becomes his resource: redirect up to 20 ft of it to himself or another willing creature. Even generosity is a vector, and he is its master. Reaction when an ally within 30 ft willingly moves: redirect up to 20 ft of that movement to yourself or another willing creature."}, {"name": "White Wings", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Black Wings", "text": "When Black Wings would end, he may spend 4 CE to shed them as a single vector discharge — 4 Vector Dice and a 20-ft push to all within 20 ft. A wing that ends as a weapon. Nothing of his is ever simply discarded. When Black Wings would end, you may spend 4 CE to shed the wings in a single vector discharge instead: each creature within 20 ft makes a Str save, taking 4 Vector Dice force and being pushed 20 ft on a failure, or half damage and no push on a success. Black Wings then ends."}], "e100": [{"name": "Good Dog", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Dominion", "text": "Her Compelled throw themselves into harm’s way: once per round, when she would be hit, one within 15 ft may interpose itself with its reaction. Loyalty, operationalized. Your Compelled creatures throw themselves in harm's way: once per round, when you would be hit by an attack, a Compelled creature within 15 ft may use its reaction to interpose itself, becoming the target instead."}, {"name": "Contract Lawyer", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Public Safety Contract", "text": "She enforces the fine print: when a creature breaks the price of a written contract she holds, a reaction and 2 CE calls in the debt — a failed Cha save makes it Dominion-eligible. Default is a kind of confession. You enforce the fine print: when a creature breaks the stated price of a written contract you hold or witnessed, you may spend a reaction and 2 CE to call in the debt — it makes a Cha save, becoming Dominion-eligible until the end of its next turn on a failure."}, {"name": "Lower Yourself", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 6", "text": "Bonus action, 2 CE: a creature she damaged this turn saves or is Frightened of her — and fear is eligibility. She manufactures the very conditions her leash requires. Bonus action, 2 CE: one creature you damaged this turn makes Wis save; failure is Frightened of you until end next turn and therefore becomes Dominion-eligible."}, {"name": "Remote Handler", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Eyes and Ears", "text": "Her commands no longer need her voice: she may issue simple orders telepathically to Dominated creatures within a mile. The chain of command, at the speed of thought. You may issue simple commands telepathically to Dominated creatures within 1 mile."}], "e101": [{"name": "Vrrrm Vrrrm", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Rip Cord", "text": "He revs the saws as they manifest: spending 2 Blood tokens turns the activation itself into an attack — each creature within 5 ft saves or takes a Devour Die. The entrance is the attack. You rev the chainsaws as you manifest them: when you activate Rip Cord, you may spend 2 Blood tokens to make the manifestation itself an attack — each creature within 5 ft makes a Dex save, taking one Devour Die slashing on a failure."}, {"name": "Blood Lash", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Blood-Fed Engine", "text": "Bonus action, 3 Blood tokens: pressurized blood whips extend his chainsaws to 10-ft reach until end of turn. Hunger has range. As a bonus action, spend 3 Blood tokens to extend your chainsaws with whips of pressurized blood: your chainsaw attacks gain 10-ft reach until the end of your turn."}, {"name": "Door to Hell", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 9", "text": "When he reduces a cursed spirit to 0 HP, he learns whether it has manifested elsewhere or can reincarnate under campaign lore. The devourer keeps a map of what he has eaten. When you reduce a cursed spirit to 0 HP, learn whether it has previously manifested elsewhere or can reincarnate under campaign lore."}, {"name": "Save Me, Chainsaw Man", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Hero of Hell", "text": "Reaction when an ally within 60 ft drops to 0 HP: he moves up to his speed toward them and makes one chainsaw attack against an adjacent creature. The hero arrives the way heroes do — loudly, and through the enemy. Reaction when an ally within 60 ft drops to 0 HP: move up to speed toward them and make one chainsaw attack against a creature adjacent to them."}], "e102": [{"name": "Ki Savant", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ki Read", "text": "While Ki Read is active, a bonus action focuses on one sensed creature: he learns whether it concentrates on a technique, with advantage on his first Black Hole contest against its effects this round. Reading precedes erasing. While Ki Read is active, you may spend a bonus action to focus on one creature you sense: you learn whether it is concentrating on a technique or effect, and you have advantage on the first Black Hole contest against its effects this round."}, {"name": "Dark Cloaked Blade", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 3", "text": "His weapon counts as magical and cursed while the technique is available, and may deal necrotic instead of its normal physical type. The blade is no longer merely steel with intentions. Your weapon counts as magical/cursed while technique is available and may deal necrotic instead of its normal physical type."}, {"name": "Black Hole Mastery", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Black Hole", "text": "He learns to catch rather than merely erase: when Black Hole consumes a projectile or line, a reaction and 2 CE holds it for one round, then releases it as a 60-ft line with its original dice. What he swallows, he may return. You have learned to catch rather than merely erase: when Black Hole consumes a projectile or line effect, you may spend a reaction and 2 CE to hold it for one round, then release it as a 60-ft line using its original damage dice (Dex save for half)."}, {"name": "Surpass Your Limits", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 11", "text": "At 0 HP, before falling, he may spend all remaining CE (minimum 5) to release one final Dimension Slash along his facing — then fall. The last thing he ever does is the truest thing he knows. When you are reduced to 0 HP, before falling you may spend all remaining CE (minimum 5) to release one final Dimension Slash along your facing; resolve the attack, then fall unconscious."}], "e103": [{"name": "Second Hand", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Time Theft", "text": "He lends his hoard: reaction and 2 TU when an ally within 30 ft fails a save — a borrowed moment, a reroll, the better result kept. Once per round. Stolen seconds make excellent gifts. You lend stolen seconds to others: when an ally within 30 ft fails a saving throw, you may spend a reaction and 2 TU to grant them a borrowed moment — they reroll the save and take the better result. Once per round."}, {"name": "Precise Stasis", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Stasis Sphere", "text": "His frozen may perceive and speak while still unable to move or act. Even the prison has visiting hours. You may allow a frozen target to perceive/speak while still preventing movement/actions."}, {"name": "Borrowed Second", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 9", "text": "Reaction, 3 TU: an ally within 30 ft gains +10 ft movement and one object interaction, immediately. He loans time the way a banker loans coin — briefly, and at exactly the right moment. Reaction, spend 3 TU to grant an ally within 30 ft +10 ft movement and one object interaction immediately."}, {"name": "Grand Clock", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 15", "text": "His rewind turns surgical: when using Chrono Anastasis, 2 TU per creature excludes up to PB creatures from the rewind — they keep current HP, positions, and conditions. The clockmaker decides who the hands spare. Your mastery of the rewind is surgical: when you use Chrono Anastasis, you may spend 2 TU per creature to exclude up to PB creatures from the rewind — they keep their current HP, positions, and conditions."}], "e104": [{"name": "Anti-Magic Swordsman", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Demon-Slayer", "text": "His sword drinks curses aimed at others: reaction when an ally within 5 ft saves against an external CE effect — they use his save result instead. The shield is a greatsword held flat. Your sword drinks curses aimed at others: when an ally within 5 ft must save against an external CE effect, you may use your reaction to interpose your anti-cursed sword — they use your save result in place of their own."}, {"name": "Bull Thrust", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Black Form", "text": "Dash at least 20 ft in a straight line, and a bonus action drives the anti-cursed sword into a creature moved adjacent to during the dash — one melee attack, momentum carrying the cut. The charge is the technique; the sword merely attends. When you take the Dash action and move at least 20 feet in a straight line, you can use a bonus action to drive your anti-cursed sword into a creature you move adjacent to during the dash, making a single melee attack with the sword as the charge’s momentum carries the cut."}, {"name": "Sword Flight", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Demon-Dweller", "text": "He rides the Demon-Slayer or Dweller — fly speed equal to walking while Black Form is active. The void, it turns out, is a perfectly good vehicle. Ride Demon-Slayer/Dweller for fly speed equal walking while Black Form is active."}, {"name": "Liebe's Partner", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Devil Union", "text": "When Devil Union ends, the departing devil’s anti-magic discharges as a parting gift: reaction, end one ongoing CE effect on each hostile within 30 ft — as Demon-Destroyer, with no check required. The devil leaves the room the way it entered it: unmaking things. When Devil Union ends, the departing devil's anti-magic discharges as a parting gift: as a reaction, you may end one ongoing CE effect on each hostile creature within 30 ft (as Demon-Destroyer, no check required)."}], "e105": [{"name": "Dustproof", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Decay", "text": "His Decay recognizes its maker: immune to his own Decay damage, and his ruined terrain is never difficult terrain for him. When triggering Awakening or Deika Collapse, he may ride the crumble as part of the same action, moving up to his speed across it — sinking through his own ruin like a ship through its own wake. Your Decay recognizes its maker: you are immune to your own Decay damage, and ruined terrain you create is never difficult terrain for you. When you trigger Awakening or Deika Collapse, you may ride the crumble as part of the same action, moving up to your speed across the affected area — sinking through cracked ground and erupting at its edge. This movement does not provoke opportunity attacks from creatures standing in the decay."}, {"name": "Chain Reaction", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 9", "text": "A creature reduced to 0 by Decay automatically spreads 1 Mark to all creatures touching it. Death, too, is a surface. A creature reduced to 0 by Decay automatically spreads 1 Mark to all creatures touching it."}, {"name": "Selective Hand", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 6", "text": "He can make ordinary hand contact without accidental Decay, even under stress — with advantage on saves against effects that would force the technique to trigger. The hand learns the difference between touching and unmaking. You can make ordinary hand contact without accidental Decay even under stress; advantage on saves against effects that would force your technique to trigger."}, {"name": "Ruined City", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Awakening", "text": "He shapes the ruin as he makes it: when using Awakening, 1 CE raises a 10-ft section of debris into a 5-ft rubble rampart (half cover) or collapses it into a 10-ft pit (climb to escape). Destruction, itemized. You shape the ruin as you make it: when you use Awakening, you may spend 1 CE to raise one 10-ft section of debris into a 5-ft-high rubble rampart (half cover) or collapse it into a 10-ft-deep pit (climb check to escape)."}], "e106": [{"name": "Surgeon's Hand", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Reconstruction", "text": "His repairs rebuild more than flesh: when healing with Overhaul, 1 AP also ends one poison or disease — the affliction disassembled outright. The surgeon removes the illness the way he removes a splinter: by taking it apart. Your repairs rebuild more than flesh: when you heal a creature with Overhaul, you may spend 1 AP to also end one poison or disease affecting them, disassembling the affliction outright."}, {"name": "Living Architecture", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ground Spikes", "text": "His structures wake at his command: when creating terrain with Ground Spikes or Terrain Dominion, 1 CE animates one 10-ft section for a minute — 20 ft per round under his bonus-action command, one slam attack at his CE bonus for 2 Overhaul Dice. The building has opinions now. Your structures wake at your command: when you create terrain with Ground Spikes or Terrain Dominion, you may spend 1 CE to animate one 10-ft section for 1 minute — it moves 20 ft per round under your bonus-action command and may make one slam attack (+CE attack bonus, 2 Overhaul Dice bludgeoning)."}, {"name": "Clean Fusion", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Fusion", "text": "He fuses cleanly under pressure: when he or a willing creature within 5 ft takes damage, a reaction and 1 AP begins Fusion immediately — completing at the start of his next turn, the triggering damage divided evenly between the two. Normal costs apply on completion. Pain, shared before the joining. You fuse cleanly under pressure: when you or a willing creature within 5 ft takes damage, you may spend a reaction and 1 AP to begin Fusion immediately; it completes at the start of your next turn, and the triggering damage is divided evenly between you. Normal costs apply when it completes."}, {"name": "Plague Mask", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 9", "text": "He overhauls the very air: action, 1 AP, a 15-ft cube around him for a minute — inhaled poisons and diseases disassembled on contact, advantage on saves against airborne hazards. The surgeon’s mask is the atmosphere itself. You overhaul the very air: as an action, spend 1 AP to disassemble contaminants in a 15-ft cube around you for 1 minute — inhaled poisons and diseases are destroyed on contact, and creatures in the cube have advantage on saves against airborne hazards."}], "e107": [{"name": "Baskerville", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Black Hound", "text": "His hound hunts with a body now: Black Hound may grapple creatures up to Large with his CE attack bonus — and while it holds a victim, 1 soul as a bonus action drags them 15 ft. The court’s first citizen learns the second trade. Your hound hunts with a body now: Black Hound may grapple creatures up to Large using your CE attack bonus for the grapple check, and while it holds a victim you may spend 1 soul as a bonus action to have it drag them 15 ft."}, {"name": "Casull & Jackal", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 3", "text": "Paired cursed firearms: 60/240-ft ranged attacks using Dex or CE ability, qualifying for technique riders — but not for automatic soul consumption. Even the king’s guns observe the court’s dining rules. Gain paired cursed firearms; ranged attacks 60/240 ft use Dex or CE ability and qualify for technique riders, but not for automatic soul consumption."}, {"name": "No Life King", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Extra Life", "text": "They watched him refuse to die: when Extra Life triggers, 1 additional soul lets the moment land — each hostile within 10 ft that witnessed it saves or is Frightened of him until the end of his next turn. Death refused publicly is its own kind of conquest. They watched you refuse to die: when Extra Life triggers, you may spend 1 additional soul to let the moment land — each hostile within 10 ft that witnessed it makes a Wis save, becoming Frightened of you until the end of your next turn on a failure."}, {"name": "Named Dead", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Named Familiar", "text": "The named dead still talk: 10 minutes communing with one stored Elite or Named soul — three questions about its life, answered truthfully for what it knew, or advantage on one History, Arcana, or Insight check drawing on its expertise. The court’s archives are open to its king. The named dead still talk: you may spend 10 minutes communing with one stored Elite/Named soul, asking three questions about its life (answered truthfully for what it knew) or gaining advantage on one History, Arcana, or Insight check drawing on its expertise."}], "e108": [{"name": "Crimson Bullet", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Parts Bullet", "text": "He has learned to plant rather than merely fire: a Parts Bullet may be fired into an unattended object or surface within 60 ft without damaging it — embedded for a minute, detonated as a bonus action: creatures within 10 ft save or take 3 Undead Dice. The finger is a mine now. You have learned to plant rather than merely fire: you may fire a Parts Bullet into an unattended object or surface within 60 ft without damaging it; the embedded part remains for 1 minute, and as a bonus action you may detonate it — creatures within 10 ft make a Dex save, taking 3 Undead Dice slashing on a failure."}, {"name": "Bloody Arts", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Blood Propulsion", "text": "His propulsion carries more than him: when he Blood Propels, one willing creature he touches comes along (no provoking) — or one grappled creature is dragged; a carried willing creature may make one melee attack at any point during the movement. Even his commute is a combat maneuver. Your propulsion carries more than you: when you Blood Propel, you may bring one willing creature you touch along (it does not provoke), or drag one creature you are grappling. A carried willing creature may make one melee attack at any point during the movement."}, {"name": "Sword in the Body", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Repair Boost", "text": "He draws or stores one one-handed weapon inside his regenerating body — and cannot be disarmed of it while conscious. The sheath is himself. The quickdraw is surgery. Draw/store one one-handed weapon inside your regenerating body; cannot be disarmed of it while conscious."}, {"name": "Never Stop", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 15", "text": "Once per short rest, when Restrained, Paralyzed, or Stunned: spend 10 Repair to immediately repeat the relevant save. Conditions are suggestions. He declines most of them. Once/short rest when Restrained, Paralyzed, or Stunned, spend 10 Repair to repeat the relevant save immediately."}], "e109": [{"name": "Perfect Sheathe", "prereq": "", "text": "When he reduces a hostile to 0 HP, 2 Concentration as a reaction: sheathe Yamato in one perfect motion — each hostile within 10 ft that witnessed it saves or is Frightened of him until the end of his next turn. The kill is the technique. The sheathe is the signature. When you reduce a hostile creature to 0 HP, you may spend 2 Concentration as a reaction to sheathe Yamato in one perfect motion: each hostile within 10 ft that witnessed it makes a Wis save, becoming Frightened of you until the end of your next turn on a failure."}, {"name": "Rapid Slash", "prereq": "", "text": "After using Trick, his first Yamato attack this turn may cleave into a second creature within 10 ft of the first — damage dice split evenly, one attack roll against each. Teleportation, with a follow-through. After using Trick, your first Yamato attack this turn may cleave into a second creature within 10 ft of the first: split the attack's damage dice evenly between them, rolling one attack roll against each."}, {"name": "Summoned Sword Master", "prereq": "", "text": "2 unspent Mirage Blades as a bonus action weave a spinning guard: until his next turn, ranged attacks against him have disadvantage and he gains +2 AC against them. The swords that attack learn, on command, to defend. You may spend 2 unspent Mirage Blades as a bonus action to weave them into a spinning guard: until the start of your next turn, ranged attacks against you have disadvantage and you gain +2 AC against them."}, {"name": "Dark Slayer", "prereq": "", "text": "While at 10 Concentration, when targeted by an attack: reaction, 1 CE, Trick up to 30 ft before it resolves — the attack misses if it can no longer reach him; and if he reappears within 10 ft of the attacker, one Yamato attack as part of the same motion. The perfect defense is to have been somewhere else, rudely. While you are at 10 Concentration, when you are targeted by an attack you may use your reaction to spend 1 CE and Trick up to 30 ft before the attack resolves; the attack misses if it can no longer reach you. If you reappear within 10 ft of the attacker, you may make one Yamato attack against them as part of the same reaction."}], "e110": [{"name": "Enemy Step", "prereq": "", "text": "When he hits a creature his size or larger with a melee attack, his reaction springboards off them — up to 20 ft in any direction without provoking, the creature saving or knocked prone by the push-off. The enemy is terrain. Rude, load-bearing terrain. When you hit a creature your size or larger with a melee attack, you may use your reaction to springboard off them: leap up to 20 ft in any direction without provoking, and the creature makes a Str save or is knocked prone by the push-off."}, {"name": "Royal Guard Savant", "prereq": "", "text": "He guards others as himself: reaction when an ally within 10 ft takes damage — spend 2 Guard to interpose, taking the damage instead, reduced by his Royalguard reduction. Chivalry, itemized. You guard others as yourself: as a reaction when an ally within 10 ft takes damage, you may spend 2 Guard to interpose — you take the damage instead, reduced by your Royalguard reduction (1d10 + level)."}, {"name": "Weapon Freak", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per turn, when he hits with a bound Devil Arm, he may draw a second bound Devil Arm and attack with it as a bonus action — provided it is a different named attack than his previous qualifying action, still advancing Style. The arsenal has no bottom. He checked. Once per turn, when you hit with a bound Devil Arm, you may draw a second bound Devil Arm and make one attack with it as a bonus action, provided it is a different named attack than your previous qualifying action (it still advances Style)."}, {"name": "Jackpot", "prereq": "", "text": "On a natural 20 with a ranged attack, he may call Jackpot: instead of critical damage, a celebratory spread — up to two other creatures within 15 ft of the target take half the attack’s damage (Dex save for half). The house always wins. He is the house. When you roll a natural 20 on a ranged attack, you may call Jackpot: instead of rolling critical damage, fire a celebratory spread — up to two other creatures within 15 ft of the target take half the attack's damage (Dex save for half)."}], "e111": [{"name": "Long Blade", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per turn, a missed Masamune swing extends into a second creature within 15 ft of the first — a new attack roll at disadvantage. The blade is long enough to be wrong twice. Once per turn, when you miss with Masamune, you may extend the swing into a second creature within 15 ft of the first, making a new attack roll at disadvantage."}, {"name": "Chosen by Jenova", "prereq": "", "text": "When subjected to disease, poison, or transformation: a reaction lets Jenova’s cells devour it — he is unaffected, and learns the effect’s nature and source. The cells do not defend him. They dine. When you would be subjected to a disease, poison, or transformation effect, you may spend a reaction to let Jenova's cells devour it: you are unaffected, and you learn the effect's nature and source."}, {"name": "Peerless SOLDIER", "prereq": "", "text": "When using Octaslash, up to 10 ft of movement between each attack without provoking — each slash may target a different creature, not counting against his speed. A path carved through a scattered formation in a single action. The SOLDIER does not reposition. He edits the formation. When you use Octaslash, you may move up to 10 ft between each attack without provoking opportunity attacks, and each slash may target a different creature. This movement does not count against your speed for the turn, letting you carve a path through a scattered formation in a single action."}, {"name": "Black Materia", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per long rest, the Supernova charge cannot be interrupted by ordinary damage. The ritual, insured. Supernova charge cannot be interrupted by ordinary damage once/long rest."}], "e112": [{"name": "Moon of Mahaa-Kalaa", "prereq": "", "text": "When a creature misses her with a melee attack: reaction and 1 Tempo — parry the blow into another creature within 5 ft, rerolling the attack against it. The miss was hers. The hit is negotiable. When a creature misses you with a melee attack, you may spend your reaction and 1 Tempo to parry the blow into another creature within 5 ft of you: reroll the attack against that creature."}, {"name": "Bat Within", "prereq": "", "text": "When damaged by an effect she could see: 1 Tempo as a reaction — burst into a swarm of bats, half damage, immediately move 15 ft without provoking, reforming at the destination. The body declines to be where the damage was. When you take damage from an effect you could see, you may spend 1 Tempo as a reaction to burst into a swarm of bats: you take half damage and immediately move 15 ft without provoking, reforming at the destination."}, {"name": "Accessory Witch", "prereq": "", "text": "Her accessories drink her Witch Time: once per turn, when triggering Witch Time, she may also activate one accessory’s effect as part of the same reaction, without its normal action. The dance has jewelry. The jewelry works. Your accessories drink your Witch Time: once per turn, when you trigger Witch Time, you may also activate one accessory's effect as part of the same reaction without spending its normal action."}, {"name": "Pure Platinum", "prereq": "", "text": "Her debut is flawless: the first time each combat she triggers Witch Time, she may extend its effects to one additional creature within 30 ft — speed 0, no reactions — until the end of her next turn. Perfection, shared selectively. Your debut is flawless: the first time each combat you trigger Witch Time, you may extend its effects to one additional creature within 30 ft (speed 0, no reactions) until the end of your next turn."}], "e113": [{"name": "Conductive Arc", "prereq": "", "text": "He aims at the metal, not the man. The arc does the aiming afterward — a lesson in who really chooses the target. You may fire Lightning Bolt at an unattended metal object or conductive surface within range instead of a creature: the charge arcs outward — each creature within 10 ft of the point makes a Dex save, taking the bolt's damage on a failure."}, {"name": "Polarity Shift", "prereq": "", "text": "He does not catch the arrow; he persuades it to be disloyal. One Charge as a reaction, and another man's aim becomes his instrument. When a creature within 30 ft makes a ranged weapon attack, you may spend 1 Charge as a reaction to bend the projectile's path: redirect the attack to a different creature within 15 ft of the original target, making a new attack roll."}, {"name": "Thunder Drop", "prereq": "", "text": "The fall is the attack. I have watched him turn twenty feet of gravity into a detonation — the landing itself filed as a weapon. When you fall at least 20 ft, you may spend 1 Charge as a reaction just before landing: you take no falling damage, and the grounded impact erupts — each creature within 10 ft of where you land makes a Dexterity save, taking 2d8 lightning damage on a failure. Structures and unattended metal objects in the burst take double dice."}, {"name": "Karmic Overload", "prereq": "", "text": "The vault emptied at once. It is the gambler's last hand: everything discharged, everything at zero, and the field rewritten in a single gesture. You may discharge all remaining Charge at once (minimum 6) as an action: each creature within 20 ft makes a Con save, taking 1d8 lightning per 2 Charge discharged on a failure (half on success); you are left at 0 Charge."}], "e114": [{"name": "Smoke & Mirrors", "prereq": "", "text": "He exits through himself. The departed space keeps a cloud as his alibi, and the first strike from inside it is struck from nowhere. When you use Smoke Dash, you may leave a 10-ft-radius cloud of thick smoke in the space you departed: it heavily obscures the area until the start of your next turn. The first attack you make before the cloud fades has advantage if its target cannot see you."}, {"name": "Neon Runner", "prereq": "", "text": "Light does not ask permission. When he dashes as neon, the field itself becomes a corridor — and the corridor burns whoever stands in it. You run through enemies as light: when you Neon Dash, you may pass through hostile creatures' spaces — each must make a Dex save or take 2d8 radiant damage."}, {"name": "Digital Angel", "prereq": "", "text": "The wings remember they were once blades. Two CE, and the broadcast grows teeth that do not ground him. When you activate Video flight, you may spend 2 CE to hard-light the wings into blades for the round: you may make one Video Blade attack at any point during the movement, and attacking does not end the flight early."}, {"name": "Concrete Skin", "prereq": "", "text": "He petrifies the wound shut — concrete's oldest lesson: the best response to being broken is to become the break. When you take bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage, you may spend 1 CE as a reaction to petrify the wound shut: reduce the damage by 1d10 + your CE modifier, and you cannot be moved against your will until the start of your next turn."}], "e115": [{"name": "Parkour Predator", "prereq": "", "text": "The city is a second meal. He climbs without hands and leaps from the climb — the predator reads architecture the way the scholar reads a page. You gain a climb speed equal to your walking speed, and your claws let you climb sheer surfaces without needing free hands. When you take the Dash action, your long jump distance is doubled, and you may launch a jump directly out of a climb without landing first."}, {"name": "Patsy", "prereq": "", "text": "He consumes intentions along with flesh. Five Biomass to reproduce a memory under questioning — the dead testify for him now. You consume intentions along with flesh: when you Consume a creature, you learn one short-term goal or plan it held (GM's discretion), and you may spend 5 Biomass to perfectly reproduce one specific memory under questioning for 10 minutes."}, {"name": "Adaptive Biomass", "prereq": "", "text": "His body eats what hurts it. Five Biomass to learn the wound, and the next strike of that kind feeds him instead of felling him. Your body eats what hurts it: when you take damage of a type, you may spend 5 Biomass as a reaction to analyze it — the next time you take that damage type this combat, you may convert up to 10 of it into Biomass instead of losing HP."}, {"name": "Pack Leader", "prereq": "", "text": "He tears loose a piece of himself and it learns to hunt. Fifteen Biomass for a hound with his proficiency in its teeth — the pack is the man, divided. As an action, spend 15 Biomass to tear free a piece of yourself that grows into an infected hound: use the wolf stat block, but it has 1 HP and adds your PB to its attack and damage rolls. It obeys your commands and acts immediately after you in initiative; after 10 minutes, or when reduced to 0 HP, it collapses into 5 Biomass you may reabsorb by touching it."}], "e116": [{"name": "Let Me Solo", "prereq": "", "text": "This boss has been read before. One minute of study — or an action and a hard Insight — and the familiar foe keeps one fewer secret. You know this boss: when facing a boss-tier creature you have fought before, you may spend 1 minute studying its patterns before combat (or an action and a DC 15 Insight check during it) to learn one of its resistances, immunities, or legendary actions."}, {"name": "Potent Ash", "prereq": "", "text": "One weapon, two arts. One extra CE to bind the second, and the blade changes its mind as a bonus action. You layer arts on a single weapon: when you bind an Ash of War, you may bind a second art to the same weapon for 1 extra CE, switching between them as a bonus action."}, {"name": "Rune Arc", "prereq": "", "text": "The seal is lent away: suppress the Great Rune's own benefit for a minute so allies within thirty feet may wear it. The archive shares what it cannot keep twice. You project the rune outward: you may suppress your Great Rune's passive benefit for 1 minute to instead grant it to allies within 30 ft — they gain the benefit while you lose it."}, {"name": "Thy Strength Befits a Crown", "prereq": "", "text": "Victories crystallize faster now. Slay a boss-tier foe personally and the Remembrance is taken at once — no waiting for the post-combat quiet. Your victories crystallize faster now: when you personally reduce a boss-tier creature to 0 HP, you may immediately attempt to crystallize a Remembrance from it, spending the usual costs, without waiting for post-combat downtime."}], "e117": [{"name": "Spider-Sense Echo", "prereq": "", "text": "The blind spots are someone else's job now. No advantage from flanking or pack tactics, and a hidden striker's direction is reported after the first blow. The symbiote watches your blind spots: attackers gain no advantage against you from flanking or pack tactics, and when a hidden creature attacks you, you learn its direction immediately after the attack resolves."}, {"name": "Living Parachute", "prereq": "", "text": "The fall is outsourced. A reaction, and web-wings catch what gravity dropped — sixty feet of steering for every ten descended, landed on his feet. When you begin to fall, you may use your reaction to have the symbiote snap out web-wings: you take no falling damage and glide instead, moving up to 60 ft horizontally for every 10 ft you descend, and you land on your feet. You may steer around obstacles while gliding but cannot gain altitude."}, {"name": "Eat Your Brains", "prereq": "", "text": "He tastes the mind with the flesh. One CE on a grappled bite, and the enemy's knowledge becomes his — or at least his next question does. You taste memories with the flesh: when you damage a grappled creature with a bite, you may spend 1 CE to learn one fact it knows (GM's discretion) or gain advantage on your next Insight check against it."}, {"name": "Anti-Sonic Conditioning", "prereq": "", "text": "He separates on his own terms. Once per long rest, when sonics would tear them apart, he detaches one tendril-swarm by choice — half the Echo's dice, acting alone for a minute. A retreat filed as a maneuver. You separate on your own terms: once per long rest, when sonic damage would forcibly separate you, you may instead partially detach on purpose — one tendril swarm (half the King in Black Echo swarm's dice) acts independently for 1 minute while you remain bonded."}], "e118": [{"name": "Blood Trail", "prereq": "", "text": "Wound the living and he tastes the blood — for an hour, he knows its direction to the mile, and his senses sharpen near it. One hunt at a time: wound another, and the first trail fades. The predator's courtesy: he savors his prey singly. When you damage a living creature with a Red Weapon, you taste its blood: for the next hour you unerringly know its direction while it is within 1 mile of you, and you have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to detect it while it is within 60 ft. The trail ends early if you wound another creature — you can only savor one hunt at a time."}, {"name": "Wall of Teeth", "prereq": "", "text": "Strike him in melee and the symbiote answers — the limb caught in a red maw, held fast unless torn free. The counter that bites back: every attack on him risks becoming his grip. You catch what strikes you: when a creature hits you with a melee attack, you may spend your reaction to snare the limb in the symbiote's maw — it makes a Str save or is grappled by you (escape DC = technique DC)."}, {"name": "Red Rain", "prereq": "", "text": "A spray of shards for a coin — two targets, thirty feet, the volley's smaller cousin. The appetite learns to share its attention. As an action, spend 1 CE to hurl a spray of symbiote shards at up to two creatures within 30 ft: make a ranged technique attack against each, dealing 1d8 piercing damage on a hit. This counts as your Shard Volley use for the turn."}, {"name": "Born Killer", "prereq": "", "text": "He marks the dying: forgo the wound's damage, and leave instead a bleeding promise — the next blow against the marked falls with advantage. The patient hunter: sometimes the kindest cut is the one that only points. You mark the dying: once per turn, when you hit a creature below half HP with a Red Weapon, you may forgo the damage to leave a bleeding wound instead — the next attack against it before the end of your next turn has advantage."}], "e119": [{"name": "Invisible Objects", "prereq": "", "text": "She veils what she carries, and for one more CE, what she touches. The equipment follows the same rule as the woman: seen only when it strikes. When you activate Invisibility, objects you wear and carry share it — they flicker visible for a round when you attack, exactly as you do. Additionally, you may spend 1 extra CE to veil one unattended object or 10-ft surface you touch; it remains invisible for the full 10 minutes even if your own invisibility ends early, letting you hide a door, a trap, or an ally's hiding spot."}, {"name": "Hard-Light Step", "prereq": "", "text": "Gravity is merely a suggestion. When shoved, tripped, or falling, a reaction and one CE buy a foothold out of nothing — ten feet, mid-air if needed, without asking permission. When you are shoved, knocked prone, or begin to fall, you may use your reaction and spend 1 CE to flash-form a hard-light foothold beneath you: move up to 10 ft to an unoccupied space, including mid-air, without provoking opportunity attacks. If you were falling, you land safely on the platform instead, and it supports your weight until the start of your next turn."}, {"name": "Fine Control", "prereq": "", "text": "Her constructs grow fingers. Platforms and domes manipulate like spectral hands — a bonus action's worth of Sleight at her attack bonus. Fortifications that pick pockets. Your force constructs gain fine articulation: any platform, bubble, wall, or dome you create can manipulate objects like a spectral hand. As a bonus action you may have a construct make a Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check using your CE attack bonus, lift up to 10 lb, or operate a simple mechanism within 60 ft — picking a lock, turning a key, or pulling a lever from across the room."}, {"name": "Mother's Shield", "prereq": "", "text": "The screen does two jobs now: it takes the hit and moves the ally ten feet to safety in the same reaction. Protection, filed as logistics. when you intercept an attack targeting an ally with Force Screen, you may also slide the ally up to 10 ft to unoccupied ground as part of the same reaction."}], "e120": [{"name": "Hotshot", "prereq": "", "text": "At Heat five the bolt narrows to a lance: one target at one hundred twenty feet, cover halved in relevance. Precision is the flame's rare courtesy. at Heat 5+, your fire bolt can be fired as a focused lance: one creature within 120 ft, ignoring half and three-quarters cover. This uses your action and deals normal fire bolt damage."}, {"name": "Skywriter", "prereq": "", "text": "He signs the sky. A bonus action's worth of flame-calligraphy — messages legible a mile away by night — burning for a minute. Propaganda as a technique. You shape flame and smoke with photographic precision. As a bonus action, you may write a message, sketch a map, or conjure an image in the air — legible up to 1 mile away at night or 300 ft by day — that burns for 1 minute. You may also sculpt a flame-duplicate of yourself that lasts until the start of your next turn: the first attack made against you while it burns has disadvantage, as the attacker strikes the wrong target."}, {"name": "Thermal Updraft", "prereq": "", "text": "He carries a passenger in his own weather. The updraft shields the guest with his resistance and spares them his aura — fire that has learned manners. While flying with Jet Flight, you may carry one willing creature of your size or smaller without reducing your speed, cradling them in a heat-shielded updraft that grants them your fire resistance for the ride. Your fiery aura does not harm your passenger, and you may release them as a free action — if released within 30 ft of the ground, they drift down safely and land on their feet."}, {"name": "Flame Cage", "prereq": "", "text": "Two CE for a ten-foot ring of white flame, a minute of Focus: enter or linger and pay three dice. He does not chase. He files the perimeter. As an action for 2 CE, you raise a 10-ft-radius, 10-ft-tall ring of white-hot flame that lasts 1 minute (Focus). Any creature that enters the ring's wall or ends its turn there takes 3d8 fire damage, or half on a successful Dexterity save. The cage restrains through threat as much as flame: enemies inside must choose between burning through the wall or staying trapped."}], "e121": [{"name": "Lucky Hex", "prereq": "", "text": "She spends another's misfortune: when a hostile rolls a natural one within sixty feet, a reaction and a Chaos Die move the failure to a target of her choosing. Bad luck is fungible. I have begun to suspect that luck, near her, is not random but merely unassigned. once per short rest, when a hostile within 60 ft rolls a natural 1, you may use your reaction to spend one Chaos Die and redirect the failed roll onto a different target of your choice within range."}, {"name": "Chaos Vision", "prereq": "", "text": "She reads the residue: an action to learn what reality-altering or illusion effects the last hour has left within sixty feet. The past, near her, leaves fingerprints. I have stopped assuming my own past is clean. The weaver inspects the weave. as an action, you can read probability residue: learn what reality-altering or illusion effects have occurred within 60 ft in the last hour."}, {"name": "Red Thread", "prereq": "", "text": "For one more CE, the Hex threads through probability itself — striking a target she cannot see, so long as she knows its exact place within sixty feet. Cover is a rumor she declines to hear. I have started standing very still and thinking very precisely about where I am. when you use Hex, you may spend 1 additional CE to thread it through probability itself, targeting a creature you cannot see as long as you know its exact location within 60 ft."}, {"name": "What Hex?", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per long rest, a Surge that would have happened does not: a reaction grounds it in an unattended object, which warps harmlessly and spends the Surge. The lightning rod is a vase. She can decline even her own chaos. I cannot decide whether that reassures me or terrifies me, so I have decided to be both. once per long rest, when a Chaos Surge would trigger, you may use your reaction to ground it in an unattended object within 30 ft instead: the object warps harmlessly (changes color, floats briefly) and the Surge is spent."}, {"name": "Nexus Being", "prereq": "", "text": "She pins the unpinned: a reaction and a Chaos Die to hold a creature's probability in place against teleport or displacement, contested if opposed. as a reaction when a creature within 30 ft would be teleported or forcibly displaced by a supernatural effect, you may spend 1 Chaos Die to pin its probability in place (contested against the effect's DC if opposed)."}, {"name": "Witch's Grief", "prereq": "", "text": "Below a quarter of her health, reality flinches with her: hostiles within thirty feet save or roll their next d20 twice and take the worse. Grief, weaponized at range. once per short rest, when you drop below 25% of your maximum HP, reality shudders: each hostile within 30 ft must succeed on a Wisdom save or roll its next attack, check, or save twice and take the worse."}], "e122": [{"name": "Hulk Catch", "prereq": "", "text": "He treats incoming fire as a delivery. A reaction and a contested Athletics check, and the ranged attack is caught — the projectile filed as his property. When a ranged weapon or thrown-object attack hits you or an ally within 10 feet, you may use your reaction to snatch it out of the air: make a Strength (Athletics) check against the attack's total. On a success the attack is negated, and if the projectile is physical you may immediately hurl it back as part of the same reaction — make a ranged attack against a creature within 60 feet, dealing 3d10 + your Strength modifier bludgeoning damage on a hit. You need a free hand, and you cannot catch energy beams, sure-hits, or anything larger than Large."}, {"name": "Collateral Bulwark", "prereq": "", "text": "At Rage five, a bonus action tears the terrain into cover: ranged attacks at disadvantage, half cover until his next turn. The battlefield donates its architecture. at Rage 5+, as a bonus action you can tear up the terrain into an improvised bulwark: until the start of your next turn, ranged attacks against you have disadvantage and you have half cover."}, {"name": "Banner's Mind", "prereq": "", "text": "Two Rage for a minute of lucidity — the disadvantage lifted, the memory retained. The man inside the account gets a window to count it. You can force a moment of Banner-like lucidity inside the rage. As a bonus action, spend 2 Rage: for the next minute you ignore the disadvantage on Wisdom and Intelligence checks imposed by high Rage, retain full memory of what happens while transformed, and can speak in complete sentences. You may also end Hulk Out early by spending your action — your Rage falls to 0 and you revert to normal size — but your pulse needs a minute to steady, and you cannot transform again until then."}, {"name": "Green Scar", "prereq": "", "text": "At Rage five, one Rage buys a roar: hostiles within fifteen feet save or fear him until his next turn ends. The account announces its balance. at Rage 5+, as a bonus action you can spend 1 Rage to roar: creatures of your choice within 15 ft make a Wisdom save or become Frightened of you until the end of your next turn."}], "e123": [{"name": "Diplomatic Immunity", "prereq": "", "text": "The rank is the technique. Invoke Latveria formally and ten minutes of advantage on Persuasion and Intimidation follow — sovereignty, worn like armor. Doom's sovereignty is itself a technique. When you formally invoke your rank, title, or the authority of Latveria, you have advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) and Charisma (Intimidation) checks for the next 10 minutes, and creatures that recognize your authority cannot willingly target you with hostile technique effects until you or an ally acts against them. This immunity is void against beings that do not recognize mortal titles — Domains, Calamity-grade horrors, and the genuinely insane."}, {"name": "Hidden Doombot", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per long rest, the 'you' just killed was a Doombot all along — provided one was plausibly deployed. The sovereign's death is always a draft. Once per long rest, when you would be reduced to 0 HP, you may reveal that the 'you' just defeated was a Doombot all along — provided it is logically possible: you must have had a Doombot deployed this combat or an unspent Scheme slot, and no effect may have explicitly prevented the swap. You instead appear unharmed at a location of your choice within 60 feet, leaving the Doombot behind as sparking wreckage. This revelation costs no action; it was planned for long before the battle began."}, {"name": "Mystic Armor", "prereq": "", "text": "The armor learns: succeed on a save and one CE as a reaction siphons the residue into a Siphon token. Survival, filed as income. when you succeed on a save against a technique while wearing Doom Armor, you may spend 1 CE as a reaction to siphon its residue, gaining a Siphon token as if from Power Siphon."}, {"name": "DOOM Does Not Beg", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per short rest, a failed Wisdom or Charisma save becomes intelligence: he learns the source's technique and a named feature, and gains advantage on the saves against it. He does not endure attacks. He catalogues them. once per short rest, when you fail a Wisdom or Charisma save, you may use your reaction to file the attack as intelligence: you learn the source's technique and one named feature it used, and you gain advantage on saves against that source for 1 minute."}], "e124": [{"name": "Faster Than a Bullet", "prereq": "", "text": "When an ally within twenty feet is targeted, a reaction carries him up to twenty feet to their side — flying, without spending — and he may interpose. The body arrives before the bullet's paperwork. When an ally within 20 feet is targeted by an attack, you may use your reaction to move up to 20 feet to a space adjacent to them — you may fly for this movement without spending Charge. If you end the movement between the attacker and your ally, the attack targets you instead. Damage you take this way is halved while your Solar Body is active; the Man of Steel was built for exactly this."}, {"name": "Freeze Breath", "prereq": "", "text": "The breath learns winter: flash-freeze instead of push, Constitution instead of Strength — and failure leaves the target Restrained until his next turn ends. When you use Super Breath, you may flash-freeze instead of pushing: targets make a Constitution save instead of Strength. On a failure they take the breath's cold damage and are Restrained until the end of your next turn, ice sheathing their limbs; on a success they take half damage and are not restrained. The ice melts at the end of your next turn, or early if the target takes 10 or more fire damage at once."}, {"name": "Hope", "prereq": "", "text": "One Solar Charge and an action: every ally within thirty feet who can see him may reroll one Frightened save with advantage. The allowance pays out in courage. as an action for 1 Solar Charge, each ally within 30 ft who can see you may immediately attempt a new save against one Frightened effect, with advantage."}, {"name": "Sun-Drinker", "prereq": "", "text": "Fire and radiant damage become income: a reaction halves it and banks one Solar Charge, once per round. He is taxed by the sun and keeps the change. when you take fire or radiant damage, you may use your reaction to absorb it: halve the damage and gain 1 Solar Charge. Once per round."}], "e125": [{"name": "Bullets & Bracelets", "prereq": "", "text": "The negated projectile is not wasted: one Favor as a reaction ricochets it back at sixty feet for its original damage. The enemy's aim becomes her ammunition. when your Bracelets reduce a ranged attack's damage to 0, you may spend 1 Favor as a reaction to ricochet it: make a ranged technique attack against a creature within 60 ft, dealing the projectile's original damage on a hit."}, {"name": "Amazon Grappler", "prereq": "", "text": "The lasso'd cannot use reactions, and a bonus action drags them fifteen feet. Truth is also a leash. a creature grappled by your Lasso cannot use reactions, and you may use your bonus action to drag it up to 15 ft."}, {"name": "Princess of Peace", "prereq": "", "text": "She is an emissary, not only a blade: one full minute of formal de-escalation earns her expertise — the Lasso's spirit of truth presiding over the table. You are an emissary of Themyscira, not only its blade. If you spend one full minute formally de-escalating — speaking terms, offering quarter, letting the Lasso's spirit of truth hang over the table — you gain expertise in Charisma (Persuasion) for the duration of the negotiation, and any creature that accepts your terms must succeed on a Wisdom save to break its word to you within the next 24 hours. Rushed words gain nothing; peace takes a minute."}, {"name": "Warrior Born", "prereq": "", "text": "The weapon is an oath, not an object: ten minutes of weapon-rites in a rest rebinds sword to spear to shield. The arsenal is a single vow in different clothes. Your divine weapon is an oath, not an object. During a short or long rest, you may spend 10 minutes in Themysciran weapon-rites to rebind your armament: your sword becomes a spear, your spear a shield, your shield a sword — carrying the same divine enchantment, damage die, and Favor interactions. You may also reshape its appearance freely each rest; the gods recognize the wielder, not the shape."}], "e126": [{"name": "Creative Mind", "prereq": "", "text": "His constructs are never single-purpose: one utility function woven free into every Complex Construct — silence, light, sealed air. The blueprint has margins, and he uses them. Your constructs are never single-purpose. When you forge a Complex Construct, you may weave one additional utility function into it at no extra Charge: silent operation, a built-in light source, a sealed airtight compartment, wheels or skids, or a fine-manipulation limb. The utility shares the construct's Integrity and duration, and cannot duplicate another feature's damage. There is always one more use for the ring."}, {"name": "Ring Slinging", "prereq": "", "text": "The projectile may launch from any point he can see within thirty feet — not from himself. The ring's arm is longer than his. when you create a projectile construct, you may launch it from any point within 30 ft of you that you can see, rather than from yourself."}, {"name": "Fearless", "prereq": "", "text": "An attempt to Frighten him becomes raw material: a reaction forges the fear into a ten-Integrity construct shaped like its source — and if it survives to his next turn, the fear is spent. He builds with the enemy's threats. when a creature attempts to Frighten you, you may use your reaction to forge the fear into a construct: create a 10-Integrity construct shaped like the source of the fear. If it still exists at the start of your next turn, you gain 1 Will."}, {"name": "Emergency Protocol", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per long rest, at zero HP the ring flares on instinct: automatic stabilization and temporary HP equal to remaining Will plus proficiency. The will outlives the body — literally. Your will outlives your body. Once per long rest, when you are reduced to 0 HP while wearing the ring, it flares on instinct: you are automatically stabilized and gain temporary HP equal to your remaining Will + your proficiency bonus, lasting 1 minute. You remain unconscious — but your constructs do not fall. Any you were maintaining persist for the minute, held together by refusal alone."}], "e127": [{"name": "Detective Mind", "prereq": "", "text": "Reading is half the craft: while holding surface thoughts he has advantage on Insight, and the reading arrives with understanding attached. The detective's density. Reading a mind is half of detection; understanding the reading is the other half. While you hold a creature's surface thoughts through Mind Link, you have advantage on Wisdom (Insight) checks against it, and you immediately sense when its words contradict the thoughts you are reading. Once per short rest, you may spend 1 CE as a bonus action to cross-reference: ask one yes-or-no question about the creature's current intentions, answered truthfully from what it is thinking right now."}, {"name": "Ghost", "prereq": "", "text": "While Phased, one hand may solidify as a bonus action — a single strike, a turned key — though the resistance lapses until his next turn. The elsewhere keeps one foot in the world. while Phased, you may partially solidify one hand as a bonus action to make a single unarmed strike or manipulate an object without ending Phase; attacks against you lose the B/P/S resistance until the start of your next turn."}, {"name": "Many Faces", "prereq": "", "text": "Ten minutes of observation — or a read of surface thoughts — and the Shapeshift learns voice, scent, biometrics. The skin becomes the person. Your shapeshifting is only skin-deep until you learn someone properly. If you observe a creature for at least 10 minutes — or read its surface thoughts — your Shapeshift can also mimic its voice, scent, and biometric details: retinal pattern, fingerprints, heartbeat cadence. Mundane scrutiny, guard dogs, and voice-print locks cannot tell you apart. Magical or supernatural detection still contests your technique DC, and you must have seen and heard the target to attempt this."}, {"name": "Fear of Flame", "prereq": "", "text": "When he passes a fire or fear save, a reaction scatters his density: Light for movement until his next turn ends — gaps, speed, and gone. Even the fear is filed as an exit. when you succeed on a save against fire exposure or fear, you may use your reaction to scatter your density: until the end of your next turn you count as Light density for movement (squeeze through tiny gaps, +10 speed) without spending the bonus action to switch."}], "e128": [{"name": "Parademon General", "prereq": "", "text": "Apokolips provides: three CE for a minute's hunting pack — three 1-HP parademons, one bonus action commanding all. The tyrant travels with an entourage. Apokolips provides. As an action for 3 CE, you may crack a brief Boom Tube and call a parademon hunting pack: three 1-HP parademons (AC 13, fly 40, bite 1d8+2) that last 1 minute and share one command as a bonus action. They are cowardly — if the whole pack dies, you cannot call another until you finish a short rest. Their minds are too broken to carry messages or leave the battle."}, {"name": "Stone God", "prereq": "", "text": "While the Avatar holds, the beam may originate from any point he can see within fifteen feet. The throne has many windows. I have started assuming that every window is a muzzle. while your Avatar is active, your Omega Beam may originate from any point within 15 ft of you that you can see."}, {"name": "Equation Fragment", "prereq": "", "text": "Advantage on Intimidation against the Frightened — and successful intimidation of such leaves its mark. The fragment shows in the voice. I have heard that voice. It does not raise itself. It does not need to. I have noted the exact pitch at which my own resolve begins to annotate itself. You have glimpsed a fragment of the Anti-Life Equation, and it shows in your voice. You have advantage on Charisma (Intimidation) checks against creatures Frightened of you, and when you successfully intimidate such a creature it also cannot willingly move away from you until the end of its next turn — despair roots it in place. This is a fragment, not the Equation; it compels dread, never action."}, {"name": "There Is No Escape", "prereq": "", "text": "After a missed beam, the next turn's bonus action redirects the still-burning shaft at the same target, no CE re-spent. The evidence refuses to be dismissed. after a missed Omega Beam, you may use your bonus action on your next turn to redirect the still-burning beam at the same target with a new attack roll, without spending CE again."}, {"name": "Kneel", "prereq": "", "text": "When a hostile kneels, surrenders, or falls to his hand, a reaction demands fealty of one witness within thirty feet — Wisdom or Frightened until his next turn ends. The audience participates. Defeat, in his presence, is contagious. I have begun to counsel my own forces against watching. when a hostile kneels, surrenders, or drops to 0 HP from your actions, you may use your reaction to demand fealty: one other hostile within 30 ft that sees it makes a Wisdom save or is Frightened of you until the end of your next turn."}, {"name": "Final Crisis", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per long rest, the Sanction opens as a doorway instead of a prison: he or a willing ally steps through as a bonus action, emerging within sixty feet of the condemned when it returns. The sentence commutes the jailer. once per long rest, when you use Omega Sanction you may open it as a doorway instead of a prison: you or one willing creature within 30 ft may step through as a bonus action, emerging within 60 ft of the target when it returns."}], "e129": [{"name": "Mental Fortress", "prereq": "", "text": "A probe turned back on its sender. When he succeeds on a mental save, one Thought spent as a reaction reads the surface thought of whatever targeted him — the interrogator, interrogated. when you succeed on an Intelligence or Wisdom save, you may spend 1 Thought as a reaction to reflect the probe: learn the surface thought of the creature that targeted you, as Telepath with no save."}, {"name": "False Memory", "prereq": "", "text": "An illusion wearing the shape of something the victim already believes is almost real. Built from a mind he has read within the minute, his illusions contest harder and strike first — disadvantage on their first save, disadvantage on their first look. The best lies are the ones the mark half-remembers. An illusion built from the victim's own mind is almost real. When you create an illusion — such as Perfect Illusion or Illusory Double — to deceive a creature whose surface thoughts you have read within the last minute, you have advantage on the technique contest (see Rules — Shared Resolutions) to establish the illusion, and the target has disadvantage on its first saving throw against it, and it has disadvantage on its first Investigation check to see through the illusion, which wears the shape of something it already believes. This advantage does not stack with other advantage on the same roll."}, {"name": "Architect of Thought", "prereq": "", "text": "He does not spend Thought; he mortgages it. A feature's effect can be set as a contingency, waiting up to a minute for a named trigger — one trap laid at a time, and the future springs it for him. when you spend Thought on a feature, you may set it as a contingency: the effect waits up to 1 minute for a trigger you name, then resolves. You can maintain one contingency at a time."}, {"name": "Unraveler", "prereq": "", "text": "His unmaking broadens. Unsummon may target a persistent effect or a Focus-maintained feature instead of a summon — a won contest suppresses it until the controller's next turn. Nothing his enemies maintain is safe from review. your Unsummon can target a persistent magical effect or Focus-maintained feature within 60 ft instead of a summon or construct; on a won contest it is suppressed until the end of its controller's next turn."}], "e130": [{"name": "Gravecrawler", "prereq": "", "text": "One of her dead refuses the ledger's final entry. A chosen zombie, destroyed, rises at the start of her next turn with one hit point — position and orders kept, elite rank surrendered. Death may file its paperwork; this one appeals. One of your dead refuses to stay down. Choose one Zombie under your control as your Gravecrawler: the first time it is destroyed each combat, it rises again at the start of your next turn with 1 HP, dragging itself from its own corpse. It keeps its position and your commands but loses any elite upgrades. You can maintain only one Gravecrawler at a time; you may choose another during a short rest."}, {"name": "Cruel Bargain", "prereq": "", "text": "When she sacrifices a summon she may detonate its corpse instead of taking energy or flesh — ten feet of necrotic ruin, Dexterity to halve. The technique's economy has always had a second market. when you sacrifice a summon with Dark Bargain, you may detonate its corpse instead of regaining CE or temp HP: creatures within 10 ft make a Dexterity save, taking 2d8 necrotic on a failure."}, {"name": "Necromancer's Command", "prereq": "", "text": "Her orders no longer need her voice. Commands reach her dead telepathically across a hundred and twenty feet, and a bonus action may set one to aid an ally or wrestle with Athletics. The general's reach, extended. you may issue commands to your undead telepathically within 120 ft, and command one undead to use the Help action or make a Strength (Athletics) check as your bonus action."}, {"name": "Liliana's Triumph", "prereq": "", "text": "The ledger balances itself. When one of her undead is destroyed, her reaction harvests its final moment — one more Corpse card, as if a meaningful death had occurred. The army is never smaller than the grave allows. when one of your undead is destroyed, you may use your reaction to harvest its final moment: record a Corpse card from its remains, as if a meaningful creature had died."}], "e131": [{"name": "Young Pyromancer", "prereq": "", "text": "Her big magic sheds living sparks. The first time each combat she casts a fire technique costing three or more, the excess coalesces into a one-hit-point fire elemental — a spark, not a summon, tethered within thirty feet, winking out if she goes a round without dealing fire. The forge's children are brief. Your big magic sheds sparks that live. The first time each combat you cast a fire technique costing 3 or more CE, the excess flame coalesces into a 1-HP fire elemental token (AC 13, fly 30, touch 1d6 fire) that lasts 1 minute and acts on your initiative under your bonus-action command. It cannot leave a 30-foot radius around you — it is a spark, not a summon — and it winks out if you go a full round without dealing fire damage."}, {"name": "Shared Flame", "prereq": "", "text": "She may lend her Living Flame to a willing creature as a bonus action — its next weapon attack before her next turn ends carries an extra die of fire. Even her allies may borrow the furnace, briefly. as a bonus action, you can share your Living Flame with a willing creature: the next weapon attack it makes before the end of your next turn deals an extra 1d8 fire damage."}, {"name": "Reckless Spark", "prereq": "", "text": "Pain is fuel, so she spends it. When she rolls fire damage she may take her proficiency in unpreventable damage to reroll any number of dice and keep the new results — and if the burn drops her to zero, the reroll still resolves. Her spark does not care what it burns, including her. Pain is fuel. When you roll fire damage for one of your techniques, you may take damage equal to your proficiency bonus — this cannot be reduced or redirected — to reroll any number of the dice and keep the new results. You must accept the second roll. If this damage drops you to 0 HP, the reroll still resolves; Chandra's spark does not care what it burns, including her."}, {"name": "Can't Be Extinguished", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per long rest, struck while Ember runs at five or more, her reaction erupts: the attacker takes her proficiency in fire dice, and she gains one Ember. The forge answers blows with interest. once per long rest, when you take damage while Ember is 5+, use your reaction to erupt: the attacker takes PBd8 fire, Dexterity save for half, and you gain 1 Ember."}], "e132": [{"name": "Lotus Cobra", "prereq": "", "text": "When she attunes a new Land she may read its memory — learning what crossed it within the hour. The ground keeps better records than any scout. when you attune a new Land, you may read its memory: learn what creatures have crossed it within the last hour."}, {"name": "Elvish Guidance", "prereq": "", "text": "As a bonus action, one ally standing on her Land may move ten feet without reprisal. Her territory extends its courtesies. as a bonus action, one ally standing on your Land may move up to 10 ft without provoking opportunity attacks."}, {"name": "Living Terrain", "prereq": "", "text": "As a bonus action she may coax her Land to shelter a willing creature upon it — ranged attacks against it at disadvantage until it leaves or her next turn begins. The ground, playing bodyguard. as a bonus action, you can coax your Land to shelter one willing creature standing on it: ranged attacks against that creature have disadvantage until it leaves the Land or the start of your next turn."}, {"name": "Nature's Claim", "prereq": "", "text": "Structures damaged by her land effects grow unstable: fifteen feet of difficult terrain around them until repaired. Her victories leave the field itself untrustworthy. structures damaged by your land effects become unstable: the ground in a 15-ft radius around them is difficult terrain until repaired."}], "e133": [{"name": "Mage of Zhalfir", "prereq": "", "text": "He cannot be surprised, and once per short rest he may trade initiative results with a willing ally after the roll. The treasurer arrives exactly when he means to. you cannot be surprised, and once per short rest you may swap your initiative result with one willing ally after initiative is rolled."}, {"name": "Momentary Blink", "prereq": "", "text": "As a bonus action he may phase only his senses — seeing and hearing through ten feet of solid obstruction until his turn ends. Even walls are merely scheduling conflicts. as a bonus action, you can phase only your senses for an instant: see and hear through up to 10 ft of solid obstruction until the end of your turn."}, {"name": "Untap", "prereq": "", "text": "When a delayed effect he created resolves, his reaction may echo its timing: one willing creature within thirty feet immediately uses its reaction to move half its speed. Good timing, like good coin, circulates. when a delayed effect you created resolves, you may use your reaction to echo its timing: one willing creature within 30 ft may immediately use its reaction to move up to half its speed."}, {"name": "No, Not Yet", "prereq": "", "text": "He lends his Delay to others. As a reaction when an ally within sixty feet is targeted by a one-action technique, he may contest it on their behalf at the normal cost. The treasurer's clients are well served. you can lend your Delay to others: as a reaction when an ally within 60 ft is targeted by a 1-action technique, you may contest it with Delay on their behalf (normal cost; (see Rules — Shared Resolutions))."}], "e134": [{"name": "Cruel Intellect", "prereq": "", "text": "He sifts pain for intelligence. When he deals psychic damage, one Supremacy as a bonus action reveals one of the target's named options — the interrogation conducted through the wound. when you deal psychic damage to a creature, you may spend 1 Supremacy as a bonus action to sift the pain: learn one of the target's currently available named options."}, {"name": "Dragon's Hoard", "prereq": "", "text": "When his Spellbreaker halves a technique's damage, he may capture the suppressed half — and within a minute, loose it as a fifteen-foot cone of force as a bonus action. The court's taxes are collected in full. when your Spellbreaker halves a technique's damage, you may capture the suppressed half: as a bonus action within 1 minute, release it as a 15-ft cone dealing the captured dice as force damage (Dexterity save halves)."}, {"name": "Schemer", "prereq": "", "text": "His Mind Shatter reads as it wounds — skimming surface thoughts, learning one fear or desire. A psychic echo, not a leash. He wounds and reads in the same gesture. I have interrogated prisoners. He interrogates the wound itself. I find I prefer my method, and I find that preference is fear. Your Mind Shatter does more than wound — it reads. When you deal psychic damage to a creature with Mind Shatter, you skim its surface thoughts in the same instant: for the next 10 minutes you have advantage on Charisma (Deception) and Charisma (Intimidation) checks against that creature, and you learn one fear or desire it holds. This is a psychic echo, not ongoing telepathy, and it fades if you use it against another creature."}, {"name": "The Ravager", "prereq": "", "text": "His breath may be exhaled as a lingering miasma instead of a cone — a twenty-foot cloud, the save repeated by all within. The dragon does not merely breathe. He weathers. I have weathered sieges. I have not been the weather. your breath can be exhaled as a lingering miasma instead of a cone: a 20-ft-radius cloud lasting until the start of your next turn; creatures entering or starting their turn inside make the save, taking half damage on a success."}, {"name": "Planeswalker Spark", "prereq": "", "text": "When he teleports in combat he may arrive striking — one melee attack as part of the same action. The throne lands like a siege engine. I have braced against charges. The charge that arrives from nowhere, striking, is a category I had not budgeted for. when you teleport in combat, you may arrive striking: make one melee attack against a creature within reach of your destination as part of the same action."}, {"name": "Bolas's Citadel", "prereq": "", "text": "Below half health, his stolen magic strains to be free: once per round, a used Echo may also strike one additional creature within thirty feet of the original target at half dice. Even wounded, the court collects double. while below half HP, your stolen magic strains to be free: once per round, when you use a stored Echo, you may have it also target one additional creature within 30 ft of the original target at half dice."}], "e135": [{"name": "Walking Ballista", "prereq": "", "text": "She animates with purpose. An object with a ranged function wakes as a Walking Ballista — a sixty-foot ranged strike for two dice of force, no melee, five fewer hit points for the delicate clockwork. The household has artillery now. You can animate with purpose. When you use Animate Artifact on an object with a ranged function or shape — bow, crossbow, cannon, sling, or similar — it becomes a Walking Ballista: its attack becomes a 60-foot ranged attack dealing 2d8 force, but it cannot make melee attacks and its HP is reduced by 5 for the delicate clockwork. You choose this configuration when you animate it; changing it requires re-animating."}, {"name": "Voltaic Key", "prereq": "", "text": "She carries a silver wand of command. Once per round on her turn she may move one animated Artifact ten feet — no action, no command spent — though the key's pull is gentle: nothing lifted, nothing dragged through barriers or out of grapples. A shepherd's crook, not a chain. You carry a voltaic key — a silver wand of command for your machines. Once per round on your turn, you may move one animated Artifact you control up to 10 feet; this costs no action and does not consume your command. The key's pull is gentle: it cannot lift an Artifact off the ground, move it through a barrier, or drag it out of a grapple."}, {"name": "Darksteel", "prereq": "", "text": "Her plating can lock rigid: as a bonus action one animated Artifact goes immobile until her next turn, granting half cover to those behind it. Sometimes the kindest thing a relation can do is stand still and be a wall. as a bonus action, one animated Artifact becomes immobile until the start of your next turn; while immobile it grants half cover to creatures behind it."}, {"name": "Urza's Legacy", "prereq": "", "text": "When she uses Creator's Touch she may grant a temporary modification instead of healing — ten feet of range, one damage resistance, or advantage on one save type, lasting until her next long rest. The mending hand also improves. when you use Creator's Touch, you may grant a temporary modification instead of healing: +10 ft range, one damage resistance, or advantage on one save type, lasting until your next long rest."}], "e136": [{"name": "Vampiric Link", "prereq": "", "text": "His thirst is efficient; nothing is wasted. When his vampiric healing would exceed his maximum, the excess becomes temporary hit points — up to five plus his level, for a minute, his veins visibly darkening. The stolen-blood shield, recalculated each time. Your thirst is efficient; nothing is wasted. Whenever one of your vampire features would heal you above your maximum HP, the excess becomes temporary HP instead, up to a maximum of 5 + your level. This stolen-blood shield lasts 1 minute and visibly darkens your veins, and it does not stack with itself — recalculate the total each time."}, {"name": "Blood Artist", "prereq": "", "text": "Every death near him is a vintage. Once per round, when a creature within thirty feet dies — his own summon included — his reaction harvests its final pulse for one Blood. Friend or foe; he does not discriminate. No death pays twice. Every death near you is a vintage. Once per round, when a creature within 30 feet of you dies — including one of your own summons — you may use your reaction to harvest its final pulse, gaining 1 Blood. This works on any death you witness, friend or foe; Sorin does not discriminate. You cannot gain Blood twice from the same death."}, {"name": "Ancient Grudge", "prereq": "", "text": "When a creature damages him, his reaction may taste its blood from afar — learning its current hit points and whether it bleeds below half. The aristocrat keeps a cellar book on everyone who has ever cut him. when a creature damages you, you may use your reaction to taste its blood from afar: learn its current HP total and whether it is below half."}, {"name": "Sanguine Bond", "prereq": "", "text": "He forges a bond with a chosen enemy: one Blood as a bonus action marks a creature within sixty feet until his next turn ends — and the first time each turn he heals himself, the marked one takes his proficiency in necrotic. His wounds close; theirs open in sympathy. Foreign healing muddies the link and breaks it. You forge a sanguine bond with a chosen enemy: as a bonus action for 1 Blood, mark one creature you can see within 60 feet until the end of your next turn. The first time each turn you heal yourself while the mark persists, the marked creature takes necrotic damage equal to your proficiency bonus — your wounds close and theirs open in sympathy. The bond breaks early if the target receives magical healing from another source; foreign blood muddies the link."}], "e137": [{"name": "Dream Eater", "prereq": "", "text": "When her Nightmare wounds a creature bearing three Fear Marks, she may strip all its Marks to grant the Nightmare two more dice of psychic for a minute. The specimen, fed on its own subject. when your Nightmare damages a creature with 3 Fear Marks, you may remove all its Marks to grant the Nightmare +2d8 psychic on its attacks for 1 minute."}, {"name": "Faceless Fear", "prereq": "", "text": "Her Nightmare is never what it was a moment ago. As a bonus action it may alter its appearance freely — face, voice, stature — becoming anyone the marked creature fears or trusts, statistics unchanged. A creature that sees through it is immune to the trick for a day, but the fear remains: the Marks stay. Presentation, not transformation — claws remain claws. Your Blueprint is never what it was a moment ago. Your summoned Nightmare Shikigami can alter its appearance freely as a bonus action — face, voice, stature — becoming anyone the marked creature fears or trusts, without changing its statistics. A creature that sees through the disguise (Investigation vs. your technique DC) is immune to this trick for 24 hours, but the fear remains: it keeps its Fear Marks. This is presentation, not transformation — claws remain claws."}, {"name": "Mill the Mind", "prereq": "", "text": "When a creature reaches three Fear Marks, she may immediately loose Exile Thought against it as a reaction, unspent, once per round. The cabinet's door swings shut the moment the specimen is complete. when a creature reaches 3 Fear Marks, you may immediately use Exile Thought against it as a reaction without spending CE. Once per round."}, {"name": "Night Terror", "prereq": "", "text": "When a creature bearing at least one Fear Mark moves, her Nightmare may move up to its speed as a reaction to follow — once per round. The specimen does not lose its subject. when a creature with at least 1 Fear Mark moves, your Nightmare may move up to its speed as a reaction to follow it. Once per round."}], "e138": [{"name": "Pack Bond", "prereq": "", "text": "When he commands his beasts, two may combine their attacks on one target — a single roll with advantage, both beasts' damage on a hit. The pack's oldest tactic: one throat, many teeth. when you command your beasts, you may have two of them combine attacks on one target: make a single attack roll with advantage, dealing both beasts' damage on a hit."}, {"name": "Primal Hunter", "prereq": "", "text": "His beasts do not hunt with eyes alone. The marked creature gains nothing from invisibility, obscurement, or hiding against them — scent and tremor betray it — and they have advantage to locate it, nor can it surprise the pack while the mark lasts. The mark still ends at the hour. Your beasts do not hunt with eyes alone. A creature marked by your Hunter's Mark cannot benefit from invisibility, obscurement, or being Hidden against your beasts — scent, sound, and the tremor of its steps betray it. Your beasts have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to locate the marked target, and it cannot surprise your pack while the mark persists. The mark still ends after one hour."}, {"name": "Trample", "prereq": "", "text": "A charging beast is a siege engine. When one with the Charge trait moves twenty feet straight at a creature and lands a melee hit, the target saves its Strength or is pushed ten feet — and the beast may keep moving. The hunt does not stop for obstacles. A charging beast is a siege engine. When one of your beasts with the Charge trait moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and hits it with a melee attack, the target must succeed on a Strength save against your technique DC or be pushed 10 feet directly away from the beast. The beast may continue its movement after the push if it has speed remaining."}, {"name": "Unnatural Predation", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per short rest, he may command a beast within sixty feet of an enemy that harmed an ally to answer it with an attack as a reaction. The pack protects its own. reaction command beast to attack an enemy that harms an ally (the beast must be within 60 ft of that enemy) once/short rest."}], "e139": [{"name": "Mox Engineer", "prereq": "", "text": "When one of his constructs is destroyed, his reaction salvages the wreckage — one final attack or activation before it collapses. Nothing in his workshop dies without filing its last report. I have debriefed the dying. His debriefs are filed by the wreckage, on schedule. When one of your constructs, Thopters, or Blueprint devices is destroyed, you can use your reaction to salvage its wreckage: it makes one final attack or activation at its current position before collapsing."}, {"name": "Academy Rector", "prereq": "", "text": "He may open his Academy's workshop to allies: one willing ally attunes to a single prepared device and uses it once. Good supply serves the whole army. I have supplied armies. His supply, I observe, is a curriculum. You can open your Tolarian Academy workshop to allies: during a short rest, one willing ally can attune to a single prepared Blueprint device and use it once before your next long rest."}, {"name": "Master Transmuter", "prereq": "", "text": "As an action for two energy he may transmute one prepared Blueprint into another — the plan, revised under fire. I revise plans under fire. His revisions, I note, are manufactured on the spot, to specification. As an action for 2 CE, you can transmute one prepared Blueprint into another you know, rebuilding the device in the field. The new device must serve a similar function (a sensor array can become a grapnel, not a Titan Engine), and a burned Blueprint cannot be transmuted."}, {"name": "Blind Seer", "prereq": "", "text": "His hands read machines the way scholars read books — name, properties, command words, whether trapped. Function, not history. True artifacts resist, yielding one property of his choice. Even the seer respects a locked drawer. I have picked locks. He reads them. I am revising my definition of 'secure.' Your hands read machines the way scholars read books. By touching a cursed tool and concentrating for 1 minute, you learn its name, its activated properties, its command words, and whether it is trapped or cursed — as the identify spell, but only for crafted objects and devices. This reveals function, not history; it will not tell you who made it or why. True artifacts and legendary tools resist: from such an item you learn only one property of your choice."}, {"name": "Mishra's Rival", "prereq": "", "text": "His Titan Engine may mount one of his other Blueprints as a hardpoint — beam, shield, or sensor integrated, usable as a bonus action while the Engine stands. The siege's crown, jeweled. Your Titan Engine can mount one of your other Blueprints as a hardpoint: while the Engine is active, one prepared device (beam, shield, or sensor) is integrated into it and can be used as a bonus action on your turn."}, {"name": "The Brothers' War", "prereq": "", "text": "His Titan Engine may carry his smaller machines into battle — four Thopters or one drone docked, untargetable while docked, deployable as a bonus action. The war chest travels with its loose change. Your Titan Engine can carry your smaller machines into battle: up to four Thopters or one drone can dock with the Engine. While docked they cannot be targeted separately, and the Engine can deploy them as a bonus action."}], "e140": [{"name": "Toxic", "prereq": "", "text": "Her oil hangs in the air around her: past Oil five she exudes a miasma, and a creature starting its turn within five feet saves its Constitution or gains one Infection, three at most. The manuscript has an atmosphere. Your oil hangs in the air around you: once you reach Oil 5, you exude a miasma. A creature that starts its turn within 5 feet of you must make a Constitution save or gain 1 Infection (maximum 3)."}, {"name": "Viral Drake", "prereq": "", "text": "Her Infection spreads like a virus: when she Proliferates, one creature bearing her Infection may leap the oil to another within ten feet — a failed Constitution save, one Infection gained. The footnote cites another footnote. Your Infection spreads like a virus: when you Proliferate, choose one creature bearing your Infection. One creature within 10 feet of it must make a Constitution save or gain 1 Infection as the oil leaps hosts."}, {"name": "Steel Thane", "prereq": "", "text": "Her compleated plating can lock rigid: as a reaction to bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage she gains resistance to that instance — but her speed becomes zero until her next turn as the plating seizes. Armor has opinions about mobility. Your compleated plating can lock rigid: as a reaction when you take bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage, you gain resistance to that instance of damage, but your speed becomes 0 until the start of your next turn as the plating seizes."}, {"name": "Gitaxian Probe", "prereq": "", "text": "A hair-thin probe of oil toward a creature within sixty feet: as a bonus action for one energy she learns its resistances, immunities, vulnerabilities, and how hurt it is — unharmed, bloodied, or critical. Near-invisible, leaving no Infection: observation, not corruption. Once probed, her Adapt may copy its resistance profile untested. The editor reads before revising. You extend a hair-thin probe of glistening oil toward one creature you can see within 60 feet: as a bonus action for 1 CE, you learn its damage resistances, immunities, and vulnerabilities, plus how hurt it is — unharmed, bloodied, or critical. The probe is near-invisible (Wisdom (Perception) vs. your technique DC to notice) and leaves no Infection; it is observation, not corruption. Once you have probed a creature, your Adapt feature may copy its resistance profile even if you have not yet taken that damage type."}], "e141": [{"name": "Pathrazer", "prereq": "", "text": "His Void Limb phases through obstructions — ignoring cover, striking through walls, the barrier taking damage first and the excess carrying through. Absence does not knock. I have knocked. I have also been knocked through. Neither prepared me for the limb that does not acknowledge the wall. Your Void Limb phases through obstructions: its attacks ignore half and three-quarters cover, and you can strike a creature through a wall or barrier within your reach. The barrier takes the damage first, and any excess carries through to the creature."}, {"name": "Brood Lineage", "prereq": "", "text": "His brood feeds on its own dissolution: a sacrificed Scion becomes Void, or a survivor strikes harder. The void recycles. I have recycled supplies. His supply chain, I note, is his own children, and the margins are excellent. Your brood feeds on its own dissolution: when one of your Eldrazi Scions is sacrificed or destroyed, you gain 1 Void, or one surviving Scion deals an extra 1d8 damage on its next attack."}, {"name": "Reality Smasher", "prereq": "", "text": "Past six Void his warped mass barrels through the world — difficult terrain ignored, walls smashed into five-foot breaches. The map is redrawn by walking. I have redrawn maps. His revisions are made with his body, at speed, and they are not submitted for approval. At Void 6+, your warped mass barrels through the world: you can move through difficult terrain without penalty and smash through nonmagical barriers and walls, leaving a 5-foot breach in your wake."}, {"name": "Ulamog's Hunger", "prereq": "", "text": "His Reality Hunger devours what it unmakes: destroying a summon refunds two energy and one Void. The meal pays for itself. I have run campaigns on foraging. His foraging, I observe, is ontological, and the yield is excellent. Reality Hunger devours what it unmakes: if its sphere destroys a summon, construct, or barrier, you regain 2 CE and 1 Void."}, {"name": "Kozilek's Distortion", "prereq": "", "text": "He may twist a hostile illusion back on its caster — the caster saves or suffers its own illusion. The nothing returns the lie to sender. I have returned correspondence. His returns, I note, are addressed to the sender's own mind. You can twist a hostile illusion back on its caster: as a reaction for 1 Void when you succeed on a save against an illusion, the caster must succeed on an Intelligence save or suffer the illusion's effect as if they were its target."}, {"name": "Emrakul's Whisper", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per long rest, when a creature fails a save, he may whisper through the Blind Eternities — Charming it and dictating one action of its next turn. The void speaks, and it gives orders. I have given orders. His orders arrive from nowhere, in a voice that is not a voice. I have started checking my own orders for provenance. Once per long rest, when a creature fails a save against one of your technique features, you can whisper through the Blind Eternities: it is charmed by you until the end of its next turn, and you can dictate one action it takes on its next turn."}], "e142": [{"name": "Gemhide", "prereq": "", "text": "A sliver's gemhide is condensed mana. As a bonus action he may sacrifice one summoned Sliver within thirty feet — never the Queen; her hide is load-bearing — dissolving it into one energy regained. The sacrificed cannot be re-summoned until his next turn. The chorus donates a voice to the cause. A sliver's gemhide is condensed mana. As a bonus action, you may sacrifice one of your summoned Slivers within 30 feet: it dissolves into component mana and you regain 1 CE. You cannot sacrifice the Sliver Queen this way — her hide is load-bearing. A sacrificed sliver cannot be re-summoned until your next turn."}, {"name": "Hibernation", "prereq": "", "text": "When the brood is caught in an area effect, instinct takes over: as a reaction he may dismiss any number of Slivers into hibernation — half damage, returning at his next turn's start, the already-dead staying dead. Dormant slivers cannot act or be targeted. The chorus holds its breath. When your brood is caught in an area effect, instinct takes over. As a reaction when one or more of your Slivers would take damage from an area effect, you may dismiss any number of them into hibernation: they vanish into the hive-mind's dormant state, take half damage from the effect, and return at the start of your next turn in their previous spaces (or the nearest free space). Slivers reduced to 0 HP by the halved damage do not return — hibernation cannot save the already dead. Dormant slivers cannot act or be targeted."}, {"name": "Crystalline", "prereq": "", "text": "Their refractive hides turn blades aside: as a reaction when a Sliver is hit, another within five feet may interpose itself and become the target. The chorus takes its wounds in rotation. Your Slivers' refractive hides turn blades aside: as a reaction when a Sliver is hit by an attack, another Sliver within 5 feet can interpose itself, becoming the target instead."}, {"name": "Necrotic", "prereq": "", "text": "A dying sliver's final act is spite: when one is destroyed, one adjacent hostile takes a die of necrotic with no save — rupturing ichor, not an attack, unredirectable. Slivers sacrificed cleanly through Gemhide do not burst; their mana is harvested before it can rupture. Even the exits are choreographed. A dying sliver's final act is spite. When one of your Slivers is destroyed, one hostile creature adjacent to it takes 1d8 necrotic damage with no save, as rupturing ichor sprays outward. This is not an attack and cannot be redirected — it is simply what happens when sliver-flesh bursts. Slivers sacrificed cleanly, such as through Gemhide, do not burst; their mana is harvested before it can rupture."}], "e143": [{"name": "Mana Dork", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per short rest she may grow a one-hit-point mana dork — holding one temporary Mastery rank, spendable by any ally within five feet. The council keeps a page. I have kept pages. Hers carries a vote. Once per short rest, you can grow a 1-HP mana dork for 1 minute: it holds one temporary Mastery rank of a color you choose, and any ally within 5 feet of it can spend that rank once as if it were their own rank-1 color feature."}, {"name": "Fetchland", "prereq": "", "text": "Her mana base is a landscape she can reshape — moving Mastery between colors, never past three, spent colors locked. Pulling the right land from the deck, in the old parlance. I have reshaped terrain. She reshapes the ground her own power stands on, mid-battle, as an action. The parlance, I confess, is inadequate. Your mana base is a landscape you can reshape. As an action once per short rest, you may redistribute one Mana Mastery point from one color to another — pulling the right 'land' from the deck, in the old parlance. The point must come from a color with at least 2 ranks, and the receiving color cannot exceed 3 ranks this way. Colors you have already spent from this turn are locked; you cannot fetch what is already cast."}, {"name": "Gold Spell", "prereq": "", "text": "Her guild repertoire runs deeper: one additional pair spell, fixed — the guild she apprenticed in — while the other two remain re-choosable. The old allegiance, kept. I have kept allegiances. Hers is not loyalty but load-bearing structure. Your guild repertoire runs deeper than most. You learn one additional two-color pair spell beyond the two you choose at rest, drawn from the same list — Azorius detention, Dimir mind theft, Rakdos sacrifice-flame, Gruul overrun, Selesnya mass ward, and the rest. This third pair is fixed, the guild you apprenticed in, while your other two remain re-choosable at each rest. It costs the same CE and obeys the same rank requirements as your other pair spells."}, {"name": "Command Tower", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per long rest she may raise her Command Tower — and for a minute, cast any color's rank-one basics for one energy. For sixty seconds, every court is in session. I have called councils into session. Hers convenes at full strength for sixty seconds, on demand. The minutes, I note, are the ones that matter. Once per long rest, you can raise your Command Tower for 1 minute: during that time you can cast any color's rank-1 basics by spending 1 CE, regardless of your current Mastery distribution."}, {"name": "Progenitus Echo", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per long rest, as a reaction, she echoes Progenitus's immunity: one damage type, she and allies within ten feet resisting it. Protection, from the oldest precedent. I have cited precedent. Hers is not cited but embodied — the oldest immunity, worn for a turn. Once per long rest, as a reaction when you or an ally within 10 feet would take damage, you can echo Progenitus's immunity to harm: choose one damage type, and you and allies within 10 feet gain resistance to that type until the start of your next turn."}, {"name": "Door to Nothingness", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per long rest, with all five colors ranked, she may open the Door: one creature saves or is exiled to the void between colors, returning with exhaustion. The council's final sanction. I have sanctioned. Her sanctions, I observe, are not punishments but removals — from the map, from the colors, from the proceedings. The ayes have it. Once per long rest, while you have at least 1 rank in all five colors, you can open the Door as an action for 10 CE: one creature within 60 feet makes a Charisma save or is exiled to the void between colors until the end of your next turn, returning with 1 level of exhaustion."}], "e144": [{"name": "Museum-Grade Repair", "prereq": "", "text": "The final flourish of the craft: a repaired vessel is not merely whole — the next blow slides off the gold. Your golden seams hold stronger than the original: when you fully repair an object, construct, or cursed tool, you can lace the break with gold. The next time it would take damage, it takes none instead, once per object."}, {"name": "Beautiful Scar", "prereq": "", "text": "The seam leaves more than strength; the mended carry the surgeon's blessing into their next trial. A creature you Mend yourself (an ally’s self-seal with Seal the Seam does not count) gains advantage on its next saving throw before the end of your next turn. Once per creature per short rest."}, {"name": "Shatterpoint", "prereq": "", "text": "The potter's eye is also a duelist's eye — she sees the moment the cracks reach their limit, and is there before it falls. When a hostile creature reaches its maximum number of Fractures, you may immediately move 10 feet without provoking opportunity attacks. Your next attack against it before the end of the turn has advantage."}], "e145": [{"name": "Foundation First", "prereq": "", "text": "Victory before battle: she surveys the ground before the first blow, and the network is already standing when initiative is called. You survey foundations before the first blow: if you spend 10 minutes studying a location, you can designate up to PB willing creatures there as Supports the instant initiative is rolled within the next 24 hours, without using an action."}, {"name": "Shock Absorber", "prereq": "", "text": "The shock passes through her and out again — what was meant to punish her becomes the thunder that answers it. When you take damage redirected through Weight Distribution, you can Discharge the shock as part of the same reaction: one creature within 15 feet makes a Dexterity save or takes that damage as thunder and is pushed 10 feet away from you. Once per round."}, {"name": "Counterweight", "prereq": "", "text": "Every lever has its opposite end. When the structure hurls the enemy, she rides the counter-motion to safety. When you push a creature with Discharge, you may move the same distance in the opposite direction without provoking opportunity attacks."}], "e146": [{"name": "Sailor’s Hands", "prereq": "", "text": "The veteran's trick: splice through an old Knot to lay the new one farther than the arm can reach, around corners the eye cannot see. You can splice your cords through existing Knots: when you tie a Knot, you may route it through another creature or object already bearing one of your Knots, extending your tying range to 60 feet for that Knot and ignoring cover between the relay and the target."}, {"name": "Quick Release", "prereq": "", "text": "She never holds a knot she cannot let go of — and the letting-go carries her five feet toward the next opportunity. When one of your Knots ends, move up to 5 feet without provoking opportunity attacks. Once per turn."}, {"name": "Executioner’s Knot", "prereq": "", "text": "The noose is the cord's oldest argument. Three Knots deep, the quarry learns what the hangman always knew. As an action for 3 CE, you can tie a hangman's noose around a creature bearing 3+ of your Knots within 30 feet: it makes a Constitution save or is restrained until the end of your next turn, unable to speak or use verbal components while the noose holds."}], "e147": [{"name": "Seismograph", "prereq": "", "text": "He listens to the ground the way a banker listens to markets — and knows exactly how many debtors stand upon it. You can read the earth's complaints: as an action, take a seismic reading. You learn how many creatures within 60 feet are touching the ground, and whether any Huge or larger creature is moving within 300 feet."}, {"name": "Hairline Crack", "prereq": "", "text": "The auditor begins before the first word is spoken: one Fault is already on the books when initiative is called. When you roll initiative, place one Fault on a visible surface or creature that has already taken damage, no action required."}, {"name": "Cascade Failure", "prereq": "", "text": "One account settled by death pays its neighbor's balance — the panic spreads to the nearest Fault. After a creature bearing your Fault drops to 0 HP, one Fault within 30 feet immediately gains 2 Strain."}], "e148": [{"name": "Joseki Study", "prereq": "", "text": "She knows the classical shapes: a stone placed in good company lets her reposition — the old sequences still win. You know the classical shapes: when you place a Stone adjacent to at least two of your other Stones, you may immediately move one deployed Stone up to 10 feet across a surface, as if using Sente."}, {"name": "Sacrifice Play", "prereq": "", "text": "A stone may be given to take: when one would be destroyed, she detonates it — the sacrifice was always the plan. Reaction when one of your Stones would be destroyed: detonate it. Creatures within 5 feet make a Dexterity save or take 2 Influence Dice force damage."}, {"name": "Reading Ahead", "prereq": "", "text": "The master reads before the game begins: one stone placed free when initiative is called. At the start of combat, after initiative is rolled, place one Stone within 10 feet of yourself for free."}], "e149": [{"name": "Old Growth", "prereq": "", "text": "She keeps one ancient Node: doubled in body, doubled in connection — but old growth fruits no new blooms. After a long rest, choose one of your Nodes to become old growth: it becomes Large with double HP and counts as two Connected Nodes for adjacency and teleportation, but it can never be converted into a Bloom."}, {"name": "Medicinal Culture", "prereq": "", "text": "She cultivates a healing strain apart: a poultice grafted before the wound, waiting to burst into repair. You cultivate a healing strain: as an action for 1 Nutrient, graft a poultice onto a willing creature within 10 feet of a Node. The poultice persists until the bearer takes damage. If Distributed Organism negates the triggering damage, the poultice is not expended. When that happens, the poultice bursts and heals it for 2 Spore Dice."}, {"name": "Cordyceps Reflex", "prereq": "", "text": "The network rewards her predators: every fallen or bound hostile feeds it one more Nutrient. When a hostile creature within 10 feet of a Node falls prone, grappled, or restrained, gain 1 Nutrient. Once per round."}], "e150": [{"name": "Archivist’s Eye", "prereq": "", "text": "She reads an object's revisions by touch — the alterations are footnotes to her, and she follows them. You can read an object's revisions: by touching an object for 1 minute, you learn whether it has been magically altered since you last touched it, and you gain advantage on checks to discern the alteration's nature."}, {"name": "Margin Walker", "prereq": "", "text": "She lingers in the margin between records: untargetable, unacting, until the return. You can linger in the margin between records: when you use Position Note on yourself, you can delay your return until the start of your next turn. While in the margin you cannot be targeted or act; you then return as a free action."}, {"name": "Errata", "prereq": "", "text": "Even a resisted revision leaves its mark: the creature's speed carries the subtraction of one Revision Die. When a creature succeeds on a save against Position Note or Redaction, it still subtracts one Revision Die from its speed until the end of the turn."}], "e151": [{"name": "Emergency Lane", "prereq": "", "text": "One lane may be declared an emergency: allies speed along it, and the first hostile each turn is pushed along its direction. As a bonus action, declare one of your Lanes an emergency lane until the start of your next turn: willing creatures traveling along it gain 10 feet of speed, and the first hostile creature each turn that enters it must make a Strength save or be pushed 10 feet along the lane's direction."}, {"name": "Traffic Camera", "prereq": "", "text": "She sees every vehicle on her roads — speed and Citations known at a glance. You know the current speed and number of Citations of every creature standing in one of your Lanes."}, {"name": "Repeat Offender", "prereq": "", "text": "The thrice-fined lose the cover of the crowd: her attacks ignore their half cover until the fines are paid. When a creature reaches 3 Citations, your attacks against it ignore half cover until its Citations are spent."}], "e152": [{"name": "Perfumer’s Case", "prereq": "", "text": "She decants her formulas into thrown vials: thirty feet, ten-foot radius — and even Courage Accord may be splashed. You can decant a formula into a thrown vial: as an action, throw one prepared bottle up to 30 feet. It shatters on impact, applying its effect in a 10-foot radius (single-target formulas allow a Dexterity save for half). A thrown Courage Accord is a splash of fortitude: each creature in the radius that fails the Dexterity save gains half the Veil’s temporary HP (rounded down); every creature’s Scent Veil still blooms when depleted."}, {"name": "Cold Extraction", "prereq": "", "text": "The patient perfumer: a day-old scene still yields its trace, if the residue remains. You can gather Hunter’s Trace from a scene up to 24 hours old if physical residue remains."}, {"name": "Acquired Taste", "prereq": "", "text": "The final cruelty of the craft: the failed victim craves the scent — and the craving walks him toward her. A creature that fails its save against one of your formulas develops a craving for it: for the next hour, you can use a bonus action and 1 CE to release a trace of that scent. The craving creature must make a Wisdom save or use its reaction to move up to half its speed toward you by the safest route."}], "e153": [{"name": "Organized Shelving", "prereq": "", "text": "Her shelves are cross-indexed by need: once per short rest, the needed mundane item is simply there. Your archive is cross-indexed by need: once per short rest, when you or an ally within 30 feet needs a mundane item (rope, tools, rations, a healer's kit), you can produce it from the archive immediately without spending a Claim Ticket, provided it fits your size limit."}, {"name": "No Receipt Needed", "prereq": "", "text": "The disarmer's privilege: a successfully disarmed object is shelved without spending the reaction. When you successfully disarm a creature, you may Archive the dropped eligible object immediately without using your reaction."}, {"name": "Premium Loaner", "prereq": "", "text": "One loaner each rest is presentable enough to lend: an ally may wield it for the hour, even should she fall. Choose Weapon, Barricade, or Restraint after each long rest: your premium loaner is presentable enough to lend. An ally can wield it as if you had created it for them, and it persists for 1 hour even if you fall unconscious."}], "e154": [{"name": "Blink Hunter", "prereq": "Blind Spot", "text": "Refinement observed: any other expenditure of an observer's reaction now ends the watch — and once per round, the Reflex answers it. The subject's trigger conditions are widening. Update the protocol again. When a creature that is currently Observing you spends or loses its reaction for any other reason, its Observation immediately ends. Once per round this may trigger Blink Reflex."}, {"name": "Concrete Idol", "prereq": "Blind Spot, level 3", "text": "Defensive finding: perfect stillness absorbs the blow — a subject that moves nothing may blunt incoming harm as a reaction. The statue discipline, weaponized. Even its defense is about not being seen to move. If you willingly move 0 feet on your turn, you may use a reaction before your next turn to reduce one damage instance by 5 × PB + CE modifier."}, {"name": "No Peripheral Vision", "prereq": "Blind Spot, level 6", "text": "Edge case, verified: against a single observer, the subject can force a micro-blink — the Step resolving before observation resumes. One eye is no longer sufficient. Minimum staffing requirements updated. If exactly one Observer can see you, you may attempt Blind Spot Step by paying +2 CE. That Observer makes a Wisdom save; on failure it experiences a micro-blink and ceases Observing before the Step resolves."}, {"name": "Neck-Line Anatomy", "prereq": "Blind Spot, level 11", "text": "Lethality finding: arrival strikes that overwhelm resistance by a wide margin do not merely fell the target — they stun. The nervous system, overloaded at the moment of the subject's arrival. We have not tested whether the subject is aware of the limit. Once per short rest when Snap Strike hits and the target fails its Constitution save by 5 or more, it is stunned until the end of your next turn instead of the normal failed-save result."}], "e155": [{"name": "Grief-Fueled Momentum", "prereq": "Shamebound Pursuit", "text": "Feedback loop confirmed: when the Quarry's blow lands, the subject gains one Fury. Being struck enrages rather than deters. Standard deterrence models do not apply; do not apply them. Once per round when your Quarry damages you, gain 1 Fury after that damage resolves."}, {"name": "Unseen Photograph", "prereq": "Four Pixels", "text": "Resolution finding: the imprint may shrink to four pixels — perception, not possession, is the trigger. Merely owning the image is insufficient; the image must be seen. Our monitors are now set to thumbnail. This feels like losing. Your cursed face imprints may be as small as a four-pixel detail. A creature must actually perceive the detail to become a Witness; merely possessing the image is not enough."}, {"name": "No Rest Until Silence", "prereq": "Shamebound Pursuit, level 6", "text": "Fury persistence: half is retained when the Quarry falls, transferable to the next Witness designated. The hunt does not end with the Quarry. It pauses, politely, and continues. When your Quarry drops to 0 HP, retain up to half your current Fury until the end of your next turn. If you choose another Witness as Quarry before then, transfer that Fury."}, {"name": "Inhuman Acceleration", "prereq": "Shamebound Pursuit, level 11", "text": "Closure event, verified: once per short rest, a sixty-foot gap is closed in a single turn — across water, up walls, without an action spent. Distance is the one variable the subject has fully solved. Once per short rest, when you start your turn at least 60 feet from the Quarry, you may Dash without an action and your movement that turn may cross liquid surfaces and vertical walls."}], "e156": [{"name": "House Call", "prereq": "Pestilence Doctrine", "text": "Reach extension: fifteen feet through a spectral gloved hand — the examination need not touch. The subject can now diagnose at a distance. Social distancing, as a concept, has been retired for this ward. Clinical Touch and The Cure gain 15-foot reach through a spectral gloved hand. This does not let you pass through total cover."}, {"name": "Second Opinion", "prereq": "Clinical Examination", "text": "Deeper rendering: examinations now report exact hit points, or name one resistance or vulnerability. The subject's charting is more thorough than ours. This is embarrassing, professionally. Your examinations render deeper diagnoses: when you use Clinical Examination on a creature, choose one — learn its current hit points as a number, or learn one of its damage resistances or vulnerabilities."}, {"name": "Field Surgeon", "prereq": "Crude Surgery", "text": "Field adaptation noted. It works faster under pressure. So do we, now. Outside combat, Crude Surgery takes 1 minute instead of 10. In combat, a corpse you personally reduced to 0 HP may be made a Patient as a full-turn action for 4 CE even before level 11."}, {"name": "Humoral Imbalance", "prereq": "Pestilence Doctrine, level 11", "text": "Systemic stage: at four Symptoms the humors rebel — speed sapped, reactions lost on failed resistance. The body begins to agree with the diagnosis. That is the most frightening sentence in this file. A creature with 4+ Symptoms also has its speed reduced by 10 feet and cannot take reactions after it fails a Constitution save against your technique until the start of its next turn."}], "e157": [{"name": "Black Mucus", "prereq": "Corrosive Threshold", "text": "Terrain finding: the Marks leave difficult ground — the fallen in it pay extra to stand. Even the floor is on the subject's side. We have filed a complaint with the floor. A Surface Mark creates a 5-foot patch of difficult terrain for enemies. A creature that falls prone in it cannot stand without spending an additional 5 feet of movement."}, {"name": "Predator Beneath", "prereq": "Predatory Emergence", "text": "Submersion option: after the Walk the subject may remain half-submerged — half cover for the price of stillness. It waits inside the wall like a crocodile. We have stopped using the word 'wall' as if it meant safety. After Threshold Walk, you may remain partially submerged until the start of your next turn. You have half cover but your speed is 0 and you cannot make opportunity attacks while submerged."}, {"name": "Liquefying Grip", "prereq": "Corrosive Touch, level 6", "text": "Third-Mark effect: no reactions until the subject's next turn, and the grapple attempted in the same motion. The seasoning, the seizing, and the swallowing — all in one gesture. Efficient. We hate how efficient. When you apply the third Corrosion Mark to a creature, it cannot take reactions until the end of its next turn and you may attempt to grapple it as part of the same attack."}, {"name": "Recall Protocol", "prereq": "Corrosive Threshold, level 11", "text": "Once per short rest, the quartered threshold keeps him: two CE and the reaction, and he is at any Mark within a hundred and twenty feet. Once per short rest when damage would reduce you below one-quarter HP, use your reaction and 2 CE to teleport to any Surface Mark within 120 feet after the damage resolves."}], "e158": [{"name": "Perfect Voiceprint", "prereq": "With Many Voices", "text": "Mimicry depth: beyond speech — breath, weeping, footsteps — and two archived sounds layered at once, calling from two directions. In trial 9 the subject held a conversation with itself, in our voices, about us. We have the transcript. We are not releasing the transcript. Your mimicry extends beyond speech: you can reproduce any nonverbal sound made by a creature whose voice you have archived — breathing, crying, footsteps — and layer two archived sounds at once, a voice calling from one direction and footsteps from another."}, {"name": "Dark Hunter", "prereq": "Troglobitic Senses", "text": "Projection finding: the voice hunts ahead — projected to a point, the subject hears through it as through its own ears. Its hearing is wherever its voice has been. The concept of 'elsewhere' is thinning in this file. Your voice hunts ahead of you: as a bonus action for 1 CE, project a Voiceprint to a point within 60 feet. Until the start of your next turn you can hear through that point as if you were there, and your blindsight extends 30 feet from it."}, {"name": "No New Memories", "prereq": "Amnestic Breath, level 6", "text": "Deep-erasure event: the failed victim loses the last minute itself — cannot describe the subject, the room, or its orders. For one hour, the witness is a perfect, polite absence of evidence. Our interview transcripts from this stage are blank pages with timestamps. We keep them anyway. A creature that fails its save against your Amnestic Breath also loses its short-term memory of the last minute: for the next hour it cannot describe you, recall the room's layout, or remember orders received in that time."}, {"name": "Pack Echo", "prereq": "With Many Voices, level 11", "text": "Pack finding: allies' strikes on the twice-hollowed are lured from the wrong direction, with advantage. The subject shares its hunting ground the way a conductor shares a baton. We are the orchestra. We did not audition. When an ally within 30 feet attacks a creature with 2+ Lost Moments, use your reaction and 1 CE to make the target hear the ally from the wrong direction. That attack gains advantage; this does not make you hidden."}], "e159": [{"name": "Lent Loathing", "prereq": "Adaptive Hatred", "text": "Hatred, it turns out, can be charitable. Once per round, when you take damage from a Threat Tag for which you have an installed Adaptation, you may use your reaction and 1 CE to lend that Adaptation’s benefit to one ally you can see until the start of your next turn: resistance for a damage Tag, or advantage on saves against a condition Tag. Your own Adaptation is unaffected."}, {"name": "Hostile Evolution", "prereq": "Reactive Morphology", "text": "Retaliation finding: every blow received becomes a blow returned. The subject does not counterattack. It returns fire with the attacker's own postage. Our insurance carrier has been notified. Once per turn, after a creature damages you with a Tag for which you have an installed Adaptation, you may use your reaction and 1 CE to make one unarmed strike against that creature. On a hit it takes an additional Adaptation Die of damage of the Tag’s damage type, or force damage if the Tag is a condition or environmental hazard."}, {"name": "Keter Genome", "prereq": "Adaptive Hatred, level 6", "text": "Acceleration event: the body now outpaces the ledger, installing what it merely remembers. Learning has become reflex. The subject is no longer studying pain; it is fluent in it. Once per round, when you take damage from a Threat Tag for which you hold at least 1 Data but have no installed Adaptation, you may use your reaction and 1 CE to immediately replace one installed Adaptation with an Adaptation to that Tag without spending Data."}, {"name": "Consume and Rebuild", "prereq": "Adaptive Hatred, level 11", "text": "Dietary finding: even the flesh may eat to learn. The subject incorporates meaningful quantities of matter during rest. We have stopped asking what it eats. The quartermaster's reports are redacted at the subject's request, which it made politely, in writing. Regain PB Adaptation Dice HP and gain 1 Data for one environmental or material Threat Tag that the consumed matter reasonably demonstrates; GM adjudicates the Tag."}], "e160": [{"name": "Honeyed Words", "prereq": "The Possessive Mask", "text": "Social finding: a silver tongue earns its marks without spending an action. The subject talks its way into faces the way other organisms breathe. Interviewers are now rotated every ten minutes. Once per turn when you succeed on Deception, Persuasion, or Intimidation against a creature currently at 0 Temptation, you may spend 1 CE to give it 1 Temptation without using an action."}, {"name": "Black Ichor", "prereq": "Corrosive Secretion", "text": "Ichor persistence: where spilled on a surface, it lingers as a corrosive patch. The stage retains the performance. Our floors have begun to keep a memory of every show. When Corrosive Secretion corrodes an unattended surface, leave a 5-foot corrosive patch until the start of your next turn. A creature entering it for the first time on a turn has its speed halved until the start of your next turn, maximum once per turn."}, {"name": "Borrowed Aptitude", "prereq": "Host Transfer, level 6", "text": "Skill acquisition: every body brings its own training; the mask keeps the best of it. Eleven hosts, eleven proficiencies, one resume. The subject is, technically, the most qualified individual in the facility. When you enter a living Host, choose one skill in which that Host is proficient. You gain proficiency in it while possessing that body; if already proficient, you gain no additional expertise."}, {"name": "Never Without a Face", "prereq": "Host Transfer, level 11", "text": "Contingency observed: the prudent actor keeps a spare costume within a mile — a prepared vessel, designated during rest. The subject always has an understudy waiting in the wings. We have mapped three. There are, we suspect, more. During a short rest, designate one valid nonliving vessel — a corpse, mannequin, or statue you have prepared — within 1 mile as your contingency. The first time within the next 24 hours that a Host ejects you or reaches 0 Integrity, your consciousness transfers to the contingency vessel immediately without spending CE or an action, instead of returning to the Prime Host or falling free."}], "e161": [{"name": "Salvage Intake", "prereq": "Refining Clockworks", "text": "Scavenging behavior: the machine learns to catch what the battlefield throws away — wreckage within thirty feet fed straight to the Intake as a reaction. Nothing is wasted. Including, we note, our battlefields. When a construct, vehicle, or unattended object is destroyed within 30 feet of your manifested Clockworks, you may use your reaction to feed the wreckage straight into the Intake, gaining Scrap as though you had used Rough on it for its size, without spending an action."}, {"name": "Restorative Refinement", "prereq": "Very Fine", "text": "Restoration mode: refinement run backward — the machine remembers what the object used to be. It rebuilds the broken to full function, no roll, no Risk gained. The subject's memory of objects is better than the objects' memory of themselves. When you activate Very Fine, you may choose restoration instead of rolling: rebuild one damaged or broken mundane object, or one non-Special-Grade cursed tool, placed in the Intake, restoring it to full function and clearing the broken condition. Pay the normal activation cost; no roll is made and no Risk is gained."}, {"name": "Decoupled Line", "prereq": "Portable Clockworks", "text": "Spatial finding: Intake here, Output thirty feet there — the mill stretches. The subject's workflow now spans the room. Our floor plan has been updated. The subject updated it first. When you manifest the Clockworks, you may place the Intake and Output frames up to 30 feet apart — both within 60 feet of you — instead of adjacent. Items fed into the Intake emerge refined from the Output normally."}, {"name": "Hot-Swap Tuning", "prereq": "Fine, level 6", "text": "Upgrade mobility: upgrades become tenants; they may change rooms. Nothing the subject improves is fixed in place. Including, we have begun to suspect, the subject's definition of 'improved.' As a bonus action, move one active Fine upgrade from an item you touch to another valid item you touch; the upgrade’s remaining duration continues on the new item. An item may still hold only one Fine upgrade."}], "e162": [{"name": "Flat-Pack Trap", "prereq": "Infinite Retail", "text": "Assembly targeting: the catalog learns to assemble itself around the prone — Merchandise built around a fallen creature within thirty feet. The store practices hospitality on the horizontal. Guests report the service is confining. When you use Flat-Pack Manifestation, you may target a prone creature within 30 feet instead of an unoccupied space, assembling the Merchandise around it. The target makes a Strength saving throw against your technique DC; on a failure it is restrained inside the furniture until it uses an action to break free against your technique DC. The Merchandise has its normal statistics and can be attacked."}, {"name": "Fire Exit Plan", "prereq": "Closing Shift", "text": "Exit control: the founder decides where the Exit appears — hospitality, weaponized. The store chooses the door. The door is always technically an exit. Technically is doing a great deal of work in that sentence. When a creature you can perceive manifests an Exit by succeeding on Search for an Exit, you may use your reaction to choose where that Exit appears: any unoccupied space within 30 feet of that creature, inside the Domain, instead of within 10 feet of it."}, {"name": "Night Watch", "prereq": "Settlement Founder, level 6", "text": "Rousing event: when Closed Hours begin, a Settlement may be roused to watch. The homes the Stranded built open their eyes. The store, which never sleeps, respects those that try to. When Closed Hours begins, you may use your reaction to rouse one Settlement you can perceive. Until the next Store Phase, up to PB creatures inside it may make opportunity attacks against Staff that enter or leave the Settlement, and your Display Fixtures’ difficult terrain does not impede them."}, {"name": "Exchange & Returns", "prereq": "Restocking Cycle, level 11", "text": "Dawn audit: what survived the night may be returned for Hit Dice — the willing inside a surviving Settlement recover without action. The store pays its survivors in health. The exchange rate, for once, seems fair. When Open Hours begins, instead of restoring Merchandise or removing Remains with Restocking Cycle, choose one Settlement that survived the previous Closed Hours. Every willing creature inside it may immediately spend one Hit Die and regain that much HP without using an action."}], "e163": [{"name": "Bridgewatcher", "prereq": "", "text": "Initiative is rolled; the watcher already knows which structures will fail. When initiative is rolled, choose one visible structure, vehicle, barrier, or terrain feature. You know whether it is currently stable, damaged, trapped, or likely to catastrophically fail within the next minute. If it fails during the encounter, gain 2 Omens."}, {"name": "Scarlet Afterimage", "prereq": "", "text": "A moved creature leaves its red ghost behind — and the ghost takes the next attack. When Eyes Before the Storm moves a creature, leave a red afterimage in its old space until the start of its next turn. The first hostile attack made through or into that space is made with disadvantage."}, {"name": "Bad Feeling", "prereq": "", "text": "One CE to ask the GM what the location is hiding — prophecy as due diligence. Once per short rest, after the GM describes a location but before the party commits to entering it, spend 1 CE to ask whether an immediate physical or cursed threat is present within 300 feet. The answer is yes/no/unclear; it does not identify the threat."}, {"name": "Prophet of Impact", "prereq": "", "text": "At three ticks, mark the square where the disaster will land. Prerequisite: Disaster Clock. When a Clock reaches 3, you may spend 2 Omens to mark one 10-foot square you can see. If the marked creature enters that square before your next turn, it falls prone and cannot take reactions until the end of that movement."}], "e164": [{"name": "Eddy Reading", "prereq": "", "text": "The atmosphere eddies around bodies, and the witness reads the eddies. While your Veil is active, you read the atmosphere eddying around bodies: you know the direction and distance of every creature inside the Veil that has at least 1 Exposure, even if you cannot see them."}, {"name": "Sickening Trail", "prereq": "", "text": "The Veil lingers where you walked — but each creature testifies only once per turn. Spaces you leave during your turn remain Veiled until the start of your next turn. A creature can gain Exposure from only one of your Veil areas per turn."}, {"name": "Static Autopsy", "prereq": "", "text": "Watch the Exposed for one round and learn where they are strongest. After observing a creature with Exposure 3+ for one round, learn whether its highest saving throw is Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, or mental (Int/Wis/Cha)."}, {"name": "Red Star Descent", "prereq": "", "text": "Descend twenty feet and drive the Veil down with you. Prerequisite: Floating Apparition. When you descend at least 20 feet immediately before using Atmospheric Pulse, you may drive the Veil down with you: the Pulse affects only creatures within 10 feet of you, but creatures that fail the save gain 2 Exposure instead of 1."}], "e165": [{"name": "Roofline Hunter", "prereq": "", "text": "Vertical surfaces become roads; the hunt runs up walls. Climbing costs no extra movement and you may run across vertical surfaces during your turn if you end on a legal surface or remain flying."}, {"name": "Hellish Whinny", "prereq": "", "text": "Panic betrays the frightened — direction and distance known for a full minute. When a creature fails its save against Devil’s Cry, its panic betrays it: for 1 minute you always know its direction and distance, and it cannot become hidden from you. This does not let you see it while invisible, but you know which space it occupies."}, {"name": "Near Miss", "prereq": "", "text": "The hunt feeds on near misses — an opportunity attack dodged is Pursuit earned. When a creature misses you with an opportunity attack, gain 1 Pursuit, once per round. The hunt feeds on near misses."}, {"name": "Broken-Bridle Pursuit", "prereq": "", "text": "Restrain the hunter and the hunger only sharpens. Prerequisite: Marked Quarry. When your Quarry imposes restrained, grappled, or prone on you, gain 2 Pursuit after the condition is applied."}], "e166": [{"name": "Polite Stranger", "prereq": "", "text": "The Offer travels by phone, speaker, intercom — a mile of politeness. You may deliver Offer through a phone, speaker, intercom, or other live two-way communication within 1 mile. The target must hear and voluntarily accept."}, {"name": "Take My Hand", "prereq": "", "text": "One more kindness on the menu: stand, and walk ten feet toward the hand that offered. Add one Offer option: the target may stand from prone and move 10 feet toward you without provoking. If accepted, you may move 10 feet toward it as well."}, {"name": "Guest Right", "prereq": "", "text": "Inside a Threshold whose controller invited you, no one surprises you. While inside a Threshold whose controller has invited you, you cannot be surprised, and you sense whenever a creature enters or leaves that Threshold."}, {"name": "The Eyes Are Wrong", "prereq": "", "text": "Two Doors deep, and they can no longer read you — or hide from you. A creature that has granted you 2+ Open Doors has disadvantage on Insight checks against you and cannot benefit from being invisible against your technique senses."}], "e167": [{"name": "Tall Enough", "prereq": "", "text": "Jumps doubled, Large creatures stepped over — the legs keep their own counsel. Your standing jump distance and height double, and you may step over Large or smaller creatures without treating their spaces as difficult terrain."}, {"name": "Walk Behind the Camera", "prereq": "", "text": "Thirty feet through dim light, and the procession vanishes without an action. If you end your turn in dim light or darkness after moving 30+ feet, you may Hide without an action once per round."}, {"name": "Friendly Procession", "prereq": "", "text": "An ally walks the Path; fall in step behind them for fifteen feet. When an ally moves along your Procession Path, you may use your reaction to move up to 15 feet along the same path without provoking opportunity attacks, falling in step behind them."}, {"name": "Dropped Frame", "prereq": "", "text": "An attack misses through Echo disadvantage — the dropped frame becomes a Step. Prerequisite: Processional Echoes. When an attack misses you due to Echo disadvantage, gain 1 Step."}], "e168": [{"name": "Count Again", "prereq": "", "text": "Doubt every face: the next attack rolls at disadvantage. When a creature fails an Insight check to identify you or a decoy, it is left doubting every face: it has disadvantage on its next attack roll before the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Campfire Voice", "prereq": "", "text": "Any voice heard for a minute, reproduced perfectly — though mimicry alone buys no Headcount. You can perfectly reproduce any voice heard for at least 1 minute, though this alone never grants a Headcount benefit."}, {"name": "Wrong Footprints", "prereq": "", "text": "Sixty feet of false evidence, laid for a Headcount creature. As an action and 1 CE, create false tracks, scent, and mundane evidence for one Headcount creature across a 60-foot trail."}, {"name": "Seventh Shadow", "prereq": "", "text": "The decoy may Help once — and is destroyed by its own usefulness. Prerequisite: There Were Six of Us. Your decoy may take the Help action once on your turn; doing so destroys it after the helped roll resolves."}], "e169": [{"name": "Livestock Sense", "prereq": "", "text": "Smell tells you who carries CE, and who is below half. You can determine whether a creature you can smell within 30 feet currently has CE and whether it is above or below half HP."}, {"name": "Spraying Wound", "prereq": "", "text": "A critical hit marks a second creature for free — the wound sprays. Once per turn, when you score a critical hit with a piercing or slashing melee attack, you may mark a second creature within 5 feet of the target with a Feeding Wound without spending CE; it counts against your maximum active wounds."}, {"name": "Packless Hunter", "prereq": "", "text": "Alone, the solitude becomes a weapon — drive the wounded from the herd. When no ally is within 15 feet of you, your solitude is a weapon: once per turn when you hit a wounded creature, you may drive it from the herd. It makes a Wisdom saving throw against your technique DC, becoming frightened of you until the end of your next turn on a failure."}, {"name": "Purging Molt", "prereq": "", "text": "Regress one stage to slough tainted flesh — the molt purges poison and disease. As an action, regress one stage on the Metamorphosis track (minimum Gaunt Predator) to slough tainted flesh: end one poisoned condition or disease affecting you."}], "e170": [{"name": "Sand Listener", "prereq": "", "text": "Press yourself to a segment and read its memory: number, size, direction. As an action, press yourself to one of your Tremor Path segments and read its memory: learn the number, size categories, and direction of travel of creatures that crossed that segment in the last 10 minutes."}, {"name": "False Tremor", "prereq": "", "text": "A fake signature within sixty feet — the desert learns to lie. As an action and 1 CE, create a fake Path signature within 60 feet that lasts 10 minutes and fools ordinary tremor detection."}, {"name": "Venom Static", "prereq": "", "text": "Acid and lightning in one round — the nerves short-circuit, and reactions die. When one creature takes both acid and lightning damage from you in the same round, its nerves short-circuit: it cannot take reactions until the start of your next turn."}, {"name": "Buried Ambush", "prereq": "", "text": "Combat begins while you are underground — the first strike lands before the first round. If combat begins while you are underground in one of your existing Paths, you may spend 1 CE to Erupt against a creature within 10 feet of your position before the first round begins, resolving the attack before initiative order starts."}], "e171": [{"name": "Ambush Sign", "prereq": "", "text": "Designate ten feet of False Trail as the ambush point — the rumor bites. When you create a False Trail, you may designate one 10-foot segment of it as your ambush point. The first hostile creature to willingly enter that segment provokes an opportunity attack from you if you are hidden within 10 feet of it."}, {"name": "Tree Line", "prereq": "", "text": "Climb at full speed; the high branches grant half cover. You may climb natural surfaces at full speed and gain half cover while at least 10 feet above the ground among dense branches/foliage."}, {"name": "No Clear Photo", "prereq": "", "text": "Divination, camera, scope, recorder — all must beat your DC while you hold Evidence. A creature using a divination, camera, scope, or recording device to identify you must beat your CE DC with its relevant check if you have at least 1 Evidence."}, {"name": "Track the Tracker", "prereq": "", "text": "Whoever tracks you grants Evidence — and tells you where they are for an hour. When a creature succeeds on tracking you and grants Evidence, learn its direction and approximate distance for 1 hour."}], "e172": [{"name": "Shiny Eyes", "prereq": "", "text": "Dim light at your choosing — and the invisible are seen within the swarm. The swarm sheds dim light 10 feet when you choose and can see invisible creatures within its space."}, {"name": "Roof Scratcher", "prereq": "", "text": "What scratches above makes the first attack below go wide. A creature starting its turn directly beneath the swarm on a ceiling makes Wisdom save or has disadvantage on its first attack that turn."}, {"name": "Tiny Thieves", "prereq": "", "text": "Grab learns to take the small and the precious — never the attuned, never the armor. Grab may target a worn pouch, keyring, magazine, potion, phone, talisman, or similarly small accessible object, but never armor, an attuned item, or an object physically integrated into the target."}, {"name": "No Bodies Found", "prereq": "", "text": "The swarm leaves no corpse — only one last delivery, sixty feet out. When the swarm disperses, it leaves no corpse or permanent material — and it may complete one last delivery: it deposits one object it is holding in an unoccupied space within 60 feet of its position before vanishing."}], "e173": [{"name": "Snake Crown", "prereq": "", "text": "The snakes lend their senses: blindsight, and Perception by vibration and scent. You gain blindsight 10 feet from the snakes’ senses and advantage on Perception based on vibration or scent."}, {"name": "Do Not Look Away", "prereq": "", "text": "The averted retreat; you follow ten feet for one CE. When an Averting creature voluntarily moves away from you, use reaction and 1 CE to move 10 feet toward it."}, {"name": "Mirror-Bearer", "prereq": "", "text": "One touched weapon, shield, or object becomes a polished reflection. You can make one weapon, shield, or carried object you touch count as a polished reflection for Bronze Reflection."}, {"name": "Cracking Stone", "prereq": "", "text": "When another's attack strikes the calcified — shatter the shell on reaction. Prerequisite: Calcification 3. Once per round, when a creature with Calcification 3+ is hit by an attack you did not make, you may use your reaction to shatter its calcifying shell: it sheds 1 Calcification and falls prone. This may spare an ally from petrification — or deny an enemy its stony armor — without spending your own attack."}], "e174": [{"name": "Swamp-Born", "prereq": "", "text": "The hydra's native element: water, where her wounds are safe from the flame. You gain a swim speed equal to your walking speed and can hold your breath for 1 hour. While fully submerged, fire and radiant damage lose their cauterizing edge: a Neck Wound marked on a turn you end underwater cannot be cauterized until after your next turn begins, giving the regrowth time to root. As a bonus action while submerged, you may spend 1 CE to exhale venom-tinged murk into a 15-foot radius around you, heavily obscuring it until the start of your next turn."}, {"name": "Guarding Heads", "prereq": "", "text": "A neck interposed for another — the garrison's duty turned outward. When an adjacent ally is hit, spend 1 Head Die and reaction to reduce its damage by the die + CON modifier."}, {"name": "Venom Reservoir", "prereq": "", "text": "Venom as a leash: the slowed, the tracked, the held. A creature poisoned by your Hydra Venom also has its speed reduced by 10 feet. Your necks track the venom's spread through the victim's body: your Bite's reach extends by 5 feet against a poisoned creature, and when it tries to move away from you, you may spend 1 CE as a reaction to force a Strength saving throw — on a failure its movement ends immediately. The speed penalty and the leash both end when the poison ends."}, {"name": "Heracles Problem", "prereq": "", "text": "Spite, formalized: the enemy is punished for thinking like Heracles. When an enemy deals fire/radiant damage solely to cauterize a pending Neck Wound, gain one Head Die of temporary HP after that damage resolves."}], "e175": [{"name": "Weigh the Dead", "prereq": "", "text": "Even the dead can be weighed — a corpse's heaviest bargain, read within the hour. As an action and 2 CE, you may Weigh the heart of a corpse dead no more than 1 hour; it makes no save. You learn one significant burden it knowingly accepted in life — a bargain, betrayal, or sacrifice — as the GM describes. This offers no Temptations and adds no Heart Weight."}, {"name": "Sweet Temptation", "prereq": "", "text": "A fifth boon, offered in the moment of harm: Safety, which halves damage at the price of one Weight. Add Safety: when you or an ally within 30 feet would take damage from the Weighed creature, you may offer it Safety as a Temptation without spending an action (once per round). Accept: the damage is halved and it gains 1 Heart Weight. Refuse: the damage lands in full."}, {"name": "Borrow the Burden", "prereq": "", "text": "The sorcerer takes an ally's Weight as his own — generosity as damage control. When an ally within 30 feet accepts a Temptation, you may take the Heart Weight instead of them once per round. Temptations accepted by the hostile Weighed creature (such as Safety) do not trigger this feat — it covers allies’ acceptances only."}, {"name": "Devour Excess", "prereq": "", "text": "A target at maximum Weight leaks power with every great expenditure; the scale drinks it as temporary CE. When a 6-Weight creature spends 3+ CE, gain 1 temporary CE, maximum PB temporary CE, expiring after 1 minute. Temporary CE never raises your CE maximum."}], "e176": [{"name": "Iron Appetite", "prereq": "", "text": "Even under Tyr's Hand, self-healing is possible — at a surcharge. While obeying Tyr’s Hand, healing you grant yourself through RCT is not prohibited, but costs +1 CE."}, {"name": "Moon-Eater", "prereq": "", "text": "Snap Moon Chain and bite the backlash: the overspender takes five psychic for its extravagance. When Moon Chain breaks, you may use your reaction to bite the backlash: the creature whose action triggered the break takes 5 psychic damage as the snapped chain lashes through its overspent cursed energy."}, {"name": "Slipped Leash", "prereq": "", "text": "A saved hold becomes a ten-foot slip — the failed leash turned into distance. When you succeed on a saving throw against a grapple, restraint, or forced-movement effect, you may use your reaction to move up to 10 feet without provoking opportunity attacks, slipping through the failed hold."}, {"name": "Unbroken Oath", "prereq": "", "text": "Finish an encounter unbroken, and earn the right to ignore one trigger next time — discipline, rewarded in kind. If you complete an encounter without breaking a prepared Bond, choose one of your prepared Bonds. The next time that Bond’s trigger occurs, you may keep it unbroken instead of breaking it; you gain no Ragnarök from the ignored trigger."}], "e177": [{"name": "Ocean Coil", "prereq": "", "text": "Jörmungandr's home water: segments on the sea, and a swimmer's speed. Segments may be placed on water and you gain swim speed equal walking speed."}, {"name": "Tail Around the Party", "prereq": "", "text": "Guard Rings that steady allies against forced movement across their line. Guard Rings grant allies advantage on saves against forced movement across their boundary."}, {"name": "Venom of the World", "prereq": "", "text": "Venom beyond immunity: the immune treat it as resistance. Poison immunity treats your Coil poison as resistance; poison resistance still functions normally."}, {"name": "Closing Snap", "prereq": "", "text": "The completed circuit bites — a hostile pulled ten feet toward the Ring's center on a failed Strength save. When a Segment you place completes a Ring, the circuit closes with a snap: one hostile creature of your choice inside the new Ring makes a Strength saving throw against your technique DC; on a failure it is pulled 10 feet toward the Ring’s center."}], "e178": [{"name": "Perfect Accent", "prereq": "", "text": "An hour of listening buys the accent flawless — though not the language beneath it. After listening to a language for 1 hour through a recorded Mask, you can reproduce its accent flawlessly but do not learn the language itself."}, {"name": "Dinner Guest", "prereq": "", "text": "Where the identity is expected, casual scrutiny slides off — until she behaves out of character. While impersonating someone inside a place where that identity is expected, gain advantage on checks to avoid casual scrutiny until you behave obviously out of character."}, {"name": "Backward Hands", "prereq": "", "text": "A failed Sleight or Deception reads the room for her: she learns exactly who is suspicious. Once per round, when you fail a Sleight of Hand or Deception check while masked, the Mask reads the room: you immediately learn which creatures that witnessed the check are suspicious of you."}, {"name": "Predator’s Memory", "prereq": "", "text": "One social note per Mask — a routine, a title, a public preference — carried without secret knowledge. You can store one additional purely social Memory Note per Mask: a public relationship, routine, title, or preference you personally observed. It grants no secret knowledge."}], "e179": [{"name": "Rain-Bringer", "prereq": "", "text": "The naga's weather: light rain for ten minutes, quenching flame and finding water. As an action and 1 CE, create light rain in a 30-foot radius for 10 minutes; it extinguishes mundane flame and gives advantage on Survival to find water."}, {"name": "Jeweled Hood", "prereq": "", "text": "She senses around every coiled creature — ten-foot blindsight centered on each bearer, and no surprise from within. While at least one of your Coils is active, you sense the space around every Coil-bearing creature: you have blindsight to 10 feet centered on each creature bearing one of your Coils, and you cannot be surprised by a creature within that radius."}, {"name": "Constriction Expert", "prereq": "", "text": "A Constrict Coil spent to anchor: forced movement negated entirely, by her reaction. When a creature bearing one of your Constrict Coils would be forcibly moved, you can use your reaction to spend that Coil and anchor it in place, negating the movement entirely."}, {"name": "Shared Skin", "prereq": "", "text": "Ward Coils passed hand to hand — a willing bearer may give the coil to another willing creature within thirty feet. As a bonus action, a willing creature bearing one of your Ward Coils can pass it to another willing creature within 30 feet; the Coil keeps its remaining duration."}], "e180": [{"name": "Fox Bridegroom", "prereq": "", "text": "The liar's craft: Deception mastered, and cosmetic shapechanging at will. Gain proficiency or expertise in Deception; harmless cosmetic shapechanging can alter hair, eyes, ears, tail, and clothing appearance at will."}, {"name": "Blue Foxfire", "prereq": "", "text": "A wisp kindled in a Paper Fox's space — the first lured soul hears an ally's voice in the flame. You may kindle a foxfire wisp in the space of one of your Paper Foxes. The first creature that becomes lured by that wisp regards you as a trusted ally while lured, hearing an ally’s voice calling from the flame."}, {"name": "Clever Enough to Believe Yourself", "prereq": "", "text": "Frightened or charmed, she may pass the condition to a Paper Fox — the illusion believes the lie instead. When you fail a save against being frightened or charmed, you may use your reaction and spend 1 CE to make one of your Paper Foxes within 30 feet believe the lie instead: the condition ends on you and the illusion is destroyed."}, {"name": "Thousand-Year Trick", "prereq": "", "text": "At eleventh level, even a discovered illusion pays: the wasted inspection counts as fuel for the next claim. Prerequisite: level 11. The first time each round a creature identifies one of your illusions, you may treat that wasted inspection as fuel: it counts as a deception that wasted an action for the purpose of claiming your next lie."}], "e181": [{"name": "Bone Chime", "prereq": "", "text": "He hears the half-dead: creatures below half HP within thirty feet, if they have bones to rattle. You can sense creatures below half HP within 30 feet if they have bones or a comparable internal structure."}, {"name": "Graveyard Architecture", "prereq": "", "text": "The Torso anchors to terrain — structure, cover, and a climb for allies. Torso of a Nation may anchor to terrain and counts as a structure for allies using cover or climbing."}, {"name": "Starving Maw", "prereq": "", "text": "Starvation damage may be passed to a Jaw-grappled victim — the skeleton gnawing through its own hunger. When you would take starvation damage for ending your turn at Hunger cap, you may instead force one creature grappled by your Jaw to take that damage as necrotic, your manifested skeleton gnawing through its own hunger. The grapple continues."}, {"name": "Jaw of Famine", "prereq": "", "text": "End a Jaw grapple to feed: one Hunger and five temporary HP from the released meal. As a bonus action while a creature is grappled by your Jaw, you may end the grapple to feed: gain 1 Hunger and temporary HP equal to 5."}], "e182": [{"name": "Zal’s Feather", "prereq": "", "text": "The rescue that refuses the margin: once per long rest, a feather spent to leave a fallen ally at one HP instead of zero. Once per long rest, when a creature within 30 feet would fall to 0 HP, consume any Feather to leave it at 1 HP instead. This cannot prevent instant death that does not reduce HP."}, {"name": "Scholar of Ages", "prereq": "", "text": "The archive's other wing: History or Medicine mastered, and Skill Feathers spendable on either. Gain proficiency or expertise in History or Medicine. A Skill Feather may be spent on either of those skills regardless of how it was created."}, {"name": "Carry the Young", "prereq": "", "text": "The wings bear a passenger: one willing creature of her size or smaller, carried without slowing. While flying, you may carry one willing creature of your size or smaller without reducing your speed."}, {"name": "Memory of Fire", "prereq": "", "text": "Survival itself may be recorded: a save against fire, fear, or death becomes an instant Resolve Feather. When a willing creature within 60 feet fails a save against fire, fear, or death effects, you may use your reaction and spend 1 CE to record the moment of survival: create one Resolve Feather immediately (once per round, still subject to your cap)."}], "e183": [{"name": "Polyphonic Horror", "prereq": "", "text": "Two phenomena failed in one round earn a Wisdom save against fright — the storm speaking with many throats. When a creature fails saves against two different Typhon phenomena in one round, you may use your reaction and spend 1 Cataclysm to force it to make a Wisdom save against your CE DC; on a failure it is frightened of you until the end of its next turn, as the storm speaks with many throats."}, {"name": "Tireless Coils", "prereq": "", "text": "Drive the limbs into the ground: immobile, immovable, and advantaged on shoves and grapples until his next turn. As a bonus action, you can drive your serpent limbs into the ground: until the start of your next turn you cannot move, but you cannot be moved against your will and you have advantage on Strength checks and saves to shove or grapple."}, {"name": "Volcanic Prison", "prereq": "", "text": "Two Cataclysm and a grappled foe buy cooling magma — restrained, burning, until the end of its next turn. As an action while a creature is grappled by your Serpent Limbs, you may spend 2 Cataclysm to encase it in cooling magma: it must succeed on a Strength save against your CE DC or be restrained until the end of your next turn, taking 1 fire die at the start of each of its turns while restrained."}, {"name": "Last Challenge of Olympus (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The death he refuses quietly: at zero HP, erupt — every Cataclysm spent as a die of fire, lightning, or thunder in fifteen feet, before he falls. When you drop to 0 HP, you may use your reaction to spend any amount of Cataclysm and erupt: each creature within 15 feet must make a Dexterity save against your CE DC, taking 1 fire, lightning, or thunder die per Cataclysm spent (your choice) on a failure, half on success. You then fall unconscious as normal."}], "e184": [{"name": "Ambidexterity Is Meaningless", "prereq": "", "text": "Hands may be committed to the Help action — a different ally aided per Hand, within thirty feet. You can commit Hands to the Help action: each committed Hand aids a different creature you can see within 30 feet, granting the aid's benefit on the first attack roll or ability check that creature makes before the start of your next turn."}, {"name": "Jailor of Titans", "prereq": "", "text": "Two twenty-foot spectral grapples maintained at once, each paid and contested separately. You can maintain two 20-foot spectral grapples at once, paying the normal Hand cost for each and making separate contested checks for each."}, {"name": "Catch the Sky", "prereq": "", "text": "The defensive reaction extends to the sky: ranged technique attacks parried from thirty feet. defensive Hand reaction can protect against ranged technique attacks from 30 ft."}, {"name": "Briarean Barrage (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The Hands may fuse into one massive fist: a single thirty-foot melee strike, a Hand Die per Hand spent, and a Strength save or prone. When you use Stone Barrage, you may instead fuse the Hands into one massive fist: make a single melee technique attack with 30-foot reach, dealing one Hand Die per Hand spent plus your CE modifier once; on a hit the target must succeed on a Strength save against your CE DC or be knocked prone."}], "e185": [{"name": "Appraiser's Eye", "prereq": "", "text": "The dragon knows her gold: a bonus action's appraisal of value, CE, and curse — and a mark placed in the same motion. As a bonus action, you may appraise one object you can see within 30 feet, learning its approximate value, whether it bears cursed energy, and whether it shows signs of a curse, binding, or forgery. If the object is eligible to become a Hoard Mark, you may immediately mark it with Covetous Scale as part of the same bonus action, still paying the 1 CE. Once per long rest, you may appraise a cursed tool worn or carried by a creature this way, reading its nature despite its keeper."}, {"name": "Jealous Wings", "prereq": "", "text": "Two Greed in Wyrm Shape buy jealous wings — thirty feet of flight until the end of her next turn. While in Wyrm Shape, you may spend 2 Greed as a bonus action to unfurl jealous wings, gaining 30-foot flight until the end of your next turn."}, {"name": "No Thief Escapes", "prereq": "", "text": "The hunt shared: allies perceive the golden thread to the thief and may spend reactions to pursue. Once per round when Dragon's Claim reveals a thief's direction, you may spend 1 CE as a bonus action to share the hunt: your allies perceive a glinting golden thread pointing at the thief until the start of your next turn, and each may use their reaction to move up to half their speed toward it."}, {"name": "Accursed Gold (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "One Greed makes a stolen Mark unbearably heavy — the carrier's speed halved until it drops the prize. As a bonus action, you may spend 1 Greed to make one stolen Hoard Mark within your Claim's 1-hour window unbearably heavy: the carrier's speed is halved while it carries the mark, until it drops it."}], "e186": [{"name": "Burial Goods", "prereq": "", "text": "A second, portable Anchor — a five-pound burial token — though only one projects the Mound at a time; destroy it and he bleeds psychic per Restlessness held. You may maintain a second, portable Grave Anchor — a sealed burial token weighing 5 lb — alongside your main Anchor, though only one Anchor projects your Grave Mound at a time; switching which Anchor projects the Mound costs a bonus action and 1 CE. A hostile creature that moves while carrying or touching the portable Anchor generates Restlessness for you as though it were moving inside your guarded space, rewarding the thief's greed. If the portable Anchor is destroyed, you take psychic damage equal to one Grave Die per Restlessness you hold, up to a number of dice equal to your PB."}, {"name": "Anchor's Pull", "prereq": "", "text": "One Restlessness on an opportunity attack drags the victim ten feet toward the Anchor instead of dealing damage. When you hit a creature with an opportunity attack, you may spend 1 Restlessness to drag it 10 feet toward your Grave Anchor instead of dealing damage; a creature that enters your guarded space this way generates Restlessness as normal."}, {"name": "Corpse Weight", "prereq": "", "text": "While swollen, he counts one size larger for carrying, grapples, and forced movement. count one size larger for carrying/grapple/forced movement while swollen."}, {"name": "Unquiet Dead (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "Too Angry to Die infects the field: hostiles within fifteen feet save or fear him until the end of his next turn. When Too Angry to Die triggers, your rage infects the field: each hostile creature within 15 feet must succeed on a Wisdom save against your CE DC or be frightened of you until the end of your next turn."}], "e187": [{"name": "Winged Escort", "prereq": "", "text": "Flight that carries: one willing creature borne without slowing, half cover from below, and Ride to the Fallen extended to thirty feet. When you fly — under your own power or by Carry from the Field — you may carry one willing creature without any reduction to your flying speed. While carrying a creature this way, your Ride to the Fallen reaction move extends to 30 feet toward a Deed-holder, and the carried creature gains half cover against attacks made from below you. You cannot carry a creature larger than you or heavier than your carrying capacity."}, {"name": "Saga-Keeper", "prereq": "", "text": "Her own legend recorded: her crits, her brushes with death, her rescues — Deeds stored under her own name. You may record Deeds from your own dramatic moments — your critical hits, your brushes with death, your rescues — as though you were one of the allies you watch; these Deeds are stored under your name and spent normally."}, {"name": "Shieldmaiden", "prereq": "", "text": "Interposition over absorption: Ride to the Fallen may impose disadvantage on the triggering attack instead — or grant advantage on a save against a non-attack effect. When you use Ride to the Fallen, you may forgo the damage reduction to instead impose disadvantage on the triggering attack roll, decided before the roll is made — your interposition ruins the strike's line rather than absorbing it. If the attack still hits, you may still spend the creature's Deed after damage is rolled to reduce it by one die + your CE modifier, completing the same 20-foot reaction move. Against effects that call for a saving throw instead of an attack roll, you may grant the protected creature advantage on the save instead."}, {"name": "Last Seat in Valhalla (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "At eleventh level, a spent Deed buys a rerolled death save — the ally uses the new result. When an ally fails a death save, you may spend one of their Deeds as a reaction to let them reroll it; they use the new result."}], "e188": [{"name": "Footprints Vanish", "prereq": "", "text": "The assassin's passage: no tracks in snow, advantage on Stealth in the cold, silent arrivals, and invisibility beyond thirty feet to the unmagical eye while motionless in falling snow. You leave no tracks in snow, ice, or frost that a mundane tracker could follow, and you have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks in cold terrain or inside your Snowfield. When you use Woman in the Storm to teleport between snow-obscured spaces, you arrive without sound: creatures relying on hearing have disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to notice your arrival until you take an action. While you stand motionless in falling snow or a blizzard, you are treated as invisible to creatures more than 30 feet away that lack magical sight."}, {"name": "Kiss of Winter", "prereq": "", "text": "A mercy for the willing: one CE and a brow-kiss buys immunity to Frost and easy passage through her Snowfield until the end of her next turn. As a bonus action for 1 CE, you can press a winter's kiss to a willing creature's brow: until the end of your next turn it ignores Frost accumulation and treats your Snowfield as normal terrain."}, {"name": "Snowblind", "prereq": "", "text": "At two Frost, her reaction may blind the victim with driven snow until the end of its next turn. When a creature reaches 2 Frost, you may use your reaction to blind it with driven snow until the end of its next turn unless it succeeds on a Constitution save against your CE DC."}, {"name": "First Flurry (6+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The battle's opening chill: at initiative, one creature within thirty feet saves or begins the fight at one Frost. When you roll initiative, you may fling the battle's first chill: one creature you can see within 30 feet must succeed on a Constitution save against your CE DC or gain 1 Frost."}], "e189": [{"name": "Iron Skin", "prereq": "", "text": "The Blue Mask's mercy: the wall steps in front of its own people. I have watched the bruiser take a companion's wound and stand under it — the mask's endurance is not selfishness but stewardship. The mountain does not move; it lets the storm break on itself. While wearing the Blue Mask, when an ally within 10 feet takes physical damage you may use your reaction to interpose yourself: you take the damage instead, reduced by your Blue Mask's damage reduction."}, {"name": "Red Horn", "prereq": "", "text": "The Red Mask's charge, given a crown. Mark this: fifteen feet of straight-line intent before the hit — the technique rewards the sorcerer who commits without flinching. Force announced, force delivered; the prone enemy is the period at the end of the sentence. While wearing the Red Mask, if you move at least 15 feet straight toward a creature before hitting it with a melee attack, the target must succeed on a Strength save against your CE DC or be knocked prone."}, {"name": "Dread Laugh", "prereq": "", "text": "The Black Mask laughs, and the battlefield leans away. This is terror as distance: one creature, thirty feet, hears the laugh and forgets how to approach. No damage dealt, no blood drawn — the fight is won in the half-turn of a heel. While wearing the Black Mask, you may use your bonus action to laugh: one creature within 30 feet that can hear you must succeed on a Wisdom save against your CE DC or be unable to move closer to you until the end of your next turn."}, {"name": "Parade Master (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The dancer enters his own chorus line. By merging with one of his spectral oni, he wears two masks at once — two negotiations with his own myth, settled simultaneously. The price is the silhouette itself; the technique understands that a second face is worth a sacrificed body. As a bonus action, you may merge with one of your spectral oni silhouettes within 30 feet: until the start of your next turn you gain the benefits of a second Mask of your choice in addition to the one you wear; the silhouette is consumed."}], "e190": [{"name": "Silk Architect", "prereq": "", "text": "The web learns to walk. By anchoring a thread to a willing creature instead of stone, the spider takes its toll road with it — the line moves with its bearer, and the spinner always knows where the road leads. Terrain was never the point; the claim was. When you create Anchor Threads, you may anchor one end to a willing creature within 30 feet instead of a surface; the thread moves with the creature, and you always know its direction and distance while the thread lasts."}, {"name": "Tremor Reader", "prereq": "", "text": "Touch the web and you hear through it. Every anchor becomes an ear; every crossing becomes a footstep the spinner reads. I have watched prey tiptoe across a battlefield they thought was empty. The Tsuchigumo heard each toe, and smiled from the ceiling. While you are touching one of your Anchor Threads, you gain blindsight with a 10-foot radius centered on every anchor connected to that thread, reading movement through the web as though you stood at each anchor. A creature moving inside this tremor-sense cannot benefit from being unseen against your thread-snapping reactions. The sense is passive, but it ends for any anchor whose thread is cut or dismissed."}, {"name": "Spider Drop", "prereq": "", "text": "The ceiling hunter's punctuation. Drop ten feet onto the prey and let the landing be the argument — prone and grappled, crushed by the weight of the geometry above. The spider does not dive. It collects. When you drop at least 10 feet from the ceiling onto a creature, you may forgo your attack to land on it instead: it must succeed on a Strength save against your CE DC or be knocked prone and grappled by you."}, {"name": "Eightfold Knot (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The trap learns to travel. Collapsed into a portable snare, the Loom Trap is carried like a folded letter and thrown like a verdict — the triangle opens wherever it lands. Patience, it turns out, can be packed. As an action, you may collapse a Loom Trap into a portable snare that lasts 1 hour; as a bonus action you can throw it at a point within 30 feet to instantly reform the trap there."}], "e191": [{"name": "Monkey's Cunning", "prereq": "", "text": "Precision is the monkey's sacrament. Sleight of hand as expertise, the fine theft as a bonus action — lock, purse, component, gone. Mark this: the chimera's smallest animal is its most dangerous thief. Fury announces itself; fingers do not. While the Monkey aspect is active, you gain proficiency in Sleight of Hand, or expertise if you are already proficient. You may perform one fine-manipulation object interaction — picking a lock, palming a component, cutting a purse — as a bonus action instead of an action, and creatures have disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to notice it while you remain in Monkey aspect. The aspect's precision is in the hands, not just the eyes."}, {"name": "Tiger's Pounce", "prereq": "", "text": "The charge, crowned. Fifteen feet of straight-line intent, a melee hit, and the enemy must hold its footing against the tiger — prone on failure, pushed on success. The pounce is the one honest part of a fight: it tells you exactly where it lands, and lands anyway. While the Tiger aspect is active, when you hit a creature with a melee attack after moving at least 15 feet straight toward it, you may force it to make a Strength saving throw against your technique DC. On a failure it is knocked prone; on a success it is pushed 5 feet away from you. You may use this once per turn, and it has no effect on a creature two or more sizes larger than you."}, {"name": "Serpent's Patience", "prereq": "", "text": "The coil's slow verdict. A grapple, tightened by contest into a restraint, and the serpent's reach becomes a sentence: held, squeezed, one die at a time. Patience is the register here — the serpent does not hurry the end. The end is already decided; the coil is only being polite about it. While the Serpent aspect is active, when you have a creature grappled you may use your action to make a contested grapple check; on a success the grapple tightens into a restraint as your coils lock, lasting until the grapple ends or you change Aspect. A restrained creature takes 1d8 of bludgeoning damage (invented) at the start of each of its turns while the restraint holds. Changing Aspect ends the restraint but not the underlying grapple."}, {"name": "Tanuki Mist", "prereq": "", "text": "Elusiveness, worn like weather. Hide in mist, foliage, snow, or dim light — and if the turn ends hidden and unattacked, drift ten feet without breaking the veil. The tanuki is the chimera's apology to stealth: even the beast that cannot settle can be, briefly, nowhere. While the Tanuki aspect is active, you may attempt to Hide even when only lightly obscured by natural phenomena — mist, foliage, falling snow, or dim light. If you end your turn hidden this way without having attacked, you may move up to 10 feet without breaking hiding, your Tanuki swiftness carrying you between cover. Creatures have disadvantage on checks to track you by scent or sound while you remain hidden under this feat."}], "e192": [{"name": "Feather Shield", "prereq": "", "text": "A feather interposed between an ally and the blow. One Pinion, one reaction, +2 AC — decided after the roll, before the result; and if the feather turns the strike, it returns to the wing unspent. The technique's thrift is exact: mercy given is mercy that comes home. When an ally within 15 feet is targeted by an attack, you may use your reaction and spend 1 Pinion to interpose a shield of pinion feathers, granting the ally +2 AC against that attack. Decide after seeing the attack roll but before knowing the result. If the attack misses because of this bonus, the feather returns to your wings and you regain the spent Pinion, up to your maximum."}, {"name": "Sky Ferry", "prereq": "", "text": "The rescuer as transport. Carry one willing creature at full speed, and let them strike from above on your movement — one attack or cantrip, reaction-spent, the sky as a gun platform. The movement still draws opportunity attacks; the technique protects the passenger, not the itinerary. While flying with your Golden Pinions, you may carry one willing creature without reducing your flying speed. The carried creature may use its reaction during your movement to make one attack or cast a cantrip, striking from above; your movement still provokes opportunity attacks as normal. If you are forced to land while carrying a creature, you may spend 1 Pinion as a reaction to glide it safely to the ground within 15 feet of you, negating its falling damage."}, {"name": "Venom Breaker", "prereq": "", "text": "The reflex sharpens. Enemy of Venom now reaches disease and corrosive ongoing effects where appropriate — the Garuda's enmity is not limited to the listed bindings. A rescuer who has learned what a cage is recognizes every new one on sight. Enemy of Venom can apply to disease/corrosive ongoing effects when appropriate."}, {"name": "Solar Plumage (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The sun takes over the paperwork. Begin the turn in direct sunlight and the cleansing is free — poisoned or restrained ended without spending Pinions. Mark this: the technique's oldest ally is the light itself. The wings were always the sun's idea. When you start your turn in direct sunlight, you may end the poisoned or restrained condition on yourself without spending Pinions, as the sun's light does the cleansing for you."}], "e193": [{"name": "Light-Eater", "prereq": "", "text": "The eaten light is weaponized. When Swallow the Light kills a source, the bonus action turns the corpse of it against one creature within thirty feet — blinded until the end of its next turn. The Serpent wastes nothing; even the dark's leavings are spent. When Swallow the Light extinguishes a light source, you may use your bonus action to weaponize the eaten light: one creature within 30 feet that you can see must succeed on a Constitution save against your CE DC or be blinded until the end of your next turn."}, {"name": "Endless Coil", "prereq": "", "text": "At Depth 3 the coil strikes from anywhere the dark has already won. Originate the attack from any dimness or darkness you created within sixty feet — the serpent's body is wherever the night is. Distance, to this technique, is a rumor. At Depth 3, your Coil of Night can strike through darkness itself: you may originate the attack from any dimness or darkness you created within 60 feet instead of from yourself."}, {"name": "Enemy of Sunrise", "prereq": "", "text": "The light-bringer is answered. When radiant reduces your Depth, the reaction lashes back — two Night Dice of necrotic on a failed Constitution save. Mark this: the Serpent does not merely endure the sun's allies. It bills them. When a radiant effect reduces your Night Depth, you may use your reaction to lash back at the light-bringer: it must succeed on a Constitution save against your CE DC or take 2 Night Dice necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Chaos Before Creation (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The night's dregs, spent instead of surrendered. The first time each long rest your Depth would fall to 0, extinguish every light within thirty feet and blind the chosen within fifteen. This is the oldest lesson the myth carries: even the defeated night gets one last refusal. The first time each long rest your Night Depth would fall to 0, you may unleash its dregs instead: every light source within 30 feet is extinguished, and each creature of your choice within 15 feet must succeed on a Constitution save against your CE DC or be blinded until the end of your next turn. Your Depth becomes 0 afterward."}], "e194": [{"name": "Lion's Pursuit", "prereq": "", "text": "The hunt leaves fire behind. At Heat 3+, the Dash lays a five-foot trail of flame — the lioness's passage, still burning for the next turn's trespassers. I have watched prey realize too late that the road behind the predator is as dangerous as the predator. At Heat 3+, when you take the Dash action you may leave a 5-foot-wide trail of fire along your path: creatures that enter it before the start of your next turn take 1 fire die."}, {"name": "Red Beer Ritual", "prereq": "", "text": "The draught, shared. Administer the Blood-Red Draught to an adjacent willing ally — they take the healing and the cooling of fear, while your Heat still falls by 3. The ritual's cooling passes through another's body. Mark this: the Fever's mercy was always meant to be handed to someone. You may administer your Blood-Red Draught to an adjacent willing ally instead of drinking it yourself: the ally gains the healing (1 die + your CE modifier) and the end of the frightened condition, while your Heat still falls by 3 as the ritual's cooling passes through another's body. A use spent this way counts against your once-per-short-rest limit, and the ally must drink as part of your action. You cannot split a single draught's effects between two creatures."}, {"name": "Fever Claw", "prereq": "", "text": "The plague, delivered by hand. One CE on a melee hit and the target's healing is reduced as though it had breathed the pestilence. The claw is the technique's shorthand — no cone, no ceremony, just the fever passed skin to skin. When you hit a creature with a melee attack, you may spend 1 CE to deliver your plague by claw: the target's healing is reduced by your PB until the end of your next turn, as with Breath of Pestilence."}, {"name": "Two Faces of the Sun (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The Maximum's hinge. Once during its three rounds, switch between Slaughter and Mercy as a bonus action — Heat snapping to 5 or 0 to match. The sun turns its other face mid-battle. I have seen the switch end fights: the enemy braces for the furnace and meets the healer, or braces for the healer and meets the furnace. Once during your Maximum's 3-round duration, you may switch between Slaughter and Mercy as a bonus action, the sun turning its other face. Your Heat immediately becomes 5 for Slaughter or 0 for Mercy to match the new mode, and the spent round still counts toward the duration. You cannot switch again for the rest of the Maximum."}], "e195": [{"name": "Lantern Eyes", "prereq": "", "text": "The Head's lantern burns through concealment. Darkvision to one hundred twenty feet, invisible things seen within ten — and advantage on sight-based Perception while the senses ride the Head. The dullahan's passengers are never lost; the lantern has their names. Your detached spectral Head gains darkvision out to 120 feet and can see invisible creatures and objects within 10 feet of it, its lantern-light burning through concealment. While your sight and hearing originate from the Head, you have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight. If the Head is destroyed while you are seeing through it, you are blinded until the end of your next turn as your senses snap violently back to your body."}, {"name": "Unbroken Gallop", "prereq": "", "text": "Momentum refuses interruption. When forcibly moved, spend 1 Gallop as a reaction and the movement becomes 0 — the steed's straight line carries through. I have watched the rider hold his course through effects that would uproot a siege engine. Inevitability does not sidestep. When you would be forcibly moved, you may spend 1 Gallop as a reaction to refuse it: the forced movement becomes 0 as your steed's momentum carries straight through."}, {"name": "Death Coach", "prereq": "", "text": "The journey takes a passenger. One willing ally rides with the steed, sharing its movement — Gallop-fueled charges, Unbroken Gallop's refusals — and gaining half cover against attack. This is the technique's one courtesy: the herald's road has room for two. While your Black Steed is manifested, it may carry one willing ally in addition to you, and the ally shares your movement — including Gallop-fueled charges and Unbroken Gallop's refusal of forced movement — without costing either of you actions. An ally riding with you gains half cover against attacks coming from the steed's flanks. If the steed is dismissed or you are knocked prone while mounted together, the ally lands safely in an unoccupied adjacent space of its choice."}, {"name": "Last Name Spoken (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The mark is called down the road. One bonus action: the Road's End must save or spend its reaction moving its speed toward the rider by the most direct route. The name is spoken; the feet answer. The rider does not fetch. He summons, and the itinerary does the rest. As a bonus action, you can call your Road's End down the road: it must succeed on a Wisdom save against your CE DC or use its reaction to move up to its speed toward you by the most direct route."}], "e196": [{"name": "Family Wail", "prereq": "", "text": "The watch extends to the chosen. PB allies named after each long rest: the keen's witness range reaches ninety feet for them. Mark this: the technique lets the bearer decide, once, who matters most. Everything after that is the keen's decision, not hers. Choose PB allies after each long rest; your keen’s witness range extends to 90 feet for them."}, {"name": "Glass-Shattering Keen", "prereq": "", "text": "The wail's other talent: fragile things break. Double damage to glass, ceramics, thin wood — windows and pottery shattering on failed saves, carried or worn objects exemptable. The keen is not only grief; it is force, and force has opinions about windows. Your Piercing Wail deals double damage to fragile mundane objects — glass, ceramics, thin wood, and the like — shattering windows and pottery in its cone on a failed save regardless of their remaining hit points. You may exempt objects carried or worn by creatures from the cone's destructive resonance. As a finer application, you may spend 1 CE to narrow the wail to a 15-foot cone that affects only objects, keening the room's glass to shards while leaving every creature untouched."}, {"name": "Professional Mourner", "prereq": "", "text": "The mourner's ledger. Spend a minute keening over an ally the keen could not save: learn the direction and distance of whatever dealt the killing blow, within a mile, and be unsurprisable by it for a day. The apology has a second half, and it is called reckoning. When an ally you keened for dies, you may spend 1 minute keening over the body: you learn the exact direction and distance of whatever dealt the killing blow (if within 1 mile), and you cannot be surprised by it for the next 24 hours."}, {"name": "Second Cry (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The echo, shaped. When the keen fires, 2 CE turns its echo into a warning for one ally within sixty feet — +2 AC until the next turn, because they heard death coming. The first cry was for the fallen. The second is for the living, and it is the kinder of the two. When the keen fires, you may spend 2 CE to shape its echo into a warning for one ally within 60 feet: that ally gains +2 AC until the start of your next turn, having heard death coming."}], "e197": [{"name": "Long Arms", "prereq": "", "text": "The reach plants. While transformed, a bonus action plants Blight by touch within reach — a five-foot patch, one minute. The horse's long arms mean the plague no longer waits for the breath; the field grows wherever the rider passes. While transformed, you may use your bonus action to plant Blight with your long arms: touch a point within your reach to create a 5-foot Blight patch there for 1 minute."}, {"name": "Murrain Wind", "prereq": "", "text": "The plague rides the Dash. Exhale behind while dashing transformed, and a five-foot trail of Blight follows until the next turn. I have watched the rider cross a field and leave it seeded. Speed was always the plague's favorite vector. When you take the Dash action while transformed, you may exhale your breath behind you, leaving a 5-foot-wide trail of Blight along your path until the start of your next turn."}, {"name": "Salt-Air Rot", "prereq": "", "text": "The taste of the withering. Bonus action, thirty feet, a creature with 2+ Wither: learn its current HP and whether it holds Focus. The technique reads its victims the way a physician reads a chart — and prescribes accordingly. As a bonus action, you can taste the Wither on a creature within 30 feet that has at least 2 Wither: learn its current HP total and whether it is maintaining Focus on anything."}, {"name": "Black Tide (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The field, rearranged. Once per short rest, move one Blight patch ten feet — never across fresh water. The vow holds even here. Mark this: the plague's one law is older than its hunger, and the hunger obeys. once/short rest move one Blight patch 10 ft, never across fresh water."}], "e198": [{"name": "Roost Walker", "prereq": "", "text": "The ceiling becomes a chair. Climb speed equal to walking, hang hands-free from any climbable surface — and while hanging unseen, From the Sound applies to every attack that turn, not just the first. The roost is the bat's office. It does its best work upside down. You gain a climb speed equal to your walking speed and can hang hands-free from any surface you could climb, talons and tail holding you fast. While hanging hands-free and unseen, From the Sound applies to every attack you make that turn, not just the first. Releasing your grip deliberately is silent: you have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks to land unheard when you drop on purpose."}, {"name": "Blood Echo", "prereq": "", "text": "The wounded leave a trail. A bloodied creature moving within thirty feet of a node leaves a sound-track followable until the end of the next turn. The House does not chase. It listens, and the bleeding are the loudest things in the dark. A bloodied creature moving within 30 feet of one of your Echo nodes leaves a sound-track you can follow until the end of your next turn."}, {"name": "Silent Wing", "prereq": "", "text": "The swoop, unheard. Treated as unseen for the attack; enemies cannot use reactions triggered by the movement; those who never perceived the bearer do not learn its location until after. The bat's doctrine in one feature: the strike should arrive before the rumor of it. When you use Razor Swoop, your passage stays unrevealed until the attack resolves: you are treated as unseen for the swoop's attack, and enemies cannot use reactions triggered by your movement during it. Creatures that had not perceived you before the swoop do not learn your location until after damage is rolled. If the attack misses, you may immediately Swap to an Echo node within 30 feet as part of the same action, gone on the wingbeat."}, {"name": "Vanishing Wing (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The blow, declined. When hit, reaction and 1 CE swap with a node within thirty feet — the attack misses if the new position is beyond reach or sight. I have watched swords pass through the space where the bat was standing. The space, it turns out, was only ever a rumor. When you are hit by an attack, you may use your reaction and spend 1 CE to swap with an Echo node within 30 feet; the attack misses if your new position is beyond the attacker's reach or out of its line of sight."}], "e199": [{"name": "Precious Plumes", "prereq": "", "text": "The toll, reinvested. When a traversal generates a Plume, redraw one Road instead — same length, new position and direction anchored within thirty feet. The innkeeper does not hoard the guests' coins. He rebuilds the inn with them. When you generate a Plume from a full traversal, you may instead immediately redraw one of your Wind Roads, keeping its length but choosing a new position and direction anchored within 30 feet of you."}, {"name": "Tailwind Archer", "prereq": "", "text": "The shot rides the road. A ranged attack along a Road's direction may emerge from a Crossroad within sixty feet instead — originating there, ignoring cover between. The wind carries more than travelers. It carries conclusions. When you make a ranged attack along the direction of a Wind Road, you may have the attack emerge from a Crossroad within 60 feet of you instead, originating there and ignoring cover between you and the target."}, {"name": "Cloud Serpent", "prereq": "", "text": "The flight paves. While flying, bonus action: trace a thirty-foot Road along the flight path, counting against the maximum. The serpent does not just use the roads. It is the road crew, and the sky is the work site. While flying with Serpent of the Updraft, you may use a bonus action to trace a Wind Road up to 30 feet long along your flight path. It counts against your normal maximum."}, {"name": "Four Directions (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The crossings learn exchange. When a willing creature teleports between Crossroads, swap two willing creatures at two different Crossroads instead. The inn's oldest courtesy: no guest should have to walk to the room they wanted. When you or a willing ally teleports between Crossroads, you may instead swap the positions of two willing creatures standing at two different Crossroads within range."}], "e200": [{"name": "Inscribed Gate", "prereq": "", "text": "The line, hidden. Spend 1 Vigilance when inscribing: the Threshold turns invisible to hostiles, spottable only by Perception against the technique DC. The kindest ambush in guardianship — the enemy does not see the line until it has already crossed it. When you inscribe a Threshold, you may spend 1 Vigilance to render it invisible to hostile creatures. A hostile creature can spot it with a successful Wisdom (Perception) check against your technique save DC."}, {"name": "Winged Guardian", "prereq": "", "text": "The rescue, rerouted. With Bull-Lion Intercession, teleport the ally from one Threshold to another within thirty feet instead of swapping — the bearer still takes the hit. The wings were always for the guests. The guardian walks; the welcomed fly. When you use Bull-Lion Intercession, you may instead teleport the ally from one Threshold to another Threshold within 30 feet of the first, rather than swapping positions with them; you still take the hit either way."}, {"name": "Palace Watch", "prereq": "", "text": "The gates, rearranged. Bonus action, 2 Vigilance: relocate one visible Threshold to a new anchor within sixty feet. The palace's walls were never fixed; they were posted. Mark this: the guardian does not defend ground. He defends the idea of ground, wherever he plants it. As a bonus action, you may spend 2 Vigilance to relocate one Threshold you can see to a new valid anchor within 60 feet."}, {"name": "No Unrecorded Passage (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The census defeats concealment. Hostile invisible creatures crossing a Threshold are revealed until the end of their turn — invisibility suppressed for the crosser — save to resist. The gate counts its passage. It does not ask whether the passage wished to be counted. Hostile invisible creatures that cross one of your Thresholds are revealed until the end of their turn: invisibility and similar concealment are suppressed for the crossing creature as the gate counts its passage. The creature may attempt a Wisdom save against your technique DC; on a success it remains unseen but still generates Vigilance as normal. You always know the exact space where the crossing occurred. This revelation pierces magical invisibility but not total cover or anti-divination effects."}], "e201": [{"name": "Cedar Warden", "prereq": "", "text": "The jurisdiction widens. The active Face's aura now radiates twenty feet from each cedar zone within one hundred twenty feet — the bearer's own fifteen feet unchanged. The warden's beat was always larger than his body. Now the map agrees. The forest carries your face farther and wider. Your active Terror Face's aura effects now originate from a 20-foot radius around each cedar zone within 120 feet of you (instead of 15 feet within 60 feet). Your own 15-foot personal aura is unchanged."}, {"name": "Terrible Countenance", "prereq": "", "text": "The felled tree testifies. When a cedar zone is destroyed, switch Face immediately without action — and resolve the new Face against the destroyer. Mark this: the forest's death is not a loss. It is a change of edict, and the lumberjack is the first to hear it. When a Cedar zone is destroyed, you may immediately switch your Face without using an action and resolve the new Face against the creature that destroyed it."}, {"name": "Forest Voice", "prereq": "", "text": "The law needs no voice. Switch Faces while silenced, gagged, or in magical silence — and while voiceless, the switch costs no action at all. The forest speaks where the bearer cannot. Consider: the Terrors were never spoken. They were always only ever shown. Switching your Terror Face is not a verbal act: you may change Faces even while silenced, gagged, or inside magical silence — and while you cannot speak, switching your Face costs no action at all. The forest speaks where your voice cannot."}, {"name": "Sevenfold Guardian (11+)", "prereq": "", "text": "The visage splits. Once per short rest, maintain two Faces until the end of the next turn — both fear-laws holding at once, hostiles resolving both where applicable, no creature suffering more than one failed result on a single Face. Two refusals, simultaneous. The bearer has stopped choosing between edicts and started issuing them in pairs. Once per short rest, when you switch your Terror Face, you may maintain two Faces simultaneously until the end of your next turn — your visage splits and both fear-laws hold. Hostiles in your Aura resolve both Faces' effects where applicable, but a single creature cannot suffer more than one failed-save result from this overlap. When the duration ends, you keep the most recently chosen Face and the other fades."}], "e202": [{"name": "Compound Payload", "prereq": "", "text": "Two dialects in one quill. Spend 2 Spines on a single Tail Volley and combine two payload effects — the Barbed Venom quill, the Tethered Screamer. The manticore's thrift was never about spending less. It was about making every spending count twice. When you spend 2 Spines on a single Tail Volley attack, you may combine two payload effects on that attack, such as a Barbed Venom quill, instead of choosing only one."}, {"name": "Scorpion Tail", "prereq": "", "text": "The venom learns the teeth. Deliver the Venom payload through the Lion's Maw — hit, spend 1 Spine, force the save. The bite was always the honest part of the hunt; now it carries the quill's subtler arguments. You may deliver your Venom payload through your Lion’s Maw instead of a quill. When you hit with Lion’s Maw, you may spend 1 Spine to force the target to make the Venom saving throw."}, {"name": "Quill Catcher", "prereq": "", "text": "The magazine accepts donations. Once per round, when a ranged weapon attack misses: reaction, snatch it from the air, recover 1 Spine — and immediately fire it back as a Tail Volley without spending. The predator's thrift extends to the enemy's ammunition. Their misses are his resupply. Once per round, when a ranged weapon attack misses you, you may use your reaction to snatch the projectile from the air and add it to your Tail Magazine, recovering 1 Spine. If you do, you may immediately make a Tail Volley attack against a creature within range without spending a Spine, firing the caught missile back. This return shot follows the normal Tail Volley rules but cannot apply payload effects."}, {"name": "Hunter's Mouth", "prereq": "", "text": "The carrion clause. Bite an object, the dead, or the incapacitated with the Maw: recover 2 Spines instead of 1. The technique makes no moral distinction about the meal. A spine is a spine, and the magazine does not ask where dinner came from. When you hit an object or a dead or incapacitated creature with Lion’s Maw, you recover 2 Spines instead of 1."}], "e243": [{"name": "Dialed In", "prereq": "Ben 10 feat", "text": "As a bonus action, you may rearrange your Active Playlist, swapping one loaded ordinary form for another Subjugated ordinary form you know. This does not count as transforming and adds no Instability."}, {"name": "Hero Time", "prereq": "Ben 10 feat", "text": "Once per short rest, use one of these triggers: when initiative is rolled, immediately transform into a loaded ordinary form without an action or CE; or when a creature you can see within 30 feet is targeted by an attack, use your reaction to transform for 0 CE before the attack resolves. The second option does not redirect the attack or grant a second reaction."}, {"name": "Quick-Change Combatant", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 6", "text": "When you Quick Change, you retain one passive trait of your previous form, such as a movement mode or sense, until the end of your next turn."}, {"name": "Form Specialist", "prereq": "Repeatable: different forms", "text": "Choose one Subjugated non-Way Big form. Once per short rest, while transformed into a different form, you may use one feature of your chosen form, paying its normal CE cost. You may take this feat again for another form, but never twice for the same form."}], "e244": [{"name": "Fast Scribe", "prereq": "", "text": "Once per turn, you may inscribe a Tier I rune as a bonus action instead of an action."}, {"name": "Blood-Carved Staves", "prereq": "", "text": "You may carve a persistent rune directly into your own flesh as a living stave. A rune carved this way moves with you, cannot be dispelled by effects that target objects, and once per short rest you may invoke it as a bonus action instead of an action."}, {"name": "Ætt-Binder", "prereq": "", "text": "When you form a Bindrune from two runes of the same ætt, you may inscribe it on a weapon, shield, or tool you touch. Either component rune can then be invoked separately without breaking the Bindrune. Wyrd belongs to no ætt and can never benefit from this feat."}, {"name": "Runeseer", "prereq": "", "text": "Reading of the Three takes 1 minute instead of 10. Its Foretold Die becomes your Rune Die. Once per long rest, you may ask one simple yes/no question concerning the next 24 hours; the GM answers truthfully according to the most likely course of events at the time of the reading."}], "e246": [{"name": "Straight Man", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Comedy", "text": "Choose one willing ally who can see and hear you. That ally may deliver one of your Gags as if they were you, using your CE save DC, though you still pay any CE cost. The ally must be within 30 feet of the Gag’s target."}, {"name": "Super Gag", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Commit to the Bit", "text": "You have stepped up your game with some premium material you read online. You gain the following gags while your technique is active: Written on your Face. As an action for 3 CE, you target a creature within 30 ft that you can see. For 1 minute or when your technique ends, the target’s emotions and intentions are literally written on their face. The target has disadvantage on attacks against anyone who can see their face. Anyone that can see their face knows their general emotions and can tell whenever they are scheming or planning something by reading the doodles on their face. Costume Switch. As an action for 2 CE, you apply a wardrobe change to a number of creatures equal to your CE modifier within 30 ft of you that you can see. This effect is purely cosmetic and cannot change their AC or movement and cannot give them any conditions. You can also change a property about them, such as giving them multiple eyes or arms. These changes are nonfunctional and a creature can take an action to make a Wisdom (Perception) or Intelligence (Investigation) against your CE save DC inspect these changes. On a success, they realize the changes are fake. This feature lasts for a number of minutes equal to your CE modifier before disappearing."}, {"name": "Maximum: Laugh Track", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Peak Comedy", "text": "While your technique is active, your invisible audience can deliver your Gags for you. A Gag you use may originate from any point within 30 feet of you that you choose; creatures cannot tell the Gag came from you without succeeding on a Wisdom (Perception) check against your CE save DC."}, {"name": "Lasting Laughs", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Comedy", "text": "Even when you’re the one telling the joke, you can’t stop laughing. For an additional 2 CE when you activate Comedy, you can make the technique last 10 minutes. This does not work with Peak Comedy."}], "e247": [{"name": "Bestial Seance", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Seance", "text": "You have learned to bring a bit of whimsy to your usually ghastly technique. When you use Seance on yourself, you can choose to instead channel the Physical Information of a Beast with a CR equal to or less than your proficiency bonus. You gain all the creature’s traits, senses, movements and actions in addition to the normal effects of Physical Information. To use this technique, you must be wearing a costume of that specific animal, costing $200 x the Beast’s CR. You can wear this costume with armor, but if it takes an amount of damage (other than psychic) equal to 3 x your level, it becomes unusable and you lose any benefits from this feature."}, {"name": "Warded Circle", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Ritual of Resurrection", "text": "When you begin your Ritual of Resurrection, you may trace a warding circle around yourself. For the ritual’s duration, hostile creatures treat the 10-foot-radius circle as difficult terrain and must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your CE save DC to willingly enter it."}, {"name": "Cling to Life", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Maximum: Black Seance", "text": "When a target runs out of cursed energy and can no longer maintain the seance, they can choose to forcefully hold the spirit within their body. At the beginning of the target’s turn, they instead spend 5 HP, reducing their maximum by the same amount. The target regains up to 15 of the lost hit point maximum after each long rest (invented)."}], "e248": [{"name": "Blood Production", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Rot Techniques", "text": "You have found a way to link your blood to Cursed Energy. For 1 CE, you can create a sufficient source of blood worth 10 HP that can only be used for your Rot features. This does not regain HP."}, {"name": "Condensed Decay", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Scarlet Rot", "text": "When you hit a creature with a Rot Technique, you may spend up to 4 HP. The target’s speed is reduced by 5 feet for every 2 HP spent until the end of its next turn, as your blood clots around its limbs."}, {"name": "Blackened Blood", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Maximum: Wing King", "text": "Your blackened blood marks what it touches. You always know the direction and distance of any creature damaged by your Rot Techniques within the last hour, and you have advantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks to track them."}, {"name": "Wingbeat", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Maximum: Wing King", "text": "While using Wing King, you may beat your veined wings as a bonus action. Each creature within 15 feet of you must make a Strength saving throw against your CE save DC or be pushed 10 feet away from you and knocked prone."}], "e249": [{"name": "Patchwork Salvage", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must make Cursed Corpse Creation", "text": "Nothing is wasted in the workshop. When a corpse falls, an hour with the salvage grafts one of its mutations onto another. The fallen serve again — in parts. When one of your Cursed Corpses is destroyed, you may spend 1 hour harvesting its intact parts. You may transfer one mutation from the destroyed corpse to another of your Cursed Corpses."}, {"name": "Soul Imbuement", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Cursed Corpse Creation", "text": "The old heresy, done properly: copy a soul’s information into the core, wait two weeks, and the corpse wakes sentient — behaving like its donor without remembering them. One at a time. Slow. This is where ‘corpse’ stops being the right word. You have learned to copy a creature’s soul information into a Cursed Corpse. You can only have 1 soul imbued corpse at a time. This increases to 2 at 11th level and 3 at 18th level. It takes 3 long rests to imbue someone’s soul information into the core. You must have the person readily available or have a good memory of the person to turn their physical information into soul information. Once a corpse has been created, it takes 2 weeks to develop before it becomes sentient. It gains the Autonomy mutation and can choose any Innate Technique feat the GM deems appropriate (invented) as if it were a player. A corpse with this core is sentient and mimics the behavior of the soul they are imbued with, but it does not gain its memories."}, {"name": "Cursed Tactician", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Corpse Tactics", "text": "Orders relayed corpse to corpse, thirty feet per relay — the army becomes its own telegraph. Range is logistics; this feat buys it. Your Corpse Tactics orders can be relayed through your corpses. When you use Corpse Tactics, a corpse within range may pass the order to another of your corpses within 30 feet of it, which may pass it on further, extending your effective command range."}, {"name": "Mutate Specialist", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Cursed Corpse Mutation", "text": "The maker who studies his accidents learns to repeat the good ones — once a day, grant a mutation another corpse already carries, rather than trusting the dice. Once per long rest, when one of your Cursed Corpses would gain a random mutation, you may instead grant it a mutation already possessed by another of your corpses."}, {"name": "Expert Maker", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must make Cursed Corpse Creation", "text": "A lifetime of tips and tricks: a core or body at a third of the cost or a third of the time. Years of sawdust and solder, cashed in. You have spent your life learning your technique and learned tips and tricks that help you master the process. You can create a cursed core or body for 1/3 of the cost or time."}], "e250": [{"name": "Blood Production", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Blood Manipulation", "text": "He has learned to spin cursed energy into blood itself — coin minted from will rather than vein. The treasury learns to print its own currency. Note the limit: minted coin buys techniques, not health. Even alchemy respects the flesh. You have found a way to link your blood to Cursed Energy. For 1 CE, you can create a sufficient source of blood worth 10 HP that can only be used for your Blood Manipulation features. This does not regain HP."}, {"name": "Poisonous Blood", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Blood Manipulation", "text": "He seals his blood in a vessel and offers it as medicine — a draught that knits the drinker's wounds. Blood given freely heals; blood taken by force kills. The same river, two natures. Thus does the healer's art hide inside the killer's. As an action, you may draw your blood into a sealed vessel, spending up to 10 HP; the vessel holds that blood for 24 hours. A creature can drink it as a bonus action to regain hit points equal to the HP stored. You can maintain only one such vessel at a time."}, {"name": "Blood Crystallization", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Blood Constructs", "text": "He hardens his blood into lasting things — a blade, a tool, a span to cross a gap. Not the fleeting constructs of battle, but an hour of solid truth. The patient craft: blood taught to be stone, if only for a little while. As an action for 3 CE, you crystallize your blood into a solid object: a simple weapon, a tool, or a 10-foot plank or pole. The object lasts 1 hour, has AC 15 and hit points equal to twice your level, and shatters into harmless shards when destroyed."}, {"name": "Crimson Afterimage", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Flowing Red Scale", "text": "While his blood runs at flood pace, he leaves a red ghost of himself standing where he stood — a decoy painted in his own life. The first spear finds the painting, not the man. Deception bought with speed: the oldest trick, performed with the newest blood. While Flowing Red Scale is active, your accelerated blood lets you leave a bloody afterimage. As a bonus action for 3 CE, you create an illusory duplicate in your space until the start of your next turn; the first attack roll made against you before then targets the duplicate, AC 10 + your proficiency bonus, instead of you, and the duplicate vanishes whether the attack hits or misses."}, {"name": "Supernova", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Piercing Blood", "text": "He condenses his piercing blood into small waiting suns and sows them like seeds across the field. They hang, patient, until a footstep wakes them — then buckshot blooming. The minefield as garden: he plants, and the enemy harvests. You can create small orbs of condensed blood that explode like a buckshot. As an action, you condense your Piercing Blood into a tiny orb of blood in an unoccupied space that you can see within 30 feet, which stays there for a maximum of 1 minute before exploding. You can create as many orbs as your proficiency bonus in an action with each having its own cost, spending 5 CE and 5 HP for each, and can choose for them to explode immediately upon creation or manually as a reaction to a creature entering the range of explosion. The orb then explodes, forcing every creature within 10 feet of it to make a Dexterity saving throw for each orb. On a failure, the target takes 8d8 piercing damage and is knocked prone. On a success, they take half as much damage and aren’t knocked prone."}, {"name": "Wing King Imitation", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Piercing Blood", "text": "He gathers his blood into veined wings and takes the sky — the heir as a red comet, raining lines of ruin below. For one minute, the battlefield has weather. Mark the trade written into the wings: while he flies, the great beam sleeps. Even treasuries cannot fund two wars at once. You condense your blood into wings resembling veins as a bonus action for 10 CE, gathering the wings behind you and gaining the following benefits for 1 minute: your walking speed is quadrupled; you gain a flying speed equal to half your walking speed; as a free action on your turn, you can unleash lines of blood. This takes shape as three ranged Cursed Energy attacks against a creature within 60 feet. Each attack deals 3d10 + your CE modifier in necrotic damage. While using Wing King, you cannot use Piercing Blood."}], "e251": [{"name": "Aerokinesis", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Storms of Disaster", "text": "New applications of old storms: Suffocation — the air denied for two CE and a Constitution save — and Storm Sense — feeling each body displace the air inside his weather. The same hands that make the storm learn to strangle with it. Through training and understanding, you have found new applications for your storms. Choose one; you may select this feat multiple times, choosing a different application each time. Suffocation. As an action for 2 cursed energy, you target a creature within 30 feet that you can see. It must make a Constitution saving throw, taking your proficiency bonus in d6s of necrotic damage and beginning to suffocate on a failed save. While suffocating, its movement is halved and its attack rolls have disadvantage. If you move more than 30 feet away or lose concentration, the suffocation ends. Storm Sense. While a storm of your creation is active, you can sense the location of any creature within it, feeling the air each one displaces."}, {"name": "Flying Nimbus", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Storm Creation", "text": "The storm carries its maker: flight at walking speed, hovering, while the Creation endures — and a ten-foot drift on each Storms of Disaster exhalation. The sovereign does not walk where he can ride. While using Storm Creation, you have a flying speed equal to your walking speed and can hover. When you use Storms of Disaster while flying, you can immediately move up to 10 ft without spending movement or provoking opportunity attacks."}, {"name": "Squall", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Maximum: Divine Storm Sovereign", "text": "The final intimacy: within his own storm, he steps anywhere as a bonus action, and his techniques may originate from any point inside. The storm is no longer weather — it is an extension of his will. While you are within a storm of your creation, you may teleport to a different point within the storm as a bonus action, and you may originate your Storms of Disaster techniques from any point within the storm."}], "e252": [{"name": "Vermin Bulwark", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Vermin of Disaster", "text": "The swarm as shield: when a blow lands within five feet of her insects, they take it instead. The nest has always known how to lose parts to save the whole. As a reaction when a creature within 5 feet of one of your Insect Swarms is hit by an attack, you may have the swarm interpose itself; the swarm takes the damage instead of the target."}, {"name": "Vermin Techniques", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Almighty Swarm", "text": "Three new intimacies: the Cloak — standing inside the swarm, its wounds become her buffer; the Grasping Hand — a grapple through the insects for three CE, the victim pulled into the swarm; and Transport Via Bugs — six CE, a link between two great swarms, and she steps through. The nest is armor, hand, and road. You have learned to better control the combined actions of your Vermin Swarms, allowing you to learn the following ways to use your Swarms: Insect Cloak. While you are occupying the same space as one of your Vermin Swarms, you can treat the Swarm's hit points as temporary hit points for yourself. Grasping Hand. You can spend 3 CE to replace one of your attacks on your turn with a grapple check through one of your Insect Swarms against a creature within 5 ft of the swarm. Instead of an Athletics check, you make a Cursed Energy (Arcana) check. The grapple gains a +1 bonus and +5 ft of range per size category above Medium the swarm is. On a success, the creature is grappled and can be pulled into the Insect Swarm. Transport Via Bugs. As an action for 6 CE, you form a link between one Large or larger Vermin Swarm within 10 ft and connect it to another Large or larger Vermin Swarm at any distance. Before the end of your turn, you can spend 5 ft of movement to walk into the space of the Insect Swarm within 5 ft, reappearing within 5 ft of the destination Insect Swarm."}, {"name": "Festering Life Sword", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Parthenogenesis", "text": "Six CE, a bonus action, and a weapon becomes the Festering Life Sword — poison on a failed save — lasting a day or until she dies. The brood’s hatred, given an edge. As a bonus action for 6 CE, you transform a weapon you are holding. It loses all previous benefits and becomes the Special Grade Cursed Tool: Festering Life Sword — 1d8 slashing (invented); on a hit the target makes a Constitution save vs your CE DC or is poisoned until the end of your next turn (invented). You can only have one weapon transformed this way at a time and this tool disappears when you finish a long rest or die."}, {"name": "Reinforced Vermin", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Vermin of Disaster", "text": "Two CE on the command to harden one swarm — a size larger, two extra damage dice while unbloodied. The nest, when asked, grows chitin. As part of the bonus action you take to command your Insect Swarms, you can spend 2 cursed energy to reinforce one of your Insect Swarms with cursed energy for 1 minute. While reinforced, their size category increases by one and they deal an additional 2 damage dice on a successful Bites attack (only +1 if bloodied). If you use multiple Reinforced Insect Swarms to form a Vermin Swarm, it only gains these benefits once."}], "e253": [{"name": "Levitation System", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Gravity Field", "text": "The small, surgical version: Levitate for two CE — two more forces the save at disadvantage. Sometimes you do not need the whole sky — only one man’s share of it. As an action for 2 CE, you can cast Levitate. You can spend an additional 2 CE to force the creature to make the save at disadvantage."}, {"name": "Inverted Shield", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Antigravity Shield", "text": "When his shielded self is struck in melee, three CE inverts the field — the attacker is pulled ten feet in and knocked prone on a failed Strength save. The wall reaches back. As a reaction when you are hit by a melee attack while your Antigravity Shield is active, you may spend 3 CE to invert the field. The attacker must make a Strength saving throw against your CE save DC or be pulled 10 feet toward you and knocked prone."}, {"name": "Antigravitational Flight", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Boosted System", "text": "Three CE, a touch, ten minutes: sixty feet of hover for himself or another. The sky’s servant may lend the sky out. As an action for 3 CE, you can give yourself or another creature you touch a 60 feet hover speed for 10 minutes."}, {"name": "Dense Antigravity Shield", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Antigravity Shield", "text": "Three more CE, and the shield thickens: reduce all damage by half the Antigravity’s maximum-height fall-damage dice. The densest sky is the best armor. For an additional 3 CE, your Antigravity Shield instead reduces all damage against you by half your Antigravity’s maximum height fall damage dice until the beginning of your next turn."}], "e254": [{"name": "Instant Manifestation", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Dark Cube", "text": "When struck, a reaction raises the cube around him — the blow lands on geometry, not flesh. If he dodged that turn, the wall may shelter a friend within five feet. Reflex, cubed. When you are hit by an attack, you may use your reaction to manifest a Dark Cube around yourself; the cube takes the damage in your stead, applying the damage to the cube’s statistics. If you took the Dodge action on your turn, you may extend the cube to also enclose one creature within 5 feet of you."}, {"name": "Offensive Creations", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Black Box Reinforcement", "text": "The wall learns offense, three ways: Crushing Cube — four CE, crushed for 5d10 and prone; Block Strike — two CE, fists wrapped in cube dealing PB-in-d4s necrotic; Dark Press — five CE, a sixty-foot line hurled back for 6d8. The fortress has doors, and the doors are for hitting. You have focused on using your technique to devastating effects and have learned offensive applications of your cursed technique: Crushing Cube. As an action for 4 CE, you target a 30 feet tall, 10 feet wide square cylinder within 30 feet. All creatures in range must make a Strength saving throw. On a failure they take 5d10 necrotic damage and fall prone as they are crushed under a massive Dark Cube. On a success, they take half as much damage and are not prone. Block Strike. As a bonus action for 2 CE, you cover your fist or other part of your body with a Dark Cube for 1 minute. You can make a melee cursed energy attack with your unarmed strikes. On a hit you deal your proficiency bonus in d4s + your CE modifier in necrotic damage. Dark Press. As an action for 5 CE, you can create a Dark Cube in front of you that explodes in length on one side. All creatures in a 10 feet wide 60 feet long line must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failure, they take 6d8 necrotic damage and are pushed back to the edge of the line. If they impact a solid object or structure, they take the remaining distance as fall damage."}, {"name": "Sealing Cube", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Maximum: Midnight Armor", "text": "Trap a man in a Perfect Cube and you may seal his output: no technique costing more than five CE while he sits inside. A prison that taxes the soul’s exertion. When you trap a creature in a Perfect Cube, you can choose to seal the output of the creature. They can only spend the minimum cursed energy on a cursed technique while trapped within your Perfect Cube and cannot use cursed techniques that cost more than 5 cursed energy."}], "e255": [{"name": "Ferocious Courage", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Ignition", "text": "When the blade lands, one CE lets the flames leap to another creature within fifteen feet — a Dexterity save against half his Ignition damage. Courage is contagious; so is fire. When you hit a creature with your ignited weapon, you may spend 1 CE to let the flames leap to another creature within 15 feet of the target. That creature must make a Dexterity saving throw against your CE save DC, taking half your Ignition damage on a failure and no damage on a success (invented)."}, {"name": "Blazing Heart", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Mantle of Courage", "text": "The Mantle may be draped over one willing ally within thirty feet instead of himself — the aura, the resistances, all of it. The hearth, shared. When you activate Mantle of Courage, you may drape its flames over one willing ally within 30 feet instead of yourself. That ally gains the aura, resistances, and other benefits of the Mantle for the duration."}, {"name": "Soulfire", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Eternal Flames", "text": "Three CE, and the fire burns even the soul: all fire damage that turn ignores immunity and reduces maximum hit points by the fire dealt. What the flame takes, the body does not get back. You have learned to burn even the soul. When you hit with a melee attack, you can spend 3 CE to cause all fire damage dealt on your turn to ignore immunity to fire damage and reduce a creature's maximum hit points by the fire damage dealt (invented) until they complete a long rest."}, {"name": "Technique Release", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Maximum: Conflagration", "text": "End Ignition early on a hit to discharge the remaining flame — every creature within ten feet of the target but himself saves or burns. The kept flame, spent all at once — the last lesson of courage is that some fires are meant to be used up. When you hit with an attack while Ignition is active, you may end Ignition early to discharge its remaining flame. Each creature within 10 feet of the target, other than you, must make a Dexterity saving throw against your CE save DC, taking your Ignition damage on a failure or half as much on a success."}], "e256": [{"name": "Dowsing Vibrations", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Cursed Centipede", "text": "While the centipede is summoned, both feet on the ground: tremorsense to a hundred feet — nothing touching the ground surprises her. The appetite listens through the floor. While your centipede shikigami is summoned, you gain tremorsense out to 100 feet while both of your feet are on the ground. You cannot be surprised by creatures touching the ground within your tremorsense, and you know the exact location of invisible creatures touching the ground within it. The range increases to 150 feet at 6th level, 200 feet at 11th, and 300 feet at 18th level."}, {"name": "Wu Gong", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Insect Storage", "text": "One CE on a melee hit, hers or the centipede’s: concentrated venom, a Constitution save, the wound carrying poison. The gullet shares its chemistry with the blade. You have learned to concentrate the venom of your cursed centipede and add it to your attacks. When you or your centipede hit with a melee attack, you can spend 1 CE to force the creature to make a Constitution saving throw. On a failure, the creature takes your proficiency in d6s of poison damage and they are stunned until the beginning of their next turn."}, {"name": "Living Gullet", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Insect Storage", "text": "The stomach carries living cargo: one willing or incapacitated Medium creature or smaller, breathing inside, blinded and restrained, disgorged by command. The safest place on the battlefield is inside the mouth. Your centipede’s stomach can carry living cargo. It may swallow one willing or incapacitated creature of Medium size or smaller; the creature can breathe inside but is blinded and restrained while swallowed. Disgorging the creature takes an action. The centipede cannot store items while carrying a creature."}], "e257": [{"name": "Forcible Confession", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Binding Vow", "text": "Two CE, a bonus action: thirty feet, and the target speaks only truth for a minute — or until a Charisma save ends it. The auditor’s first instrument is the deposition. As a bonus action for 2 CE, you can force a creature within 30 ft to speak only truthful words for 1 minute, or until they succeed on a Charisma saving throw at the end of their turn."}, {"name": "Cunning Judicator", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Retrial", "text": "When a creature breaks a vow with her, five CE as a reaction: a Charisma save, or d4s of force per ten hit points remaining. The penalty clause, enforced at the moment of breach. When a creature breaks a Binding Vow with you, you can spend 5 CE as a reaction to force the creature to make a Charisma saving throw. On a failure, it takes 1d4 force damage per 10 hit points it has remaining (rounded down, maximum 10d4)."}], "e258": [{"name": "Dead-Man's Circuit", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Cursed Circuitry", "text": "He may key a pattern to his own vitals — if he falls unconscious or dies, the circuit fires regardless of its condition. The engineer’s final contingency: even his corpse keeps an appointment. You may key a circuit pattern to your own vital signs. When you set the pattern, you may choose for it to trigger if you fall unconscious or die, even if its normal activation condition is never met."}, {"name": "Circuit Chain Reaction", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Advanced Circuits", "text": "Two CE on activation: a pattern within twenty feet fires too, regardless of its condition. One held breath wakes the next; the room exhales all at once. When a circuit pattern is activated, you can spend 2 cursed energy to cause a chain reaction. Choose a circuit pattern within 20 feet of the activated pattern. That pattern is also activated, even if its activation condition is not met. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest."}, {"name": "Living Circuitry", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Linked Circuits", "text": "Ten CE, an action, one minute: his own body infused — unarmed strikes carrying d6s of lightning and more besides. When the floor is not enough, he becomes the circuit. You have learned to infuse your own body with cursed circuitry. As an action, you can spend 10 cursed energy to gain the following benefits for 1 minute: your unarmed strikes deal an additional 1d6 lightning damage; you gain resistance to lightning damage; you can use Burst Leap on yourself as a bonus action without needing a circuit pattern. At 11th level, you can spend 15 cursed energy instead to also gain immunity to being stunned."}, {"name": "Closed Circuit", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Circuit", "text": "Efficiency, internalized: he leaves no cursed-energy residuals, and detection checks against him are made at disadvantage. The most patient trap is the one nobody knows is laid. Your technique specializing in energy efficiency has begun to develop your body. You no longer leave residuals of your cursed energy and creatures have disadvantage on checks to directly detect you through your cursed energy. As an action, you can concentrate for up to 1 minute to hide your cursed energy within your circuit, giving anyone a -5 to their skill checks to directly sense your cursed energy."}], "e259": [{"name": "Master Alchemist", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Cursed Transmutation", "text": "He may transmute magical objects, and may transmute what he sees within thirty feet without touching it. The pen no longer needs the hand. You can transmute magical objects, and you may perform a transmutation on an object you can see within 30 feet without touching it."}, {"name": "Philosopher's Stone", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Elemental Manipulation", "text": "The stone: an alchemical artifact granting two masterworks — base metal to gold once per rest, and more. The alchemist’s old dream, itemized. You have created a Philosopher’s Stone, a powerful alchemical artifact. It grants you two masterworks. Chrysopoeia: once per long rest, you may transmute up to 1 cubic foot of base metal into gold worth up to 100 gp. Panacea: you may crush a fragment of the Stone, which reforms at dawn, to end one poison, disease, or curse afflicting a creature you touch."}, {"name": "Soul Alchemy", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Alchemy of the Soul", "text": "Eight CE, an action: a soul bond with the willing within thirty feet — emotions and location shared, and more. The final transmutation is not of matter but of relation. You have learned to transmute souls. As an action for 8 CE, you can forge a soul bond with a willing creature within 30 ft. While bonded, you can sense each other's emotions and location, and you can communicate telepathically. If one of you takes damage, the other can choose to take half of that damage instead. This bond lasts until dispelled or until one of you dies."}], "e260": [{"name": "Wheel of Adaptation", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Dark Claw", "text": "The wheel turns above his head with every completed adaptation — and for two CE, a bonus action may turn it toward an ally within thirty feet, lending them his lessons. Survival, shared. You manifest Mahoraga's wheel above your head, turning with every adaptation you complete. As a bonus action for 2 CE, you can turn the wheel toward one ally you can see within 30 ft, lending them your hard-won resilience — they gain the resistance or immunity of one of your active adaptations until the end of your next turn."}, {"name": "Mahoraga's Fury", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Adaptation", "text": "At half health or less, the fury surfaces: two CE, a bonus action, the claw slammed into the ground — jagged claws erupt in a fifteen-foot burst. The scar’s temper has a radius. When you are reduced to half your hit points or fewer, Mahoraga's fury surfaces through your claw. As a bonus action for 2 CE, you can slam the Dark Claw into the ground, erupting jagged claws in a 15 ft radius around you. Each creature in the area must make a Dexterity saving throw, taking your unarmed strike damage on a failed save or half as much on a success. Once you use this eruption, you can't use it again until you finish a short rest."}, {"name": "Perfect Adaptation", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Eight-Handled Sword", "text": "Nothing learned is wasted: three CE, an action, discharges an adaptation — a damage type adapted this combat, released. The lesson, weaponized retroactively. Your adaptation is now perfect — nothing learned is wasted. As an action for 3 CE, you can discharge one of your adaptations: choose a damage type you have adapted to during this combat and release it in a 30 ft cone. Each creature in the area must make a Dexterity saving throw, taking 1d8 damage of the chosen type for each damage type you have adapted to this combat (maximum 5d8) on a failed save, or half as much on a success. Your adaptation to the discharged type ends."}, {"name": "Close Combat Specialist", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Claw", "text": "Within five feet, a claw hit may grapple as a bonus action — and the grappled take claw damage on his turns. The claw is not only a blade; it is a hand that does not let go. When you hit a creature with a claw attack while within 5 ft, you can attempt to grapple the creature as a bonus action. While grappling a creature, you can cause the creature to take your claw damage at the start of their turn."}], "e261": [{"name": "Ley Line Extension", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Ley Line Command", "text": "The connection may be shared: on creating the Ley Line, a number of creatures equal to his CE modifier gain its benefits. The mountain lends its footing. You have learned to extend the benefits of your connection with the earth to others. When you create a Ley Line you can give a number of creatures equal to your Cursed Energy modifier the benefits of Flow of the Dragon while they are within 30 ft and touching the same ground as you."}, {"name": "Ground Control", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Earth Dragon Soul", "text": "Three CE, an action, a stomped foot: the ground within thirty feet reshaped — in one of the listed ways. The foundation is not scenery; it is an instrument. As an action for 3 CE, you stomp your foot and transform the ground within 30 ft in one of the following ways:"}], "e262": [{"name": "Density Manipulation", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Excavation", "text": "One CE, a bonus action, a touched construct: light as pumice — carried, moved — or dense as lead. The mason adjusts the stone’s honesty. You have learned to change the density of the stone you shape. As a bonus action for 1 CE, you can touch one of your stone constructs and either make it light as pumice — it can be carried or moved freely and no longer blocks movement — or hyper-dense: a creature underneath or adjacent to it must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be pinned beneath it, restrained until it uses its action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your CE save DC to shove free."}, {"name": "Rock Burst", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Sculpted Earth", "text": "A reaction: one construct within sixty feet explodes — five feet, Dexterity or d12s of bludgeoning. What was built can be unbuilt, violently. As a reaction, you can cause one of your stone constructs within 60 feet of you to explode. Any creature within 5 feet must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, they take 1d12 bludgeoning damage and are knocked prone. You can spend CE up to half your proficiency bonus (rounded down) as part of this reaction to heighten the explosion and deal an additional 1d12 bludgeoning damage per CE and cause creatures in range to take half as much damage on a success."}, {"name": "Arms of the Giant", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Stone Arms", "text": "The Stone Arms learn new grips: Interposing Fist — the arms close around him as a shield — and more. The quarry’s hands learn gentleness, selectively. You have taught your Stone Arms new grips. While maintaining your Stone Arms, you can use your action for one of the following instead of crushing: Interposing Fist — the arms close around you, granting you three-quarters cover until the start of your next turn. Sundering Grip — crush a restrained creature as normal, and the shock of the impact gives it disadvantage on its next attack roll. Hurl — throw a restrained creature up to 30 ft to an unoccupied space you can see; if it strikes a solid surface, it takes 3d6 bludgeoning damage."}], "e263": [{"name": "Snake Scales", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Eight Lives", "text": "Like Orochi, he sheds: a reaction to damage, two CE — slough the outer scales and end grapple, restraint, or more. The skin is a receipt for a wound already paid. Like Orochi, you have learned to shed your skin. As a reaction to taking damage for 2 CE, you slough off your outer scales: you end one of the following conditions affecting you — grappled, restrained, or poisoned — and can move up to 10 ft without provoking opportunity attacks, leaving the shed skin behind."}, {"name": "Blessing of the Hydra", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Collective Will", "text": "When Eight Lives returns him, he may take resistance to the damage type that felled him — or immunity to a condition he bore — for an hour. Each death teaches the bloodline one new refusal. When you use Eight Lives to return to life, you can gain resistance to one damage type that reduced you to 0 hit points or immunity to one harmful condition you had. This benefit lasts for 1 hour."}, {"name": "Fang Versatility", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Fangs of Orochi", "text": "The fangs serve as dagger or shortsword — and may be thrown, twenty-sixty. The serpent’s teeth are cutlery as well as artillery. You have trained your technique to be more versatile in combat. You can wield Fangs of Orochi as a Dagger or Shortsword, and you can throw a Fang as a thrown weapon (range 20/60 ft) — a thrown Fang slithers back to your hand at the start of your next turn. When one of your Fang shikigami hits a creature, you can forgo the damage to have the Fang coil around the target's limb instead: the target has disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of your next turn."}], "e264": [{"name": "Diptych", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Cursed Painting", "text": "Four CE on entering a painting’s subspace: exit from one of his physical paintings instead. The private worlds are folded together; the doors connect. You have learned to fold, expand, and even connect the subspaces of your paintings. When you enter one of your painting subspaces, you can spend 4 cursed energy to exit from one of your physical paintings. Additionally, the number of paintings you can have at once increases by your proficiency bonus and the area of your subspace doubles."}, {"name": "Air Brush", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Impasto Canvas", "text": "A reaction to an attack roll, one CE: +4 AC from a formed painting — and on a miss, the attack is stored in his subspace. The canvas eats the blow. As a reaction to an attack roll, you can spend 1 Cursed Energy to add +4 to your AC against the attack by forming a cursed painting, storing the attack in your subspace on a miss. If you have taken the dodge action, you can use this reaction on allies within 5 feet."}, {"name": "Gradient", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Sgraffito", "text": "Five CE, an action: a subspace Gradient fills a thirty-foot cube around him for a minute — sixty feet at the eleventh — and his technique features work within it. A traveling exhibition of his private geography. As an action for 5 cursed energy, you create a subspace Gradient that fills a 30 ft cube centered on you for 1 minute (60 ft at 11th level). You can use your innate technique features within this subspace, but they cannot extend beyond it. As a bonus action for 2 CE while the Gradient persists, you can fade one willing creature you can see inside it into the color wash — they become invisible to creatures outside the Gradient until they attack, use a technique, or the Gradient ends."}], "e265": [{"name": "Regrown Flesh", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Faster Throws", "text": "The armory restocks itself — what has not yet detonated can be knit back into service, though the blood-tax is never refunded. You have learned to knit your explosive flesh back together. As a bonus action for 2 CE, you can regrow or reattach a body part you removed that has not yet detonated, restoring its use. You do not regain the hit points you spent to remove it."}, {"name": "Elemental Bomb", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Guerilla Tactics", "text": "The payload takes on flavors: fire to burn, cold to slow, lightning to share the wound with a second victim. You have learned how to create different types of explosions. When you use a bomb, you can spend additional cursed energy equal to the energy spent to make it an elemental bomb, choosing fire, cold, or lightning. The bomb's damage becomes that type, and it gains an additional effect: fire ignites flammable objects and deals an extra 1d6 fire damage to creatures that failed the save; cold halves the speed of creatures that failed the save until the end of their next turn; lightning arcs to one additional creature within 15 ft of the blast, dealing half the bomb's damage to it."}, {"name": "Reduced Harm", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Faster Throws", "text": "The quartermaster learns economy — the flesh-tax shrinks with level, though it is never waived entirely. You have learned to minimize the damage you take when using your technique. You decrease the hit point loss from using any part of your body as an explosive by an amount equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum 1 hit point). At 6th level, this reduction increases to an amount equal to twice your Constitution modifier plus your level (minimum 1 hit point)."}], "e266": [{"name": "Kinetic Absorption", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Store and Release", "text": "He learns to bank the enemy's blows as well as his own — a reaction that turns incoming force into a deposit. As a reaction to bludgeoning, slashing, or piercing damage, you can spend 1 cursed energy to reduce the incoming damage by your Cursed Energy score and gain 1 Jin Charge. You cannot reduce the damage of other damage types."}, {"name": "Carried Momentum", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Instantaneous Movement", "text": "The miser shares the road: one willing soul may ride the instantaneous movement beside him. You have learned to share your instantaneous movement. When you use Instantaneous Movement, you can spend 1 additional Jin charge to bring one willing creature you are touching with you, moving them to the same destination without provoking opportunity attacks."}, {"name": "Instantaneous Charge", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Instantaneous Movement", "text": "Speed spent as a weapon — three charges of motion behind a single strike, and thunder riding with it. When you use at least 3 Jin charges for Instantaneous Movement, you gain advantage on your next melee attack roll. On a hit, you deal additional thunder damage equal to your Cursed Energy modifier."}], "e267": [{"name": "Veil of the Faceless God", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Madness Inducement", "text": "The user learns to look through the cracks his own madness opens — every infected mind becomes a borrowed eye. You have learned to see through the cracks your madness opens. When a creature gains Madness from your technique, you can spend 1 CE as a reaction to peer through the fracture — until the end of your next turn, you can see and hear through that creature's senses."}, {"name": "Hands of Madness", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Madness Enhancement", "text": "The contagion moves into the fists: the user's own strikes seed Madness, and the madder the target, the harder they fall. You have learned to use your Madness to enhance your unarmed strikes. You gain 1d6 Madness when you hit a creature with an unarmed strike. Additionally, your unarmed strikes deal an additional 1d6 psychic damage for every 10 Madness the target has."}, {"name": "True Mania", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Obsession and Insanity", "text": "The user learns to aim the storm — naming the obsession of the newly berserk, choosing their target for them. You have learned to aim the madness you unleash. When a creature becomes berserk from your Madness, you can spend 2 CE to name its obsession — you choose which creature the berserk creature perceives as its target."}], "e268": [{"name": "Destined One", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Fate Manipulation", "text": "The weaver learns to tug the threads she has tied — a bonus-action pull, or a willing swap of places. You have learned to tug the threads you tie. As a bonus action for 1 CE, you can pull the red thread binding a creature affected by one of your Fates: the creature must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be pulled up to 15 ft toward the creature it is bound to. If both bound creatures are willing, no save is required and you can swap their positions instead."}, {"name": "Web of Fate", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Cursed Eyes of Fate", "text": "The loom widens: one casting now knots a crowd, though every touch-gated Fate still demands every hand. When you cast a Fate onto targets, you can instead target a number of creatures equal to 1 + your proficiency bonus within range. If the Fate requires Touch, you must touch all targets of the technique."}, {"name": "Maximum: Shears of Three Fates", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Road of Karma", "text": "The feat-form of the shears — the same slow death, granted to those who have walked the Road. As an action for 15 cursed energy, you form a scissor with your fingers and snip one of the threads of fate of a creature you can see within 5 ft of you. At the start of each of the target’s turns, they must make a Death save. This roll cannot have advantage or disadvantage and the target gains 1 level of exhaustion for every failed death save. If the target fails 3 death saves, they fall to 0 hit points and die. They are unable to be revived by cursed techniques. If the target succeeds 3 death saves or you are reduced to 0 hit points or die, the technique ends and the target becomes immune to this technique for 3 days."}], "e269": [{"name": "Greater Foresight", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Predictable Strikes", "text": "Foresight shared with the line: an ally's roll blessed with advantage, called out before it lands. Your foresight spills over to those you fight beside. As a reaction for 1 CE when a creature you can see within 30 ft makes an attack roll, ability check, or saving throw, you can call out what you have already seen and grant them advantage on the roll. You can use this a number of times equal to your CE modifier per long rest."}, {"name": "True Warstaff: Full Spread", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Precognition", "text": "The pen becomes a standing panel — a fifteen-foot page in the world, marking all who stand inside it. You have learned to unfold your Warstaff into a full manga spread. As an action for 4 CE, you can drive the Warstaff into the ground at a point within 30 ft, projecting a standing panel that fills a 15 ft cube for 1 minute. Creatures inside the panel count as marked by your technique, and you can read their futures without spending the usual cursed energy."}, {"name": "Maximum: Omniscient Reader’s Viewpoint", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Storyboard Dominion", "text": "The feat-form of the edit — the same recorded die, granted to those who have built the Dominion. You have gained the ability to not only see, but also manipulate the contents of your manga panel. At the beginning of your turn, you can choose a creature that you can see that is marked by 6 seconds and roll a d20. Record the roll. As a reaction, you can replace one roll that creature makes with the result of that roll. At the beginning of your turn, you lose any unused rolls."}, {"name": "GG True Warstaff", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Precognition", "text": "The weapon's true form: longer reach, a heavier die, and two seconds of future for every critical. You have created a more powerful version of your G Warstaff, being a true weapon of destruction. As a bonus action while you have G Warstaff active, you can spend 4 cursed energy to evolve it into its true form, GG True Warstaff. It gains the following benefits for 1 minute: ●​ It deals one additional damage dice ●​ Its reach is 15ft instead of 10ft ●​ When you score a critical hit against a creature, you gain 2 seconds instead of 1 ●​ It gains a +1 to critical range"}], "e270": [{"name": "Quick Pose", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Majestic Pose", "text": "The pose as reflex: five energy to stop time on an enemy's trigger, move, and Dodge — then pay the lethargy. You have learned to strike a pose in a fraction of a second. As a reaction for 5 CE when you are targeted by an attack or forced to make a Dexterity saving throw, you can stop time for yourself and immediately move up to your speed and take the Dodge action; time then resumes. After time resumes, your movement is 0 ft and you cannot take actions until the end of your next turn."}, {"name": "Prime Time", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Golden Week", "text": "The feat-form of the sharpened stop — and the mercy of carrying one willing soul through the pause with you. You have learned to share your stopped time. While time is stopped by your technique, you can spend 2 CE to carry one willing creature you touch up to your movement speed, placing them in an unoccupied space you can see. They have no memory of the movement."}, {"name": "Maximum: Clock Hand", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Samsara Rewind", "text": "The feat-form of the clock-hand blade, granted to those who have learned the Rewind. As a bonus action, you can spend 5 CE to summon the Clock Hand to your hands for 10 minutes. The Clock Hand counts as a Simple Melee weapon that you are proficient with and has the finesse and reach property. It deals 1d10 piercing damage on a hit and has the Hour Hand and Minute Hand properties. Hour Hand: if used against a creature in stopped time, the Clock Hand deals an additional 3d8 necrotic damage on a hit. Minute Hand: if used against a creature not in stopped time, on a hit the creature must make a Cursed Energy save or be frozen in time and suffer the penalties of stopped time until the end of their next turn."}], "e271": [{"name": "Scorpion Tactics", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Scorpion Hair", "text": "The barb's three maneuvers: a riposte against the attacker, a grapple in place of damage, a barb left to work deeper. You have trained with your hair and unlocked the following maneuvers. Barbed Defense: as a reaction to being targeted by an attack, you can make a Scorpion Hair attack against the attacker if they are within range. Hair Wrapping: on a hit with your Scorpion Hair, you can choose to deal no damage and instead grapple the creature; you can use your Cursed Energy modifier to make grapple checks with your hair. Embedded Barb: once per turn when you hit with your Scorpion Hair, you can spend 1 CE to leave a barb embedded in the wound — at the start of the creature's next turn it takes 1d6 piercing damage as the barb works deeper, then dissolves."}, {"name": "Mega-Drill", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Drill Hair", "text": "One drill, made enormous: an eighty-foot line of piercing ruin that ignores cover and deals its maximum to structures. You can now use more cursed energy to imbue one Mega-drill. As an action for 4 cursed energy, you can shoot this Mega-drill in a 5 ft wide, 80 ft long line. Creatures in this line must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failure, it deals 6d10 piercing damage. On a success, they take half the damage. This technique deals maximum damage to objects and structures and ignores half and three quarters cover. The damage of this technique increases to 8d10 at 6th level and becomes 10d10 at 11th level."}, {"name": "Air Bomber", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Aircraft Hair", "text": "The aircraft's destructive rites: the helicopter's frenzy, and the jet's crash angled into a cone of shockwave. You have learned the following destructive ways to amplify your Aircraft Hair forms. Copter Frenzy: as an action for 5 CE, you force all creatures within 15 ft to make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save they take your Helicopter Hair damage. On a successful save, they take half as much. Jet Crash: when you crash your Jet Hair into a creature or surface, you can spend 2 CE to angle the impact — creatures in a 15 ft cone behind the point of impact must make a Dexterity saving throw, taking half the crash damage on a failed save as the shockwave carries through, or no damage on a success."}], "e272": [{"name": "Extreme Inverse", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Extreme Opposites", "text": "Full mastery of the extremes: the level itself becomes the margin — subtracted above, added below. You have fully mastered your Inverse technique, allowing you to withstand devastating attacks while weak strikes take a heavy toll. When you take damage, the effect depends on whether it exceeds or falls below your threshold. If the damage exceeds your threshold, you reduce it by an amount equal to your level. However, if the damage is below your threshold, you increase the damage taken by an amount equal to your level. This makes you near-invulnerable to powerful blows, but even the lightest strike can prove perilous."}, {"name": "Inverted Field", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Quick Inversion", "text": "The feat-form of the lent law — six energy to make thirty feet of the world judge harm as he does. While training on your technique, you have found out you have a lot more to offer than just being an indestructible powerhouse. You have learned how to alter a whole area to be affected by your technique. As a bonus action for 6 cursed energy, you cause all objects and creatures within 30 ft of you to be affected by your Inverse technique for 1 minute. A creature or object is no longer affected by Inverse if they leave the range of the field. You can deactivate this as a bonus action."}, {"name": "Maximum: Antithesis", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Synesthesia", "text": "The feat-form of the outward inversion, granted to those who have opened Synesthesia. You’ve learned to channel your inverted energy outward, inverting the flow of harm itself while your Inverse is active: when you take damage within your threshold, you can spend 4 CE as a reaction to reflect half of that damage back to the attacker (damage becomes force or necrotic, your choice) if they are within 30 ft. When you take damage below your threshold, you can instead spend 1 CE as a free action to transfer the pain. Choose a creature within 30 ft to take force or necrotic damage (your choice) equal to twice your CE modifier."}], "e273": [{"name": "Combat IQ", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Demonic Intellect", "text": "The overclock's combat suite — initiative, saves, a spare reaction, and the modifier lent to damage. Your overclocked mind runs firing solutions for the whole field. While your Demonic Intellect overclock is active, you can spend 1 CE as a bonus action to feed an ally you can see within 30 ft a predicted opening — they gain advantage on their next attack roll before the end of your next turn."}, {"name": "Read the Board", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Future and Past", "text": "The calculations model other minds: two energy to learn what the enemy intends, and whom it intends it for. Your calculations now model other minds. As an action for 2 CE, you can choose one creature you can see and predict its immediate intent — the DM tells you what the creature plans to do on its next turn, including its intended target and general action. A creature with an Intelligence of 3 or lower reveals only its target."}, {"name": "Calculate Scenario", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Overload", "text": "The feat-form of the questioned future — one minute, one question, one truthful reply. You focus your mind for 1 minute and spend 3 cursed energy. You ask a single question concerning a specific goal, event, or activity to occur within 7 days. The DM offers a truthful reply. The answer doesn’t take into account any possible circumstances that might change the outcome, such as additional glimpses of the future or the loss or gain of a companion."}, {"name": "Hyper-Intellect", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Future and Past", "text": "The feat-form of the acclimated brain — three points of Intelligence now, one more at each milestone. Your brain has begun to acclimate to the constant amount of information being calculated. Your Intelligence score increases by 3 and you gain proficiency in either History, Investigation, Arcana, Religion, or Nature. Your Intelligence score increases by 1 again at 6th, 11th, and 18th level. Your maximum score for Intelligence is now 24."}], "e274": [{"name": "Beginner’s Luck", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Little Miracles", "text": "Luck pressed into another's hand: a stored Miracle given to a willing creature, to spend as their own. Your luck is generous to those you favor. As a bonus action for 1 CE, you can press one of your stored Miracles into the hand of a willing creature you touch — they hold it as one of their own and can spend it using your CE modifier where the technique calls for one. You cannot exceed your normal maximum Miracles this way."}, {"name": "Blessing of Fortune", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Miraculous Outcome", "text": "The feat-form of the death-save mercy — a failed save remade as a natural twenty. When you or a creature you can see fails a death saving throw, you can spend 1 Miracle and 1 CE as a reaction. The roll is now considered a natural 20. You cannot experience a breakthrough or gain a Miracle in this way."}, {"name": "Innate Luck", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Fated for Fortune", "text": "The feat-form of the shadowed fortune — a critical success that tips an enemy's next roll toward ruin. Your fortune casts a shadow. When you score a critical success through Fated for Fortune, you can spend 1 CE to unbalance someone else's luck — one enemy you can see within 30 ft has disadvantage on its next d20 roll made within 1 minute, as your stolen fortune tips the scales against them."}], "e275": [{"name": "Exploding Fighting Spirit", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Missile Impact", "text": "The passion made shockwave: every landed fist spills thunder to all within five feet, proficiency times per turn. You have learned to channel your passion for battle and fighting spirit into your cursed technique. When you hit a creature with Missile Fist, the impact releases a shockwave — all other creatures within 5 ft of the target take thunder damage equal to your CE modifier. You can release this shockwave a number of times each turn equal to your proficiency bonus."}, {"name": "Armored Missile Fist", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Devastating Barrage", "text": "The fists worn as gauntlets: two energy for a minute of armored hands — AC, CE-driven unarmed strikes, ten-foot reach. As a bonus action for 2 CE, you cover your hands in Missile Fists, gaining the following benefits for 1 minute: ● You gain a +2 bonus to AC while holding no weapons or shields. ● You can use your CE modifier for attack and damage rolls using your unarmed strikes. ● Your unarmed strikes deal your Missile Fist damage. ● The range of your unarmed strikes becomes 10 ft."}, {"name": "Titan's Grasp", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Unrelenting Fury", "text": "The fist as shield: a reaction and three energy to interpose a fist between harm and its target, friend or self. As a reaction for 3 CE, when you or a creature within 30 ft would take damage, you interpose a Missile Fist, reducing the damage by your Missile Fist damage. Roll the user's current Missile Fist damage dice (Xd8 + CE modifier at the user's level) and reduce the incoming damage by the result."}], "e276": [{"name": "Immortal Jellyfish", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Lunar Jellyfish", "text": "True to the name: destroyed, the jellyfish reverts to a polyp — one hit point, regrowing each turn toward half its strength. True to its name, your jellyfish refuses to die. When Moon Dregs is destroyed, you can spend 5 CE as a reaction to revert it to its polyp stage instead — it shrinks to Tiny size with 1 hit point. At the start of each of your turns, the polyp regains hit points equal to your CE modifier until it reaches half of Moon Dregs' hit point maximum, at which point it returns to full size."}, {"name": "Adorable Poison Jar", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Poisonous Cursed Energy", "text": "The venom milked and bottled: two energy for a vial, weapon-applied or thrown, with the same poison in either hand. You have learned to milk Moon Dregs' venom into a jar. As an action for 2 CE, you can harvest a vial of jellyfish venom. You can apply it to a weapon as an action — the next hit forces a Constitution saving throw against your CE save DC, poisoning the target for 1 minute and dealing 2d6 poison damage on a failed save — or throw the vial as an improvised weapon (range 20/60 ft), shattering it in a 5 ft radius with the same effect."}, {"name": "Maximum: Crippling Neurotoxin", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Cleansing of Purity", "text": "The feat-form of the crippling doctrine, granted to those who have learned the Cleansing. You have finally learned to amplify your poisonous cursed energy into a crippling neurotoxin that locks down nerves. When you use Poisonous Cursed Energy, you can spend 8 additional cursed energy to enhance the poison. If a creature fails their save against Noxious Poison they are stunned until the end of their next turn and poisoned for 8 hours. On a successful save, the target is poisoned for 1 minute. A creature poisoned in this way is treated as being under 3 temporary levels of exhaustion. If a creature fails the save by 5 or more, they are paralyzed until the end of their next turn and poisoned for 24 hours. This poison ignores cursed techniques that grant resistance, immunity, or other reductions to poison damage and the poisoned condition. This poison cannot be removed by cursed techniques or reverse cursed technique."}], "e277": [{"name": "Dull Pain", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Pain Killer", "text": "The pain dulled before it lands: an hour of nerves numbed against fear and the breaking of concentration. You can dull pain before it ever lands. As a bonus action for 1 CE, you can touch a creature and numb its nerves for 1 hour — it gains advantage on saving throws against being frightened and on Constitution saving throws made to maintain concentration, as pain can no longer distract it."}, {"name": "Field Poultice", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Practiced Hands", "text": "The medicine packed to go: two energy for a poultice that holds the technique a full day, pressed on by any hand. You have learned to pack your medicine to go. As an action for 2 CE, you can prepare a poultice of cursed energy that holds your technique. A creature can use an action to press the poultice onto itself or another creature within 5 ft, gaining the effects of Pain Killer for 1 hour. The poultice loses its potency after 24 hours."}, {"name": "Maximum: Panacea", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Analgesic", "text": "The feat-form of the miracle, granted to those who have learned the Analgesic. As a reaction to a creature within 10 feet (including yourself) falling to 0 hit points you can spend 4 CE and cause them to instead remain at 10 hit points and gain the benefits of Pain Killer."}], "e278": [{"name": "Immobilized Limbs", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Immobilizing Eyes", "text": "The gaze given anatomy: legs to halve and topple, arms to disarm, torso to strip of armor — one energy for the focus. When you use Immobilizing Eyes, you can spend 1 additional CE as part of activating the technique concentrate your eyes on a specific part of the creature, also causing one of the following restrictions while you maintain your technique: ● Legs. The target's speed is halved. If the target tries to move more than their movement speed, they must make a Dexterity saving throw or fall prone. ● Arms. The target gains an additional -3 penalty to attack rolls and cannot take object interactions. ● Torso. You reduce the target's AC by 3."}, {"name": "Measured Gaze", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Peripheral Vision", "text": "The gaze learned soft: speed halved and nothing more, no strain on the eyes, and one soul releasable without freeing the rest. You have learned to measure your gaze. When you use Immobilizing Eyes, you can soften it: the target's speed is halved but its attack rolls and AC are unaffected, and your eyes take no strain damage from that target resisting. You can also end the technique on one creature you are maintaining it against without ending it on the others."}, {"name": "Eye Drops", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Reactive Eye Movement", "text": "The eyes taught to rest: a bonus action, an energy, closed lids — and the bleeding staunched at the price of a turn's blindness. Through constant exposure, your eyes have learned to rest between strains. As a bonus action for 1 CE, you can close your eyes and let them recover — your eyes regain hit points equal to your CE modifier, but you are blinded until the start of your next turn."}], "e279": [{"name": "Regalia Versatility", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Regalia", "text": "The soul reshaped at will: a bonus action to change the weapon's form — blade, bow, or shield, as the hour demands. You have learned to alter your regalia and can change it to a different type of weapon as a bonus action, including ranged weapons and shields. While your Regalia is a ranged weapon, it creates its own ammunition. While it is a shield, you gain a bonus to AC while wielding equal to the bonus to attack and damage rolls your regalia has. Your GM may also choose to allow more unique weapons."}, {"name": "Celestial Raiment", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Cursed Wave", "text": "The scarf of the heavens: three energy for a silken ward, lending proficiency to armor or to the saving throw. While you have your Regalia manifested, you can spend 3 CE as a bonus action to summon a hagoromo scarf around your body that lasts until your Regalia disappears. As a reaction, you can add your proficiency bonus to your AC until the beginning of your next turn, or to a saving throw you make as the silken scarf protects you from harm."}, {"name": "Technique Release", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Soul Bound Treasure", "text": "The maximum output: two energy for the critical strike and the prone — and the regalia breaks in the spending. You have learned a method that allows you to use your maximum output. On a hit, you can spend 2 CE to deal critical damage — the attack is a critical hit: roll all of the attack's damage dice twice and add them together, then add modifiers as normal — and the target must make a Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. After the attack, your regalia breaks and must be resummoned. You can also use this on a Cursed Wave attack for 4 CE."}], "e280": [{"name": "Retrograde Station", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Reversion", "text": "The refusal extends to objects: touch what was destroyed and spend two coins, and the thing un-breaks — fragments vanish, the whole reforms, the timeline of the object stretching back hours, then days, then years. As an action while touching part of a nonliving object that was destroyed an hour ago, you can spend 2 cursed energy to entirely repair it. Any other fragments or separated parts of it disappear and any destroyed parts reform for the object. At 6th level this increases to 1 day, at 8th level this increases to 7 days, at 11th level this increases to 1 month, at 18th level this becomes 1 year and at 20th level this increases to any point in time. Retrograde Station fails on anything that was ever a creature or that currently bears a curse."}, {"name": "Flash Regress", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Regression", "text": "The regress learns company — for one more coin a willing creature can be carried along the reversed path. What if we just went backwards, like really fast? When you use Regression, you can bring one willing creature you can touch along with you for an additional 1 cursed energy. The creature traces your reversed path with you and ends in an unoccupied space adjacent to your arrival point. If your path is blocked, the normal Blocked Path rules apply to both of you."}, {"name": "Maximum: Sword of Retrograde", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Invert Causality", "text": "The Maximum sharpens the overrule into a blade along the target’s reversed timeline — a Constitution save or be stunned and unmoved, a success or no reactions at all. When you use Invert Causality, your guaranteed attack strikes along the target's reversed timeline. The target must make a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, it is stunned until the end of your next turn and the movement from its most recent turn is undone, returning it to the position it occupied at the start of that turn (damage and other effects it caused remain). On a successful save, it cannot take reactions until the end of its next turn. You cannot roll a black flash on this attack."}], "e281": [{"name": "Musical Climax", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Resonating Music", "text": "The sorcerer learns what every performer knows — the drop matters more than the beat. Charge the technique over rounds of concentration, then throw the sound from anywhere within sixty feet, shaping the wave into a line. You've learned that just playing isn't enough, you need to build up to the best part. As an action you can start playing your instrument to charge your technique, concentrating for up to a number of rounds equal to your CE modifier, after which you must release it. When you release a Sound Blast or Sound Wave charged this way, you can originate it from any unoccupied point within 60 feet of you that you can see, throwing your sound, and you can shape a Sound Wave into a 60-foot line instead of a cone."}, {"name": "Emotional Melodies", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Resonating Music", "text": "Five coins buy a minute of vibe, and the vibe is a weapon: happy charms, sad pins them prone and still, angry turns them berserk against their own side. As a bonus action for 5 cursed energy, you can introduce a vibe of your choice for 1 minute while concentrating. You can only have one Vibe active at a time. Deafened creatures automatically succeed. Happy Vibes: on a hit with your Sound Blast, the target makes a Charisma saving throw or be Charmed and only hear you and your music until the Vibe ends; they can repeat the save at the beginning of their turn. Sad Vibes: on a hit with your Sound Blast, the target makes a Charisma saving throw or fall prone and their speed becomes 0 until the Vibe ends; they can repeat the save at the beginning of their turn. Angry Vibes: on a hit with your Sound Blast, the target makes a Charisma saving throw or becomes berserk until the Vibe ends — a berserk creature uses their reaction to make a melee attack at the closest creature at the start of their turn and must use their action to attack; they can repeat the save at the beginning of their turn."}, {"name": "Rock Squad", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Maximum: Epic Solo", "text": "The band gets back together mid-solo — allies ending their turns near the soloist carry the rhythm into their next strike, pushing what they hit. Looks like the band is getting back together! While your Epic Solo is active, you can conduct your allies' strikes. When an allied creature ends their turn within 15 feet of you during your Epic Solo, their next attack before the start of your next turn carries your rhythm: on a hit, the target is pushed 10 feet away from the ally, as if struck by your Sound Blast."}], "e282": [{"name": "Piercing Burst", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Piercing Schrift", "text": "The perfected shot stops asking about lines of fire — one attack roll now threatens everything standing in front of or behind the target along its path. You have perfected your accuracy and combined it with your piercing ability. When you use Piercing Schrift, you can also target additional targets up to your proficiency bonus that are either in front of or behind your target as long as they are within the path of the attack. You use the attack roll against the original target to determine if you would hit the additional targets."}, {"name": "Cursed Seal Expert", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Cursed Mark", "text": "Diligent practice breeds new signatures: marks that blind or cripple on a failed Constitution save, the affliction lingering a minute with a save each turn. Through diligent practice and creativity, you have created new types of cursed seals. You gain the following options: Blinding Mark: As a bonus action for 3 CE, you mark a creature within 30 feet for 1 minute. On a hit, the creature must make a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, they are blinded for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the save at the end of their turn, removing the blinded condition on a success. Crippling Mark: As a bonus action for 3 CE, you mark a creature within 30 feet for 1 minute. On a hit, the target must make a Constitution saving throw or have either their movement speed halved for 1 minute or disadvantage on attacks for 1 minute (your choice). A creature can repeat the save at the end of their turn, ending the effect on a success."}], "e283": [{"name": "Shadow User", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Shadow Strike", "text": "The shadow becomes a vehicle and a courier — enter it for full cover and short hops between shadows, or leave an attack or a five-word message in someone else’s shadow to trigger within a day. You have furthered the uses of your shadow choosing one of the following features (This feat can be taken multiple times). Shadow Skulker: As an action for 2 CE you physically enter the shadows gaining full cover for X rounds or until you exit from a shadow within 10 feet. As an action while the technique is active, you can move into a shadow within 10 ft. You can hear and see through the shadow you entered. If the shadow is sufficiently illuminated, you exit the shadow. (X = CE mod). Shadow Envoy: As an action for 2 cursed energy, you can imbue your cursed energy into a creature's shadow within 5 ft. To attempt this technique without them noticing, you must make a Cursed Energy check against their passive perception. You can imbue conditions for when the technique is triggered. You can choose to leave either a melee attack with a range of 10 ft using Shadow Strike or a simple message. If you choose to leave a Shadow Strike, it targets a specific creature under a condition you set, uses your Cursed Energy modifier and is made at advantage if the target is unaware. If you choose a message, you can choose to leave five words. When you create the message, you can choose any number of creatures who can see the message in the shadow. The imbued trigger lasts 24 hours or until triggered, whichever comes first. You learn any two Sorcerer spells below 5th level of your choice; both must have a shadow/darkness theme approved by the GM. The CE cost equals the spell's level."}, {"name": "Lingering Bindings", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Dark Binding", "text": "The binding outgrows its hostage weapon — two more coins pin the shadow with cursed energy alone, the grapple lasting a minute under concentration. Your binding no longer needs to hold your weapon hostage. When you use Dark Binding, you can spend an additional 2 cursed energy: the target's shadow is pinned by your cursed energy alone, and you keep your weapon. The binding lasts for 1 minute while you concentrate (the target remains grappled and restrained), and the target can use its action to make a Strength check against your CE save DC to tear free. You can maintain only one such binding at a time."}], "e284": [{"name": "Constellation Network", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Minor Star Shikigami", "text": "The shikigami become a nervous system — two coins attune them for an hour, and the user knows the location of everything within thirty feet of any star they can perceive. You have linked your shikigami into a shared-sense web. As an action for 2 cursed energy, you attune to your minor star shikigami for 1 hour: you know the location of every creature within 30 feet of any of your minor shikigami that the shikigami can perceive, and you can speak brief messages through them. This does not blind or deafen you as normal sense-sharing does."}, {"name": "Keystone Star", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Major Star Shikigami", "text": "The major learns to hold the center instead of the orbit — the domain maintains its own radius while the minors fight uncommanded, until the keystone falls. Your major star shikigami can serve as the keystone of your pseudo-domain. When you form your pseudo-domain, the major star shikigami can hold its center instead of orbiting: while it holds the center, you do not need to spend your bonus action to maintain the domain's radius, and you can command your minor shikigami normally. If the major star shikigami is killed or leaves the center, the domain ends."}, {"name": "Judicial Amputation", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Army of the Dictator", "text": "The mandate grows teeth: fail the orbit’s save by five or more and the Dictator chooses an arm or a leg — the limb goes, and with it two-handed actions or half the victim’s speed. If a creature fails their saving throw against your pseudo-domain by 5 or more, the damage is treated as having the Limb Removing Effect. You choose which of the target's arms or legs is affected: a removed arm prevents two-handed actions; a removed leg halves the creature's speed."}], "e285": [{"name": "Fox in the Mist", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Kitsune Creation", "text": "The pack learns to travel light — one coin folds a fox into a mote of fog the user carries, exempt from the active limit until released within thirty feet. You can fold a fox shikigami into a mote of your cursed fog and carry it with you. As an action for 1 cursed energy, you dismiss one of your fox shikigami into a mote you carry: it does not count against your active shikigami limit while carried. As a bonus action, you can release it into an unoccupied space within 30 feet of you."}, {"name": "Fox Fire", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Living Fog", "text": "Three more coins make the fog dense enough to detonate — one action, one vapor explosion, cold damage scaled to twice the modifier in d8s. You can create incredibly dense fog that can be triggered to erupt in a vapor explosion. For an additional 3 CE when you create an area of Cursed Fog, you make the fog incredibly thick. As an action, you can cause the fog to detonate in a vapor explosion. All creatures within the fog other than yourself must make a Constitution saving throw, taking twice your Cursed Energy modifier in d8s of cold damage or half as much damage on a success as a blue explosion rips through, igniting the fog."}], "e286": [{"name": "Tools of the Craft", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Guided Control", "text": "The imbuement extends past weapons — a coin lays cursed energy into artisan’s or thieves’ tools for the day, and the technique’s modifier replaces the ability on every check. You can imbue a set of tools with your cursed energy, such as artisan's tools or thieves' tools (1 CE, lasting until your next long rest). You can use your CE modifier in place of the normal ability modifier for ability checks made using the imbued tools. Additionally, you can channel a technique through them: when you use Wind Scythe, you can originate the line from an imbued tool you can see within 60 feet of you instead of one you hold or a Floating Tool."}, {"name": "Eyes in the Skies", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Floating Tool Improvement", "text": "The mounted tool becomes a watchtower — ride twenty feet up, spend the action, and learn the location of everything within one hundred and twenty feet that isn’t in total cover. Your Floating Tool is a perfect scouting perch. While you are riding a Floating Tool at least 20 feet above the ground, you can use your action to survey the area below: you learn the location of every creature within 120 feet of you that isn't behind total cover from your vantage. Allies who can see or hear you ignore disadvantage on Perception checks to notice those creatures until the start of your next turn."}], "e287": [{"name": "Cannibalism", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Hunger of the Accursed", "text": "The hunger’s last taboo falls by table consent — humanoid corpses become edible, and their class features and techniques can be taken in base form, though never a Domain. Your hunger has overwhelmed your humanity and led you to resort to this inhumane act. You can now devour the corpses of human races and use them for your innate technique features. You can take a Class Feature or Innate Technique feature using the rules of Hunger of the Accursed from a dead humanoid, changing parts of your appearance to resemble them when used. You cannot take Domain Expansions using this feature. When you steal a cursed technique or innate technique feature from a dead humanoid, you can only take it if you are of the correct level and fulfill any prerequisites for using it. Additionally, you can only spend the base cost the technique requires. No matter what you copy, you can only use the technique in its base form. For example, a maximum output hollow purple would only come as a hollow purple. This changes if used with the Output option of Digestion at 6th level. Table consent: devouring a sapient humanoid corpse requires the table's consent, and for a PC corpse, that player's out-of-character consent — without it the corpse is inedible."}, {"name": "Necrophage", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Regurgitation", "text": "The eater learns to read before committing — a small taste, no cost, reveals one stealable feature the GM chooses, and the corpse remains fully devourable after. You have learned to read a corpse before committing your hunger. As an action, you can take a small taste of a corpse within 5 feet of you: you learn one feature, action, or trait from its statblock that you could steal with Hunger of the Accursed (your GM chooses and reveals it). Tasting costs no cursed energy and does not consume the corpse, which can still be devoured normally afterward."}, {"name": "Gourmand", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Body of the Devourer", "text": "The connoisseur’s trick — once per short rest, a Regurgitation calls a second helping from the same creature on the same bonus action. You have learned to appreciate the good food you have eaten. When you use Regurgitation, you can call upon one additional ability you stole from the same creature as part of the same bonus action, paying its cursed energy cost separately as normal. You can savor a second helping in this way once per short rest."}], "e288": [{"name": "Crossed Marks", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Mastered Teleport", "text": "The marks become doors that open both ways — four coins transpose any two marked creatures or objects across any distance, the unwilling saving to resist. Your marks are doors, and doors open both ways. As an action for 4 cursed energy, you can transpose two creatures or objects that both bear your marks, instantly trading their positions no matter the distance between them. An unwilling creature can make a Cursed Energy saving throw to resist being moved."}, {"name": "Warded Marks", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Improved Marking", "text": "The marks learn to watch as well as carry — one more coin wards a mark, and the user is alerted when the uninvited come within ten feet. Your marks can watch as well as carry. When you place a mark, you can spend 1 additional cursed energy to ward it: you are mentally alerted when a creature you did not designate comes within 10 feet of the warded mark, and you learn the creature's size category. You can also set a warded mark to flare when triggered, shedding bright light in a 20-foot radius as a silent alarm."}], "e289": [{"name": "Many Hands", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have One Man Army", "text": "The clones learn to deliver as well as strike — touch-range cursed techniques may originate from any clone’s space within sixty feet. Your clones can deliver your techniques as well as your strikes. When you use a cursed technique with a range of touch, you can originate it from the space of one of your clones within 60 feet of you instead of your own space."}, {"name": "Shell Game", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Twice the Fun", "text": "The enemy can never be sure which body is you — a bonus action trades places with any clone within sixty feet. Your enemies can never be sure which body is you. As a bonus action, you can swap positions with one of your clones within 60 feet of you."}, {"name": "Shared Burden", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Four is a Party", "text": "The duplicates learn to suffer in your place — a bonus action transfers a condition to a clone within thirty feet, and the clone bears it instead. You have learned to trade more than bodies and hit points. As a bonus action, you can transfer one condition affecting you — blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, poisoned, or restrained — to one of your clones within 30 feet of you; the clone suffers the condition instead."}, {"name": "Long Leash", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have One Man Army", "text": "The duplication outgrows arm’s reach — clones may now be created within thirty feet instead of five. Your duplication is no longer confined to arm's reach. You can create clones within 30 feet of yourself instead of 5 feet."}, {"name": "Meant to be Expendable", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have One Man Army", "text": "Four coins and a reaction summon a clone mid-blow — it shoves you five feet aside and takes the damage in your place. As a reaction to damage, you can spend 4 CE to summon a Clone, which shoves you 5 feet and takes the damage in your place."}, {"name": "Maximum: Conga Line", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Four is a Party", "text": "The Maximum is the whole parliament moving as one — eight coins as a free action, and every body moves thirty feet and takes the attack action. You can spend 8 CE as a free action to tag team an enemy with your Clones, making a Conga Line on your way to stomp them. You and all clones can immediately move 30 feet and take the attack action."}], "e290": [{"name": "Shadow User", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Divine Dogs", "text": "The user learns the shadow’s older tricks — enter it for full cover and short hops, trip an attacker’s legs out from under them, or borrow two shadow-themed sorcerer spells. You have furthered your use of shadows. Choose one of the following features (this feat can be taken multiple times). Shadow Skulker: as an action for 2 CE you physically enter the shadows, gaining full cover for a turn or until you exit from a shadow within 10 feet. At the start of your turn, you can spend 1 CE to remain in the shadow. You can hear and see through the shadow and can summon tamed shikigami within the shadow. If the shadow is sufficiently illuminated, you exit the shadow. Shadow Ridge: as a reaction for 1 CE against a melee attack, you force a creature within 10 feet to make a Dexterity saving throw; on a failure the target rolls the attack at disadvantage as their legs fall into their shadow briefly and they fall prone. You can instead spend 3 CE to give the target disadvantage on the save. Alternatively, learn any two Sorcerer spells below 5th level of your choice; both must have a shadow/darkness theme approved by the GM. The CE cost equals the spell's level."}, {"name": "Chimerafication", "prereq": "Prerequisites: Must have Totality", "text": "The fusion learns monstrosity — sacrifice even a living shikigami, fuse up to half the proficiency bonus plus one, and raise a Chimera that can wear a humanoid form. You have learned how to better fuse the powers of your shadows even at the cost of creating a monstrosity. When creating a Totality, you can sacrifice a tamed shikigami even if it is not destroyed. You can use a number of shikigami up to half your proficiency bonus (rounded up) + 1 that are eligible for Totality to fuse into an eligible non-Totality shikigami, forming a Chimera. Chimeras can have humanoid forms, but cannot be used for Well's Unknown Abyss. You can also give an additional alteration to your altered shikigami created with Well's Unknown Abyss, counting as part of the technique."}, {"name": "Maximum: Embodiment", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Chimera Shadow Garden", "text": "The Maximum skips the summoning and wears the shadow — half a shikigami’s cost buys its movement, actions, features, and one ability score for an hour. As an action, you can spend half the cost (minimum 1) of one of your tamed shikigami (no Totality or Chimera). Rather than summoning, you instead gain their movement, actions, legendary actions, features and one ability score of your choice from the shikigami for 1 hour — for example, Divine Dog's movement, Max Elephant's Constitution, or Mahoraga's Adaptation. You can embody one shikigami at a time."}, {"name": "Shadow Kennel", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Shadow Manipulation", "text": "The shadow becomes a kennel — store a tamed shikigami as an action, dismissed but kept, and release it as a reaction when an ally is attacked. Your shadow can hold living shadows as well as objects. As an action, you can store one of your tamed shikigami in your shadow; while stored it counts as dismissed. As a reaction when a creature you can see within 30 feet of you is attacked, you can release the stored shikigami into an unoccupied space within 30 feet of you."}], "e291": [{"name": "Blood Iron", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 11", "text": "Once per long rest the technique reaches past metal entirely — polarize the iron in a living creature’s blood, and one effect ignores the metal requirement with the target saving at disadvantage. Once per long rest, you may Polarize the iron in a living creature's blood. One Attract, Repel, or Crush ignores the metal requirement entirely and works on any creature; the target has disadvantage on its saving throw against that effect."}, {"name": "Debris Throne", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Magnetic Flight", "text": "Flight becomes fortification — orbiting scrap grants +2 AC against ranged attacks, and a reaction flings a shard at anyone who misses. While you are flying, orbiting scrap grants you +2 AC against ranged attacks. Once per turn when a ranged attack misses you, you may use your reaction to fling a shard — make a ranged technique attack against the attacker, dealing 2d8 + your CE modifier piercing damage on a hit."}, {"name": "Polarity Reversal", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Attract or Repel", "text": "A saved pull is not a wasted one — reverse the field as part of the same effect and move the target ten feet the other way, no save. When a creature succeeds on its saving throw against your Attract or Repel, you may reverse the field as part of the same effect: it moves 10 feet in the opposite direction (no saving throw). You may do this once per turn."}, {"name": "Polar Cage", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Crush", "text": "The constriction learns permanence — one more coin shapes the crushed metal into a cage, and the restraint lasts a minute with a save each turn. When Crush restrains a target, you may spend 1 additional CE to shape its metal into a cage: the restraint lasts 1 minute instead of until the end of its next turn (the target repeats the Strength save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success)."}], "e292": [{"name": "Reed's Calculus", "prereq": "", "text": "The genius is the second power — analyze a creature as a bonus action, learn its resistances and immunities, and grant every ally’s first attack advantage. The genius is the second power. As a bonus action, analyze a creature you can see: you learn its damage resistances, vulnerabilities, and immunities (if any), and the first attack each of your allies makes against it before the start of your next turn has advantage. You may use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest."}, {"name": "Living Bridge", "prereq": "", "text": "The body becomes infrastructure — a twenty-foot bridge, raft, or ramp for two thousand pounds, or a trampoline that turns falling allies into bouncing ones. You may shape your body into a 20-ft bridge, raft, or ramp that supports up to 2,000 lb — allies cross gaps, pits, and water on your back. Alternatively, you may become a trampoline: allies who fall onto you take no falling damage and may bounce up to 20 ft as part of their movement without provoking opportunity attacks."}, {"name": "Snapback", "prereq": "", "text": "An escaped hold is not a lost one — a reaction snaps the limb back for 2d8 and an immediate fresh grapple attempt. When a creature escapes your grapple or restraint, you may use your reaction: the limb snaps back — the escapee takes 2d8 bludgeoning damage, and you may immediately make a grapple attempt against it as part of the same reaction."}, {"name": "Containment Wrap", "prereq": "", "text": "Two coins wrap the hazardous instead of the hostile — flames smothered, traps untriggered, swarms contained, all suppressed for a minute. As an action for 2 CE, envelop a Medium-or-smaller unattended object or a 10-ft cube of hazardous terrain (fire, caltrops, a swarm, a triggered trap): its effects are suppressed for 1 minute (Focus) while wrapped — flames smother, traps cannot trigger, swarms cannot leave."}, {"name": "Elastic Rebound", "prereq": "", "text": "The membrane learns to catch — a reaction and two coins reduce a ranged attack by proficiency plus modifier, and a fully caught projectile goes home. When a ranged attack targets you, you may use your reaction and spend 2 CE to stretch a catching membrane: reduce the attack's damage by your proficiency bonus + your CE modifier as the rubber gives. If this reduces the damage to 0, you catch the projectile — fling it back as part of the same reaction by making a ranged technique attack against a creature within 60 ft; on a hit it takes the caught attack's original damage."}], "e293": [{"name": "Fastball Special", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ripped-Up Arsenal", "text": "The classic, filed as written — hurl a willing smaller creature sixty feet, and let it land swinging with advantage and your Strength behind the blow. As an action, hurl one willing creature one size smaller than you up to 60 ft in a straight line. If it lands adjacent to a hostile creature, it may immediately make one melee attack against that creature with advantage, adding your Strength modifier to the damage roll. Otherwise it lands on its feet in an unoccupied space. The thrown creature must be willing, and you cannot throw anything you could not lift."}, {"name": "Dead Stick Landing", "prereq": "Prerequisite: none", "text": "The test pilot’s last trick — falls deal the user nothing, and the landing discharges 2d8 into everything within ten feet and leaves the ground difficult. The test pilot's last trick — and proof the stone was always the point: when you fall, you take no falling damage. Each creature within 10 ft of your landing point makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 2d8 bludgeoning damage and falling prone on a failure, or half as much damage and not falling prone on a success, as your dense CE discharges into the ground. The ground where you land becomes difficult terrain until cleared."}, {"name": "Yancy Street Rules", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Ripped-Up Arsenal", "text": "The street fights back — improvised-weapon hits knock targets prone, or once per turn jar an object from their grip. The street fights back. When you hit a creature with an improvised weapon, it must succeed on a Strength saving throw or fall prone; once per turn, you may instead force it to drop one object it is holding as the blow jars it loose."}, {"name": "Seismic Sense", "prereq": "Prerequisite: none", "text": "The sedimented body reads tremors — standing on stone or earth grants thirty feet of tremorsense, and the grounded cannot be surprised. Your sedimented body conducts tremors the way a medium conducts CE: while standing on stone or earth, you gain tremorsense out to 30 ft, and you cannot be surprised by creatures in contact with the same ground."}], "e480": [{"name": "Tides of Harmony", "prereq": "Harmony", "text": "Bring yourself into Harmony with the world. Gain advantage on one attack roll, ability check, or saving throw. After using this, finish a long rest before using it again, unless you spend 2 CE to use it again. At 6th level, as a reaction for 2 CE, roll 1d6 and apply it as a bonus or penalty (your choice) to a creature's roll — after the roll, before its effects occur."}, {"name": "Chaos Control", "prereq": "Chaos", "text": "You see the patterns in the Chaos. When you use Chaos, control a random element of the effect — where an area of effect appears, which creature is affected, or the place a creature teleports to. After using this, you cannot use it again until you finish a long rest, unless you spend 2 CE to use it again."}, {"name": "Tides of Chaos", "prereq": "Chaos Amplification", "text": "You gain a modicum of control over the chaos and harmony of this world. Whenever you roll on the Chaos Table, roll twice and use either number."}, {"name": "Harmony's Ear", "prereq": "Harmony", "text": "[INVENTED] You may cast Speak with Animals or Tongues through Harmony as a bonus action by spending 1 additional CE (3 CE total)."}, {"name": "Overcharge the Bolt", "prereq": "Chaos Amplification", "text": "[INVENTED] Once per long rest, when you cast Chaos Bolt, upcast it by one additional spell level beyond its automatic level without spending CE (still capped at 9th level)."}], "e481": [{"name": "Dazzling Glare", "prereq": "Must have Light Constructs", "text": "You can interpose light between yourself and an attacking enemy when you sense killing intent. As a reaction for 2 cursed energy when you are attacked by a creature within 30 feet of you that you can see, you impose disadvantage on the attack roll with a flare of light. An attacker that can't be blinded is immune to this feature. At 6th level, the target also takes 2d8 radiant damage or 4d8 at 11th level."}, {"name": "Irradiated Light", "prereq": "Must have Light Techniques", "text": "You have learned to weaponize the radiation of your light constructs. When a creature fails a save against one of your innate technique features, you can spend 1 cursed energy to cause that creature to gain the poisoned condition and take radiant damage at the beginning of their turn equal to your CE modifier. This lasts a number of rounds equal to your CE modifier. A creature can make a Constitution saving throw at the end of their turn, ending the effect on a success."}, {"name": "Defensive Constructs", "prereq": "Must have Hyperspeed", "text": "You have learned to create defensive constructs. When you use Light Constructs, you can instead create a Shield in a free hand or a flat 5 ft x 5 ft panel of light within 20 ft of you for 1 minute. The panel of light has an AC equal to your CE save DC, hit points equal to your level times your CE modifier, and immunity to radiant, poison, and psychic damage. You can choose to make it solid or not as a bonus action, allowing targets to move through it if non-solid."}, {"name": "Light Speed Versatility", "prereq": "Must have Maximum: Light Speed", "text": "You have trained your killing intent to better adapt to the process of gaining properties of light. If you fail your saving throw when using Light Speed, you only take 10 bludgeoning damage. Additionally, as a bonus action for 3 cursed energy, you can activate Light Speed as a bonus action, sacrificing speed and damage for quicker activation. When used in this way, the length you travel and the damage dice of the technique is halved. This cannot be used with Maximum Output."}, {"name": "████ and Dark", "prereq": "Must know reverse cursed energy", "text": "Through studying reverse cursed energy, you have learned your reversal, allowing you to instead create constructs of darkness from your killing intent. You learn the Darkness spell and cast it as an action for 2 CE. Dark Constructs: as a bonus action for 4 cursed energy, you mold killing intent into a bar of darkness in a free hand. This weapon lasts for 1 minute and counts as a simple melee weapon with which you are proficient. It deals 4d8 necrotic damage on a hit and has the finesse, light, and thrown properties (range 20/60). Additionally, you can use your Cursed Energy modifier for attack and damage rolls using this weapon. If you drop the weapon or throw it, it dissipates and reappears in your hand. On a hit with this weapon, a creature's speed is halved until the end of their next turn. This does not stack. Dark Vortex: as an action for 12 cursed energy, you create a dark vortex in your hands for up to 1 minute while you maintain concentration. All creatures within 60 ft must make a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, they take 6d10 necrotic damage and are pulled 10 ft closer. On a successful save, they take half as much damage and are not pulled. You maintain the vortex as an action on your turn, forcing all creatures within range to repeat the save. As a reaction to taking damage while maintaining the vortex, you can absorb the attack into the vortex, rolling your vortex damage and reducing the attack by that much. If this reduces the damage to 0, the attack or effect is nullified. If the damage is from a melee attack, the weapon is destroyed unless it is Grade 1 cursed tool or higher. If used at Maximum Output, a creature that is pulled within 5 ft or is within 5 ft and fails their save, they treat this damage as a Limb Removing Effect. The damage of this technique increases to 10d10 at 6th level, 14d10 at 11th level, and 18d10 at 18th level."}], "e482": [{"name": "Keystone Break", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Stone Cutting Strike", "text": "[INVENTED] When you reduce an object or structure to 0 hit points with an attack, the break keeps going: each creature within 10 feet of it makes a Dexterity saving throw against your technique save DC, taking bludgeoning damage equal to your proficiency bonus plus the strike's bonus damage on a failure, or half on a success."}, {"name": "Mason's Eye", "prereq": "Prerequisite: none", "text": "[INVENTED] You read worked stone the way others read faces: you have advantage on Investigation checks concerning structures and constructions, and by touching a structure you learn its current hit points."}, {"name": "Living Quarry", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 6", "text": "[INVENTED] Constructs, earth elementals, and petrified creatures count as structures for your Stone-Cut Body: your unarmed strikes and melee weapon attacks deal twice as much damage to them, and your cursed techniques deal maximum damage to them."}], "e483": [{"name": "Double Bloom", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Cursed Lotus", "text": "[INVENTED] You can maintain two lotuses at once (each costs its own 2 CE and bonus action to create). Only one lotus can detonate per round."}, {"name": "Petal Screen", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Cursed Lotus", "text": "[INVENTED] When your lotus explodes, you may have the petals swirl defensively instead of offensively: chosen creatures within 10 feet of you gain half cover until the start of your next turn, and no damage is dealt."}, {"name": "Seed Petal", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 6", "text": "[INVENTED] As an action for 2 CE, press a petal onto a willing creature. The next time that creature takes damage within 1 minute, a smaller lotus detonates around it: creatures of your choice within 10 feet of it make a Dexterity save against your technique save DC, taking 2d4 slashing damage on a failure or half on a success. You can have a number of seeds active equal to your proficiency bonus."}], "e484": [{"name": "Catch and Release", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Residual Catch", "text": "[INVENTED] When Residual Catch reduces the triggering damage to 0, you may immediately make one weapon attack or technique attack against the attacker as part of the same reaction; your proficiency bonus damage bonus from Residual Catch applies to this attack."}, {"name": "Still Water", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Residual Catch", "text": "[INVENTED] You can use Residual Catch against damage that is not from a cursed technique, innate technique, or cursed strike (weapon attacks, falls, and the like), but the reduction is only your proficiency bonus instead of twice it."}, {"name": "Ripples", "prereq": "Prerequisite: level 6", "text": "[INVENTED] When Residual Catch lets you add your proficiency bonus to a damage roll, you may instead split that bonus across any number of damage rolls you make before the end of your next turn."}], "e508": [{"name": "Pick Up Your Sword", "prereq": "Prerequisite: The Whistle", "text": "Death despises prey that won't face him. Frighten a creature into striking elsewhere, and he snarls it back into line — courage redirected to its proper target: him. When a creature frightened of you makes an attack against anyone other than you, you can use your reaction to snarl a challenge: it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your CE save DC or target you with the attack instead. Death despises prey that won't face him."}, {"name": "Red in the Dark", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Death's Mark", "text": "His eyes burn red in the dark, and they have never once blinked at a locked door or a shadowed corner. For the marked, concealment is a courtesy Death does not extend. Your eyes burn red in the dark. You gain darkvision out to 60 feet (or extend your existing darkvision by 30 feet), and your marked target gains no benefit from invisibility, darkness, or heavy obscurement against you."}, {"name": "Snuffed Light", "prereq": "Prerequisite: \"Why Did You Run?\"", "text": "Where Death arrives, the lamps go out — or he brings the dark with him, snuffing what little light the marked had left to navigate by. When you teleport with Why Did You Run?, you can spend 1 additional CE to bring the dark with you: nonmagical light within 20 feet of your destination is extinguished, and magical light there is suppressed for 1 minute."}, {"name": "The Parting Cleave", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Reaper's Sickles", "text": "The greatsickle splits mid-swing, the harvest widening by one soul. One stroke, two settlements. When you hit a creature with the greatsickle, you can split the weapon mid-swing: choose a second creature within 5 feet of the target, which takes 1d6 slashing damage as the separating blades bite."}, {"name": "Death's Mercy", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Wounds That Do Not Close", "text": "Death decides when the due is paid. Once per long rest he may stay an end that is not his to collect — stabilizing the fallen at a single hit point, because the ledger is his and no one else's. Once per long rest, when a creature within 30 feet of you drops to 0 hit points, you can use your reaction to stay its end: it stabilizes at 1 hit point instead. Death decides when the due is paid."}], "e509": [{"name": "Angle the Shard", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Face the Shards", "text": "The mirror points where she points it — a reflected attack may be redirected to another creature near the attacker. The thrower need not be the one who catches. When you reflect an effect, you may choose a different creature within 30 feet of the attacker as the new target instead of the attacker itself. The mirror points where you point it."}, {"name": "Show Them Themselves", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Face the Shards", "text": "Her mirror catches more than damage. Hostile conditions, forced movement, charms and frighten attempts — the glass returns those too. Nothing aimed at her stays aimed at her. Your mirror catches more than damage. Non-damaging hostile effects that target only you — conditions, forced movement, charm or frighten attempts from techniques — can be reflected back onto their source just like an attack."}, {"name": "Averted Gaze", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Look Away", "text": "Look Away, perfected: a swallowed area or line effect spares everyone inside it, and nothing rebounds anywhere. Mercy, aimed. Look Away can swallow an entire area or line effect, not just what targets you: everyone inside it is spared, and nothing rebounds anywhere."}, {"name": "Nursed Grudges", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Kept Wounds", "text": "Some hurts she saves for later. Opening the ledger need not empty it — half may be kept, rounded down, for the next reckoning. When you open your ledger of hurts, you may keep half of it (rounded down) instead of emptying it. Some hurts you save for later."}, {"name": "See Yourself", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Face the Shards", "text": "Hold the mirror steady as the blow returns: the attacker, unable to stop staring, is disadvantaged against anyone but her. She becomes the only thing in the room worth hitting. When you reflect an attack, you may hold the mirror steady as part of the same reaction: the attacker must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your CE save DC or have disadvantage on attacks against anyone other than you until the end of its next turn — it can't stop staring."}], "e510": [{"name": "The Snare Left Behind", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Chain Jail", "text": "A loop of Chain Jail laid as a trap — the first designated member to enter is bound without an attack roll. Justice, pre-positioned. As an action, lay a loop of Chain Jail on a surface as a trap. The first member of the designated group to enter its 5-foot space is bound as though struck, with no attack roll. The snare lasts until triggered or you finish a long rest, and you can maintain only one at a time."}, {"name": "The Pulse Remembers", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Dowsing Chain", "text": "Press the Dowsing Chain to a surface and read the emotional truth of the last day — heartbeats leave echoes, and the chain keeps minutes. As an action (invented), press the Dowsing Chain to a surface or object: you learn the emotional truth of what happened there within the last 24 hours — heartbeats leave echoes, and the chain reads whether the dominant feeling was fear, triumph, grief, or deceit."}, {"name": "Oathbound Ally", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Judgment Chain", "text": "The stake enforces loyalty as readily as sentence — willing creatures may swear themselves to silence under the same buried blade. Breaking the rule is still death; the ally must understand the price. You may set a Judgment rule upon a willing creature — the stake enforces loyalty exactly as it enforces a sentence, and many swear themselves to silence this way. Breaking the rule is still death, and the ally must understand the price before the stake goes in."}, {"name": "Borrowed Hours", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Emperor Time", "text": "While Emperor Time burns, failure is negotiable: burn six hours of life and succeed instead. The scarlet eyes do not accept no. While Emperor Time burns, when you fail a saving throw you may use your reaction to burn 6 hours of life and succeed instead. The scarlet eyes do not accept no."}, {"name": "The Thumb's Diagnosis", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Holy Chain", "text": "The thumb reads before it mends. Laid on a creature, it reveals hit points, conditions, and any curse, vow, or foreign technique riding inside. Lay the Holy Chain on a creature: you learn its current hit points, every condition afflicting it, and whether any curse, vow, or foreign technique rides inside it. The thumb reads before it mends."}], "e511": [{"name": "Cold Reading", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Bandit's Secret", "text": "Ask the rite's question and learn the size of what you haven't stolen — how many unseen features the technique holds. A thief likes to know the shelf he's robbing. When you ask the rite's question, you also learn whether the victim's technique holds features you have not yet seen — and how many. You will know the size of what you haven't stolen."}, {"name": "The Placed Ribbon", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Double Face: The Bookmark and the Catalogue", "text": "Set a trigger on the bookmarked page — \"when I fall,\" \"when the bell rings\" — and the ability invokes itself on your reaction when it occurs. The book, given standing orders. You may set a trigger on your bookmarked ability — a condition you name, such as \"when I fall\" or \"when the bell rings.\" When it occurs, the ability invokes itself once using your reaction, then the ribbon goes slack until you reset it as a bonus action."}, {"name": "Palimpsest", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Bandit's Secret", "text": "Erase a page voluntarily and the impression remains: one true secret of the former victim — their greatest fear, their hidden vow. The living owner's feature returns to them; the knowledge stays with you. As an action, erase one of your pages voluntarily. The impression remains: you learn one true secret of the former victim — their greatest fear, their hidden vow, the thing they never say aloud (GM's choice, always true). A living owner's feature returns to them."}, {"name": "Footnote", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Two Pages Open", "text": "Speak the original owner's name when you invoke their ability. They feel the tug within a mile and know their miracle was just used. Some thieves sign their work. When you invoke a stolen ability, you may speak its original owner's name aloud. They feel the tug instantly — and know, with cold certainty, that their ability was just used and roughly where, within 1 mile. Some thieves sign their work."}, {"name": "Witness by Proxy", "prereq": "Prerequisite: The Question Compels", "text": "Scrying, a familiar's eyes, a true recorded image — the book accepts secondhand sight for the rite's witnessing. But the palm-press must still be flesh to flesh. Witnessing through your own scrying sensor, a familiar's eyes, or a true recorded image counts as witnessing for the rite's first condition. The book accepts secondhand sight — but the palm-press must still be flesh to flesh."}, {"name": "Sun and Moon", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Bandit's Secret", "text": "Two pages inked before your story began — a sun seal and a moon seal, kept warm only by post-mortem Nen. Stamped where they touch, they detonate: 8d10 fire. The troupe's farewell gift. Two pages were inked before your story began — a sun seal and a moon seal, stolen long ago from two users now dead; only post-mortem Nen keeps their pages warm (canon). As an action, press your palm to a creature or object and stamp it with a sun mark or a moon mark (your choice); a mark lasts until it detonates or you dismiss it. When a sun mark and a moon mark touch, they detonate: every creature within 20 feet must make a Dexterity saving throw against your CE save DC, taking 8d10 fire damage on a failure or half as much on a success (invented conversion — canon gives no dice). You can maintain only one sun mark and one moon mark at a time. The troupe's farewell gift."}], "e512": [{"name": "Banked Light", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Pain Packer", "text": "Vent pain as pure light instead of heat — a blinding flash or a beacon visible for miles. No damage. A signal. As an action (invented), vent at least 10 Pain as pure light instead of heat (the bank drains by the vented amount; invented): creatures within 30 feet make a Constitution saving throw against your CE save DC or are blinded until the end of your next turn — or raise a beacon of dawn-light visible for miles. No damage. A signal."}, {"name": "Cauterize", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Pain Packer", "text": "The same heat that kills, seals. Vent ten pain into a dying creature: it stabilizes at one hit point. Press banked heat into a wound: as an action, vent 10 Pain and touch a dying creature — it stabilizes and regains 1 hit point. The same heat that kills, seals."}, {"name": "Pain Ledger", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Heat Sense", "text": "Reading radiated pain tells how it was dealt — blade, flame, fall, teeth. Interrogation without questions. Reading radiated pain tells you how it was dealt: you learn the damage types a creature has suffered since its last rest, and roughly what dealt them — blade, flame, fall, teeth. Interrogation without questions."}, {"name": "Heat Haze", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Backdraft", "text": "With twenty or more pain banked, shimmering air bends light — he appears five feet from where he stands, and attacks suffer disadvantage. The stove, viewed through summer. While your bank holds 20 or more Pain, shimmering air bends light around you — you appear 5 feet from where you stand, and attacks against you have disadvantage until the bank drops below 20."}, {"name": "Solar Forge", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Rising Sun", "text": "While the Maximum's sun lingers, focus it on a single object — destroy, melt through, or superheat a weapon for an extra 2d6 fire on its next hit. One weapon at a time. As an action (invented) while the Maximum's sun lingers, focus the sun on a single object: destroy a nonmagical object up to a 10-foot cube, melt through restraints or a locked door, or superheat a weapon — its next hit within 1 minute deals an extra 2d6 fire damage. Only one weapon may be superheated at a time (invented)."}], "e513": [{"name": "Doormat", "prereq": "Prerequisite: The Mansion Door", "text": "A door hung flat on a floor, as a trap. The next uninvited step falls into the mansion's cell — welcome mat, hung by a jailer. Hang a door flat on a floor as a trap: the next creature to step on it — other than those you designated — falls into the mansion's cell. Spotting the trap takes a Perception or Investigation check against your CE save DC. It lasts until triggered or you finish a long rest."}, {"name": "Mail Slot", "prereq": "Prerequisite: The Mansion Door", "text": "A letter-sized portal paired to any door — scroll cases and whispered messages, silently, in either direction. A dead drop with no address and no courier. Cut a letter-sized portal paired to any of your doors. It passes objects no larger than a scroll case and whispered messages, silently, in either direction — a dead drop with no address and no courier. Passing an object or message through the mail slot costs an action (invented)."}, {"name": "The Vault", "prereq": "Prerequisite: More Rooms", "text": "One room, time-locked: perishables don't decay, volatiles can't detonate, nothing inside can be scried. What goes into the Vault waits, perfectly. Designate one room as a time-locked vault: perishables placed inside do not decay, volatile items cannot detonate, and nothing stored there can be scried or located by divination. What goes into the Vault waits, perfectly, until you come back for it."}, {"name": "Spare Key", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Paired Doors", "text": "Name a key-bearer: free passage through the doors, and once per long rest the right to hang a door itself — the CE drawn from your pool, with your standing permission. Name one creature your key-bearer. It may open and pass through your doors freely, and once per long rest it may hang a new door itself — the CE cost is drawn from your pool, with your standing permission."}, {"name": "Catch, Don't Kill", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Scream", "text": "A Scream portal closed on an incoming attack — reaction, three CE, the arrow filed away mid-flight. The mansion eats weapons too. Close a Scream portal on an incoming ranged attack or damaging effect you can see: spend your reaction and 3 CE, and the attack is swallowed into the mansion instead of striking — you take no damage. The portal closes on the arrow mid-flight. The swallowed attack is filed away into the mansion's cracks and dissipates harmlessly; it cannot be released (invented)."}], "e514": [{"name": "Palmed Card", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Spin the Clown", "text": "Hand a drawn weapon to a willing ally — the iron restriction transfers with it. The clown doesn't mind who plays, as long as someone does. Hand a drawn weapon to a willing ally: the iron restriction transfers with it — they must satisfy its use-condition before it can be dismissed. They wield it using your CE ability modifier for attack and damage rolls. The clown doesn't mind who plays, as long as someone does."}, {"name": "Rigged Applause", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Second Spin", "text": "Flourish the weapon as a bonus action; a watching creature that fails its Wisdom save is taunted into striking only you. Showing off doesn't count as using it. Flourish a drawn weapon as a bonus action: one creature that can see you must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your CE save DC or be taunted — it has disadvantage on attack rolls against anyone but you until the end of its next turn. Showing off doesn't count as using the weapon."}, {"name": "Prop Master", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Double Feature", "text": "Leave a used weapon as an innocent-looking object — the next creature to touch it triggers one stored attack. One prop at a time, one surprise per customer. Leave a used weapon behind as an innocent-looking object for 1 hour: the next creature to touch it triggers one stored attack from it (attack roll using your CE ability modifier against its AC, using the weapon's profile). You can maintain one prop at a time."}, {"name": "Curtain Call", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Encore", "text": "Within a minute of a dismissal, hurl the weapon's echo as a bonus action — one last attack within sixty feet. Every prop gets a final bow. Once per long rest, within 1 minute of a weapon being dismissed after use, hurl its echo as a bonus action: make one attack against a creature within 60 feet using the dismissed weapon's profile. Every prop gets a final bow."}, {"name": "The Clown Knows", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Spin the Clown", "text": "Spin during combat and the clown whispers one visible creature's damage vulnerabilities. It loves an audience, and it loves a slaughter — in that order. When you spin during combat, the clown whispers to you the damage vulnerabilities (if any) of one creature you can see. It loves an audience, and it loves a slaughter, in that order."}], "e515": [{"name": "Funny Faces", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Cursed Illusion", "text": "The goofy variant. Two extra CE makes the distorted face so absurd the Intelligence save is made at disadvantage — comedy as a weapon of war. When a cursed creature sees a distorted face, you may spend 2 CE to force its Intelligence saving throw to be made at disadvantage by making the face look extra goofy. You may also spend 1 CE to change the distortion, forcing the creature to make an additional Intelligence save on its next turn if it sees a distorted face."}, {"name": "Cursed Tracking", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Self Distortion", "text": "The mark, refined. Forgo the illusions and spend three more CE: a hidden 24-hour mark, precise location within three hundred feet plus proficiency — the curse as a leash. When a creature is cursed by your technique, you may spend an additional 3 CE to forgo the illusion effects and enhance the tracking instead. A mark appears somewhere on the target's body, out of sight and without its knowledge; it can become aware of the curse with an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your CE save DC, or if someone points it out. The mark lasts 24 hours, and while active you always know the target's precise location within 300 feet + 100 feet × your proficiency bonus. At the start of each day you may spend 5 CE to keep the mark active another 24 hours, provided the target is within range. If the target leaves your range, you cannot track it until it re-enters."}, {"name": "Maximum: Absolute Perspective", "prereq": "Prerequisite: Must have Illusive Terrain", "text": "The lie, total. All senses fooled for a full minute, the mind rationalizing every inconsistency — and once per turn, a harmful illusion that bites as psychic damage. For 10 CE, force a creature in range to make a CE save at disadvantage. On a failure, you completely fool all of its senses for 1 minute: you may freely create illusions around the target as if it were under your Cursed Illusion or Illusive Terrain, it automatically fails checks to determine the illusions are fake as its mind rationalizes inconsistencies, and once per turn when you create a harmful illusion the target takes psychic damage equal to your proficiency bonus in d6s."}]};